(76, 'Cadillac’s stars-and-stripes Miami debut as the new F1 team races on US soil', 'Cadillac driver Valtteri Bottas of Finland steers his car during the first practice session ahead of the Miami Formula One Grand Prix, Friday, May 1, 2026, in Miami Gardens, Fla. (AP Photo/Rebecca Blackwell) Cadillac driver Valtteri Bottas of Finland gets pushed back into his garage during the first practice session ahead of the Miami Formula One Grand Prix, Friday, May 1, 2026, in Miami Gardens, Fla. (AP Photo/Lynne Sladky) Cadillac driver Sergio Perez, of Mexico, speaks during a news conference at the Miami Formula One Grand Prix auto race, Thursday, April 30, 2026, in Miami Gardens, Fla. (AP Photo/Lynne Sladky) MIAMI GARDENS, Fla. (AP) — It was less than 14 months ago that Cadillac’s frustrating push to enter Formula 1 finally came to an end and the team was approved to compete in the global motorsports series. The team has completed three races already but its biggest debut comes this weekend, on American soil, at the Miami Grand Prix. Cadillac F1 markets itself as the only true American team in the European-dominated series — Haas F1 is owned by California businessman Gene Haas — and represents the American dream. The effort to enter F1 began with Michael Andretti, son of motorsports’ most famous naturalized U.S. citizen, and its 2026 car is named after Mario Andretti. And for its first race in North America, Cadillac debuted a special livery presented by the team’s primary partner, TWG AI. The design integrates a stars and stripes motif in Cadillac’s signature black and white color scheme, includes 50 stars on the front of the car and “USA” is emblazoned on the rear wing. There is also a splash of red inside the wheels to get red, white and blue on the car. “Racing at home for the first time is a major milestone for this team and something we’ve been looking forward to for a long time,” said Dan Towriss, CEO of the team and a part-time Fort Lauderdale resident. “There’s a lot of pride in representing the United States as the American team, especially in front of our home fans. We understand what that means and we’re focused on showing up and delivering for them.” Cadillac fields cars for Valtteri Bottas of Finland and Sergio Perez of Mexico, two veterans who have won in F1 for other teams. Through the first three races their best performance was Bottas finishing 13th and Perez 15th in the second round. Expected to be the worst performing team out of 11 based solely on this being its maiden year, Cadillac heads into Sunday’s race ranked 10th ahead of Aston Martin in the constructors’ standings. Colton Herta, who left the Andretti Global IndyCar team to race in F2 this season to earn the super license needed to compete in F1, is expected to eventually move into one of the Cadillac seats. The Californian was fastest in Friday’s practice for the junior series and the plan now would eventually make him the only American driver on the F1 grid. An unexpected five-week layoff because of the war in Iran forced F1 to cancel two events scheduled in the Middle East, and Cadillac used that time to put together “a fairly substantial upgrade package” for Miami. “It’s spread over different parts of the car so probably the main area is the floor, but there are also changes on front and rear brakes, front wing as well,” team principal Graeme ⁠Lowdon said. “It’s a mixture of aero and a bit of weight saving as well. It’s reasonably sizeable. We’ll be watching the performance of the upgrade with great interest because there’s an awful lot that we need to verify that other teams will be well down the route of doing.” Most of the teams came to Miami with upgrades, but because Cadillac is so new, it might not have had the bandwidth to make so many changes if not for the break. “I hope that we can make a bigger step than some other teams,” Bottas said. “Because we should be able to do that in theory from where we started. So that’s the goal. In the first three races I felt like every ⁠race was getting smoother and smoother, less and less issues.” Lowdon, however, acknowledged that Cadillac is still in its teething phase as it competes against long tenured teams. ”We’re racing against teams that have done literally thousands of grand prixs,” Lowdon said. “If there is a thing such as team muscle memory how you operate, other teams have that advantage. Everything for us is new.” Interest and popularity in Cadillac began even before one of its cars hit the track. Jim Campbell, vice president of performance and motorsports commercial operations, said General Motors CEO Mary Barra and President Mark Reuss will be in Miami all weekend, alongside dealers, customers and invited guests. “It’s our fourth race, but it’s our first time to race our Cadillac F1 on American soil, it’s super special,” Campbell said. “We’ve been looking forward to this day. We have been here the last three years, really trying to learn about the F1 platform and so to be here now racing is super exciting, as opposed to being here observing.”', 'https://apnews.com/article/f1-cadillac-miami-gp-498a7e6d7e449320e4d113ced34fca69', NULL, '2026-05-01 19:02:50', '2026-05-01 20:20:15', 'Football', 1, 3, 'en', 'https://dims.apnews.com/dims4/default/bde82df/2147483647/strip/true/crop/1087x1087+2+0/resize/60x60!/quality/90/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fassets.apnews.com%2Ff7%2Ff5%2F404c1d14410f9fbaca4744769321%2Fimg-1163-jenna-fryer.jpeg', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 2),
(77, 'Foot,Ligue 1Mais qui va remporter le trophée UNFP ?', 'Les nommés aux trophées de l\'Union nationale des footballeurs professionnels (UNFP) 2025-2026 ont été dévoilés jeudi soir sur la chaîne YouTube et Twitch de la Ligue 1 dans l\'émission « le SAV ». La cérémonie, 34e édition, se tiendra le 11 mai au Palais Brogniart, dans le IIe arrondissement de Paris. Voici les différentes catégories : meilleur joueur, meilleur espoir, meilleur gardien et meilleur entraîneur. C\'est une habitude : à chaque fois qu\'une telle liste sort, il y a des heureux et des déçus. Et les supporters de chaque club ne manquent pas de souligner l\'absence d\'un joueur. La saison dernière, le trophée de meilleur joueur était revenu à Ousmane Dembélé, auteur de 21 buts et de 6 passes décisives en 28 matches. L\'attaquant parisien va-t-il récidiver ? La saison dernière, un seul non-Parisien faisait partie des nommés : Rayan Cherki, alors à l\'OL, entourait Achraf Hakimi, Vitinha, Désiré Doué et Dembélé. Avec 3 éléments sur 5 - Dembélé, Nuno Mendes et Vitinha -, le club de la capitale est encore majoritaire. Et ils auront face à eux Mason Greenwood, 15 buts et 6 passes décisives avec l\'OM cette saison, et Florian Thauvin, 10 buts et 5 passes décisives avec Lens. Pour être éligible aux trophées UNFP, il faut avoir disputé au moins 15 matches. Dembélé en est à 19 mais n\'a été titularisé qu\'à 9 reprises, soit 30 % des rencontres. Cela pourrait-il l\'empêcher de conserver son trophée ? Ses stats sont intéressantes - 10 buts, 5 passes décisives -, similaires à celles de Thauvin. Et parmi les joueurs ayant disputé 9 matches minimum (avec au moins 45 minutes de jeu hors temps additionnel), le Ballon d\'Or France Football 2025 apparaît, dans nos notes L\'Équipe, en 2e position avec 6,22 (derrière le Lyonnais Malick Fofana, 6,22 en 9 matches). Nuno Mendes est dans une situation semblable à celle du Français. Parfois blessé (cuisse, genou), parfois sorti du banc en fin de rencontre, le latéral gauche portugais compte 20 matches de Ligue 1 dont 13 titularisations. Parmi les joueurs comptant au moins 13 matches, Nuno Mendes est 13e aux notes L\'Équipe avec une moyenne de 5,69. Aux notes L\'Équipe, Vitinha, 27 matches dont 23 comme titulaire, est 24e avec une moyenne de 5,50 (sur 22 matches). Le milieu portugais a délivré 6 passes décisives cette saison. Parmi les Parisiens qui ont pu être oubliés, on peut citer Willian Pacho (63e aux notes L\'Équipe avec 5,14), Warren Zaïre-Emery (31e avec 5,41). La non-présence de Khvitcha Kvaratskhelia n\'est pas une surprise. S\'il brille en Ligue des champions, avec 10 buts en 14 matches, il brille moins en L1, avec 7 réalisations et 4 passes décisives. Greenwood, qui a disputé 29 matches dont 26 d\'entrée, est 11e au classement des notes L\'Équipe de la saison (il faut avoir joué au moins une période lors de 16 matches), avec une moyenne de 5,72 sur 25 rencontres. En raison de la saison difficile de l\'OM, 6e du Championnat, sur une dynamique moyenne, et de ses performances en dents de scie, il ne paraît pas favori pour ce vote par des personnalités du football français (joueurs, entraîneurs, présidents). Enfin, Thauvin est le seul Lensois des cinq nommés. L\'international français est-il le meilleur Artésien de la saison ? Aux notes L\'Équipe, il est 28e avec une moyenne de 5,44, loin de ses coéquipiers Mamadou Sangaré (6,12), en tête, Samson Baidoo (6,06) ou Malang Sarr (5,93). Meilleur passeur du Championnat avec 9 offrandes, Adrien Thomasson, 20e aux notes L\'Équipe (5,55), est lui aussi absent. Joaquin Panichelli, auteur d\'un début de saison (9 buts en 10 matches) et d\'un mois de février (3 buts) canon, pouvait y prétendre, mais l\'attaquant strasbourgeois s\'est rompu le ligament croisé antérieur du genou droit fin mars. L\'actuel meilleur buteur du Championnat Estéban Lepaul, 18 buts avec Angers puis Rennes, n\'a pas non plus été nommé. Pas plus qu\'un Lyonnais - par exemple Corentin Tolisso ou Pavel Sulc - ou un Lillois.', 'https://www.lequipe.fr/Football/Actualites/Une-cuvee-2026-plus-indecise-que-jamais-mais-qui-va-remporter-le-trophee-unfp-du-meilleur-joueur-de-la-saison-de-de-ligue-1/1672380', NULL, '2026-05-01 20:20:15', '2026-05-01 20:20:16', 'Football', 1, 3, 'fr', 'https://www.lequipe.fr/_medias/img-photo-jpg/ousmane-dembele-mason-greenwood-nuno-mendes-florian-thauvin-et-vitinha-l-equipe/1500000002454934/0:0,1482:988-640-427-75/5f9c7.jpg', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 10),
(78, '— Godon : «Pas une option de perdre»', '« Quelle est la différence entre votre victoire vendredi et votre 2e place jeudi ? J\'ai encore plus mal aux jambes qu\'hier (jeudi), je suis encore plus mort (sourire). Jeudi, il y avait une bosse vraiment dure à trois bornes de l\'arrivée, je n\'ai pas pris les bonnes décisions, il y avait vent de face, il (Pogacar, vainqueur) était simplement plus frais et plus fort que moi. Là, j\'ai pu gérer ma montée (dont le sommet était à 30 kilomètres de l\'arrivée), même si j\'étais à bloc, j\'ai pu bien récupérer ensuite. Tout le monde m\'a motivé, je n\'étais pas super loin, Bob (Jungels) a roulé pendant quatre bornes pas loin du peloton, AJ (August) s\'est relevé, Laurence (De Plus) aussi, ils m\'ont ramené dans la descente, après ils ont roulé direct pour aller chercher les trois échappées devant. Tout le monde s\'est mis à 300 % pour moi, je les entendais encore à l\'oreillette à la fin. Je ne pouvais pas me rater, ce n\'était pas une option de perdre aujourd\'hui. C\'est encore plus beau quand c\'est un succès collectif comme ça. Une rivalité est-elle en train de naître avec Tadej Pogacar ? Ce n\'est pas une rivalité. Ça me tire vers le haut. Je n\'étais pas très content jeudi, au final j\'aime bien gagner. Quand tu commences à gagner, t\'en veux toujours plus, c\'est bizarre la mentalité humaine. Je suis vraiment super content d\'avoir ramené cette victoire pour l\'équipe, mes équipiers. C\'était dur mais on l\'a fait, ça fait plaisir. Cela fait cinq victoires cette saison pour vous. (Il coupe.) Pour moi, c\'est six avec le chrono par équipes de Paris-Nice où j\'ai mis beaucoup d\'implication tout l\'hiver, à travailler tout seul sur un vélo de chrono, ce n\'est pas très marrant des fois. Cette victoire était belle aussi, la première de la saison. J\'ai adoré cet esprit : le vélo pas seulement sport individuel, se faire mal avec les autres, c\'est quelque chose que j\'aime et ils se sont vraiment fait mal pour moi aujourd\'hui. L\'équipe me donne toute sa confiance, plus que je peux l\'imaginer. Au final ça marche, tout le monde croit plus en moi que moi-même donc c\'est juste trop bien. « Je suis un coureur qui a besoin de la confiance des autres, c\'est peut-être aussi ce que je recherche » C\'est cette confiance qu\'il vous manquait par rapport à votre dernière équipe ? Ce n\'est pas la même mentalité. Aujourd\'hui, il n\'y avait vraiment pas de stress, si je ne passais pas la bosse, eh bien je ne la passais pas. Quand tu vois que toute l\'équipe roule pour toi, ça pousse, tu as envie d\'aller encore plus loin. Tout est différent, on ne peut pas comparer (avec Decathlon-CMA CGM, son ancienne équipe). Tout le monde me pousse vers le haut et j\'ai besoin de ça aussi, je suis un coureur qui a besoin de la confiance des autres, c\'est peut-être aussi ce que je recherche, donc je suis vraiment très, très heureux. Six victoires fin avril, on ne peut pas espérer mieux. En plus avec le maillot bleu, blanc, rouge. Aujourd\'hui, j\'avais vraiment la rage après l\'arrivée, c\'est une de mes plus belles victoires d\'un point de vue collectif. Voir les visages de mes équipiers en joie, ça me rend aussi heureux que de gagner, je fais du vélo pour ça. Vous parlez souvent de ce maillot de champion de France. Pour moi, c\'est le deuxième plus beau après celui de champion du monde. Je suis quand même fier d\'être français. Il est juste magnifique le kit (avec le vélo, le casque, les gants tricolores également), même si je ne me regarde pas pédaler. J\'ai envie de le garder à vie, je ne crois pas trop que ce sera possible, mais je profite. Vous participerez aux Championnats de France, en juin ? Bonne question. Ça se négocie. Dans ma tête j\'y vais. »', 'https://www.lequipe.fr/Cyclisme-sur-route/Actualites/Pour-dorian-godon-vainqueur-pour-la-deuxieme-fois-sur-le-tour-de-romandie-ce-n-etait-pas-une-option-de-perdre-face-a-tadej-pogacar/1672417', NULL, '2026-05-01 20:20:15', '2026-05-01 20:20:16', 'Cyclisme', NULL, 3, 'fr', 'https://www.lequipe.fr/_medias/img-photo-jpg/dorian-godon-s-est-impose-a-orbe-vendredi-massimo-fulgenzi-sprintcyclingagency-2026/1500000002454988/295:226,1874:1278-640-427-75/6ef97.jpg', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 10),
(79, 'F1,GP de MiamiLeclerc signe le meilleur temps de la séance d\'essais libres', 'La saison de F1 a repris ce vendredi avec une séance d\'essais libres de 90 minutes sur le circuit de Miami. Unique session du week-end puisque des qualifications sprint sont prévues à 22h30, et rallongée de 30 minutes afin d\'offrir plus de temps de roulage aux 11 écuries, alors que des ajustements sur le règlement technique et la récupération d\'énergie ont été adoptés durant les cinq semaines de pause forcée. Dans ces conditions, et alors que dix écuries ont apporté des évolutions en Floride - seul Aston Martin n\'a rien changé sur sa monoplace - il n\'y a pas eu de grand changement dans la hiérarchie, puisqu\'on a retrouvé Mercedes, Ferrari et McLaren aux avant-postes. Lando Norris (McLaren) a passé la première demi-heure au sommet de la feuille de temps, en 1\'30\'\'688 puis 1\'30\'\'335, en pneus durs, avant d\'être devancé par le leader du Championnat Kimi Antonelli (Mercedes - 1\'30\'\'079) puis par Charles Leclerc (Ferrari - 1\'29\'\'855). On a retrouvé les mêmes pilotes en fin de séance lorsqu\'ils ont passé les pneus tendres pour aller chercher un peu plus de grip, sur une piste verte qui a entraîné quelques passages au large et pas mal de survirages et de sous-virages, et un peu plus de performance. Max Verstappen (Red Bull) s\'est alors tout de même mêlé à la lutte pour le meilleur chrono, en signant 1\'29\'\'776, mais il n\'a tenu que quelques secondes, Leclerc allant un peu plus vite, en 1\'29\'\'443 puis 1\'29\'\'310 dans les derniers instants, un chrono deux secondes plus lent que celui de la même séance l\'an dernier. C\'est donc le Monégasque qui finit en tête de cette unique session d\'essais libres du week-end, 29 centièmes devant le quadruple champion du monde et 44 devant Oscar Piastri (McLaren). Lewis Hamilton (Ferrari) a pris la 4e place, devant la première Mercedes, celle d\'Antonelli, qui pointe tout de même à sept dixièmes, et devance de deux centièmes celle de George Russell. Norris a lui terminé à la 7e place, à huit dixièmes. Dans le clan français, le mieux placé est Pierre Gasly, 8e avec son Alpine (+1\'\'27), juste devant Isack Hadjar (Red Bull - +1\'\'56), et Esteban Ocon (Haas) occupe la 16e place, à 2\'\'32.', 'https://www.lequipe.fr/Formule-1/Actualites/Charles-leclerc-signe-le-meilleur-temps-de-la-seance-d-essais-libres-du-grand-prix-de-miami-aucune-mercedes-dans-le-top-3/1672404', NULL, '2026-05-01 20:20:15', '2026-05-01 20:20:16', 'Rugby', 4, 3, 'fr', 'https://www.lequipe.fr/_medias/img-photo-jpg/leclerc-a-idealement-lance-son-week-end-sur-le-circuit-floridien-marco-bello-reuters/1500000002454967/0:0,1833:1222-640-427-75/df4e1.jpg', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 10),
(80, 'Foot,FC BarceloneKoundé sur le départ ?', 'Devenu le deuxième Français le plus capé du Barça lors de la rencontre face à Getafe samedi dernier (2-0), mais suspendu ce samedi face à Osasuna (21 heures), Jules Koundé compte 186 apparitions, toutes compétitions confondues, avec le club catalan. En ligne de mire désormais : les 193 matches d\'Éric Abidal. Mais l\'ancien Bordelais, arrivé à Barcelone en 2022, aura-t-il le temps de battre ce record ? Selon le journal Sport, rien n\'est moins sûr. Le latéral des Bleus (27 ans, 46 sélections) serait sur la liste des départs et pourrait quitter les Blaugranas dès cet été après avoir pourtant prolongé son contrat en août dernier jusqu\'en juin 2030. En réalité, l\'équation est plus complexe. Le joueur se sent bien en Catalogne et ne souhaite pas quitter le club, ni la région. Interrogé au mois de mars, un proche a confirmé que Koundé était très heureux et qu\'il se sentait de mieux en mieux après un début de saison compliqué marqué par un retour de blessure contractée à la fin d\'un exercice 2024-2025 très réussi sur le plan individuel et collectif (triplé national). L\'entraîneur du Barça, Hansi Flick, est lui aussi assez clair sur ses intentions et souhaite que son latéral reste. Meilleur allié de Lamine Yamal sur l\'aile droite de l\'équipe, Koundé connaît pourtant une véritable baisse de niveau cette saison. Une mauvaise passe qui n\'a échappé à personne, mais qui est loin d\'être rédhibitoire pour le technicien allemand. La preuve : l\'international français n\'a jamais perdu sa place dans l\'équipe titulaire, au contraire de son coéquipier à gauche, Alejandro Baldé, sous la pression de Joao Cancelo. Dans les faits, le Barça aimerait s\'offrir une grosse vente lors du mercato estival et s\'accorder une belle marge de fair-play financier pour s\'activer sur les dossiers importants de l\'attaquant de pointe et du défenseur central. Une offre perçue comme très satisfaisante pourrait ainsi faire pencher la balance vers un départ pour une bonne partie du vestiaire et Koundé ne fait pas exception, au contraire des incontestables Lamine Yamal, Pedri ou Pau Cubarsi. La cote de popularité du joueur en Angleterre, notamment à Chelsea et Manchester City, pourrait bousculer les choses mais, pour l\'heure, et comme souvent à quelques semaines du mercato, le temps est plutôt à la prospection.', 'https://www.lequipe.fr/Football/Article/Le-barca-veut-faire-une-grosse-vente-cet-ete-le-lateral-droit-des-bleus-jules-kounde-sur-le-depart/1672316', NULL, '2026-05-01 20:20:15', '2026-05-01 20:20:16', 'Football', 1, 3, 'fr', 'https://www.lequipe.fr/_medias/img-photo-jpg/lucas-digne-jules-kounde-et-les-freres-lucas-et-theo-hernandez-a-l-entrainement-de-l-equipe-de-france-en-octobre-p-lahalle-l-equipe/1500000002419037/0:0', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 10),
(81, 'Tennis de table,Mondiaux par équipesLes Bleus veulent renverser l\'intouchable Chine', 'Ils ont la classe, avec leurs casquettes gavroches, montres à gousset et costumes trois-pièces en tweed. Avant de s\'envoler pour l\'Angleterre, les Français du ping se sont transformés en Peaky Blinders, ce sulfureux gang criminel du Birmingham des années 1920, le temps d\'un shooting photo à la mode british. Visages fermés, les frères Lebrun, Simon Gauzy, Thibault Poret, Flavien Coton et leur coach Nathanaël Molin foulent d\'un pas assuré une ruelle pavée, sur fond de Big Ben embrumée. Derrière cette mise en scène, un message : les Bleus comptent bien rafler la mise aux Championnats du monde par équipes, qui se déroulent depuis mardi à Londres. Ils ont été privés d\'or par les Chinois, invaincus depuis 2001, lors de la dernière édition en Corée du Sud, il y a deux ans. Entre-temps, ces cinq joueurs sont devenus champions d\'Europe et ils ne se fixent désormais aucune limite. Il débarque à Londres dans la forme de sa vie, de retour à son meilleur classement (4e mondial) après six mois axés sur le travail physique. Pendant cette période de construction, les résultats ont été moins bons. Mais avec son sacre mi-mars au Champions de Chongqing, son sixième titre WTT, et un match phénoménal contre le patron du circuit Wang Chuqin (perdu 15-13 au 6e set) il y a un mois, à la Coupe du monde de Macao, Félix Lebrun a retrouvé son assurance. « J\'encaisse beaucoup d\'heures d\'entraînement sans être trop fatigué, promet le Montpelliérain de 19 ans. Je me sens très bien, dans la raquette aussi. » « Qu\'on joue ou qu\'on soit sur le banc, ça use autant d\'énergie. Il faut faire attention à ça tout en gardant une cohésion optimale » Son statut de chef de file des Bleus ne l\'intimide pas : « J\'aime cette position. Ça me donne confiance de voir qu\'il y a des joueurs extraordinaires à côté de moi et que je suis quand même le numéro 1 de l\'équipe. » Sur la « plus grande compétition de l\'année », Félix Lebrun va surveiller son influx nerveux, à la table comme aux encouragements : « Qu\'on joue ou qu\'on soit sur le banc, ça use autant d\'énergie. Il faut faire attention à ça tout en gardant une cohésion optimale. » Parole de capitaine avisé. Dernier rescapé du clan français à la Coupe du monde, éliminé en quarts à Macao, il attend ce rendez-vous collectif avec impatience. « Quand on voit l\'équipe qu\'on a, ça donne envie de se donner à fond parce qu\'on sait qu\'on peut aller chercher de grandes choses », apprécie le 12e mondial. S\'il se réjouit de l\'émulation au sein du groupe, le Montpelliérain de 22 ans n\'oublie pas qu\'à la table, il sera bel et bien seul face à son adversaire : « Ce qui compte, c\'est notre niveau de ping et on est les seuls à pouvoir le maîtriser. Mon objectif sera de répéter un niveau de top joueur sans trop de fluctuations et ce, pendant toute la compétition. » « On s\'est construit un beau palmarès et il faut réussir à l\'imposer, à montrer que jouer contre nous n\'est jamais une partie de plaisir » La médaille d\'argent glanée il y a deux ans place une cible dans le dos des Français, estime Alexis Lebrun : « On a un poids vis-à-vis des autres nations, on n\'est plus juste une équipe qui essaie. On s\'est construit un beau palmarès et il faut réussir à l\'imposer, à montrer que jouer contre nous n\'est jamais une partie de plaisir. » Les Taïwanais, premiers concurrents des Bleus, sont prévenus. Lorsqu\'il a décroché le premier de ses trois titres de champion de France en simple, en 2013, Félix Lebrun entrait à peine à l\'école primaire. Le Toulousain est, à 31 ans, le doyen des Bleus. « S\'il y a des émotions à partager, je le fais avec grand plaisir, confie avec fierté le 19e mondial. J\'ai aussi appris plein de choses des tout jeunes. » Gauzy goûte peu à ce nouveau format, qui place la France dans un groupe élite avec deux autres favoris, le Japon et l\'Allemagne, synonyme de rencontres éreintantes dès son entrée en lice : « Je comprends que ce soit super pour les téléspectateurs et les médias, par contre nous, on trouve ça un peu ridicule. On est tête de série numéro 2 pour la première fois de notre histoire, et on perd cet avantage. À part si on finit premiers de notre poule, mais ça va être compliqué. Ça met une pression, on va devoir se donner à 100 % dès le début et on sera peut-être rincés au bout de deux jours. » Rien n\'indique que Coton (23e mondial) ni Poret (26e) joueront une rencontre, puisqu\'ils sont numéros 4 et 5 français et que les trois mieux classés sont généralement alignés. Les remplaçants ont déjà connu ça en Croatie, aux Championnats d\'Europe par équipes, où ils ont été sacrés en octobre 2025 sans disputer le moindre match. Cette incertitude n\'entame pas leur motivation. « Je me prépare comme si j\'allais jouer, pour être prêt », jure Flavien Coton, 18 ans, récent vainqueur du Contender de Tunis. Le Nordiste, benjamin de la bande, connaît à Londres sa deuxième sélection. Même état d\'esprit pour Poret, 21 ans : « Le but, c\'est que l\'équipe soit la plus compétitive possible. Si je suis aligné, c\'est que je mérit', 'https://www.lequipe.fr/Tennis-de-table/Article/-quand-on-voit-l-equipe-qu-on-a-a-londres-les-bleus-veulent-renverser-la-chine-aux-mondiaux-par-equipes/1672415', NULL, '2026-05-01 20:20:15', '2026-05-01 20:20:16', 'Football', 1, 3, 'fr', 'https://www.lequipe.fr/_medias/img-photo-jpg/simon-gauzy-alexis-lebrun-nathanael-molin-felix-lebrun-entoures-de-thibault-poret-et-flavien-coton-pauce-yellodesign-fftt/1500000002454952/0:36,2000:1370-640-427-75/44678', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 10),
(82, '\"Me faire passer pour le méchant.\": le coordinateur du staff médical de Nantes annonce son départ, climat de plus en plus délétère chez les Canaris', 'Rien ne va plus au FC Nantes. Alors que l’équipe de Vahid Halilhodzic doit espérer un petit miracle pour se maintenir en Ligue 1, les sources de tension en interne se multiplie. Et voilà qu’un lourd climat de suspicion a poussé le coordinateur du staff médical a annoncé brutalement son départ à la fin de la saison. Nicolas-Pierre Bernot, en poste auprès de l’équipe première depuis 2014, est soupçonné d’avoir participer à faire virer un entraîneur du club, Luis Castro, en faisant remonter des informations à ses dirigeants et en particulier à son président Waldemar Kita. L’affaire éclate publiquement le 27 avril lorsque le président du FCN affirme au micro d’Eurosport: \"Quand quelqu\'un du corps médical vous dit: \'Président, il faut absolument changer cet entraîneur, on va à la catastrophe, il ne fait que des bêtises\'. Je fais quoi?\" Si l’identité du coach en question, Luis Castro, viré le 10 décembre, ne fait pas de doute, Waldemar Kita ne cite pas le nom du membre du staff médical. Le malaise grandit après que des journalistes de la presse locale confirment, toujours sans citer de nom, que le staff médical remonte bien des informations auprès des Kita, père et fils, qui gèrent souvent le club depuis Paris. Nicolas-Pierre Bernot est-il l’œil de Moscou qui a savonné la planche de Luis Castro? Faux assure l’intéressé, très remonté et attristé par ces suspicions: \"Je ne me sens plus en mesure de sacrifier ma vie pour être finalement sali de la sorte et jeté en pâture comme le coupable idéal et j’ai donc décidé d’arrêter, non sans difficulté et peine mais je n’ai pas d’autre choix\", a écrit le physiothérapeute dans un long message posté jeudi sur Instagram. \"Les reproches qui me sont faits ne reflètent absolument pas la réalité de ce qui se passe au club. Je suis profondément triste et déçu de ces attaques sur mon intégrité et d\'être positionné en bouc émissaire. (.) Je tiens à garantir sur ce que j\'ai de plus cher que je n\'ai jamais parlé au président pour critiquer seul des coachs qui sont passés au FC Nantes et pas davantage Luis Castro, avec qui j\'entretenais, d\'ailleurs, de très bons rapports. Je ne suis pas parfait mais je suis intègre, loyal et fidèle et je ne suis certainement pas le manipulateur machiavélique, sournois et fourbe qui a pu être décrit. M\'exposer ainsi et me faire passer pour le méchant, alors que j\'ai eu à cœur de tout mettre en œuvre au mieux pour le bien commun de l\'entreprise dans la bienveillance et la loyauté vis-à-vis de tous est inqualifiable.\" Nicolas-Pierre Bernot, 42 ans, a pu compter sur le soutien de Vahid Halilhodzic, coach avec lequel il avait déjà collaboré lors du premier passage du Bosnien sur le banc nantais entre octobre 2018 et août 2019. \"Les gens se sont trompés sur lui: compétence, professionnalisme, dévouement, attachement. J\'ai une grande reconnaissance de son travail. Les gens qui ont parlé de lui, ce n\'est pas correct\", a déclaré l’ancien buteur des Canaris jeudi en conférence de presse.', 'https://rmcsport.bfmtv.com/football/ligue-1/me-faire-passer-pour-le-mechant-le-coordinateur-du-staff-medical-de-nantes-annonce-son-depart-climat-de-plus-en-plus-deletere-chez-les-canaris_AV-202605010686.html', NULL, '2026-05-01 20:20:15', '2026-05-01 20:20:16', 'Football', 1, 3, 'fr', 'https://images.bfmtv.com/7b8tjx5XdrsfohX5BJC27tpI-NQ=/0x102:1424x903/images/Le-coordinateur-du-staff-medical-du-FC-Nantes-Nicolas-Pierre-Bernot-avec-Johann-Lepanant-face-a-Reims-le-2-fevrier-2025-2279513.jpg', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 6),
(83, 'Paul Pogba', 'Paul Pogba pourrait être titularisé pour le match de Monaco à Metz samedi (19h), dans le cadre de la 32e journée de Ligue 1. Le coach des Monégasques, Sébastien Pocognoli, a en tout cas testé cette option à l\'entraînement vendredi. Invité de Rothen s’enflamme sur RMC ce mardi, Mathias Pogba a donné des nouvelles de son frère Paul, qui accumule les pépins physiques depuis son retour à la compétition à l’AS Monaco. Arrivé l\'été dernier, Paul Pogba n\'a pour l\'heure disputé que trois bouts de matchs avec l\'AS Monaco, la faute à une succession de pépins physiques. Ses dirigeants ne savent pas quand il pourra reprendre la compétition. Paul Pogba a reçu le prix du meilleur \"retour\" lors de la cérémonie des Globe Soccer Awards ce dimanche à Dubaï. Ce qui a affligé de nombreux supporters mais aussi l\'ancien Lensois Jimmy Cabot, s\'étonnant d\'une telle récompense pour un joueur suspendu pour dopage. Une réunion improbable a eu lieu mercredi entre plusieurs personnalités du monde du foot et du MMA. Khabib Nurmagomedov, Zlatan Ibrahimovic et Paul Pogba se sont ainsi retrouvés à la même table. Pas que pour partager le repas. De retour progressivement sur les terrains après sa longue suspension, Paul Pogba fait aussi parler de lui en dehors des pelouses. Le milieu de terrain français s’est récemment affiché sur les réseaux sociaux en officialisant son partenariat avec l’Al Haboob Camel Racing Team, une équipe de courses de chameaux basée en Arabie saoudite, au sein de laquelle il officiera comme ambassadeur et actionnaire. Le choc de clôture de la 16e journée de Ligue 1 ce dimanche entre l\'OM et Monaco (20h45) se jouera sans Paul Pogba, victime d\'une gêne au mollet gauche. Resté sur le banc mardi lors de la victoire de l\'AS Monaco face à Galatasaray en Ligue des champions, Paul Pogba a une gêne physique, selon son entraîneur Sébastien Pocognoli. L\'international français reste dans la salle d\'attente avant le déplacement de Monaco à Marseille dimanche. Alors qu\'il vient de faire son retour sur les terrains de football après plus de deux ans d\'absence, Paul Pogba a également franchi une nouvelle étape en dehors des pelouses. Le champion du monde 2018 est devenu actionnaire et ambassadeur d\'Al Haboob, une équipe professionnelle de courses de chameaux en Arabie saoudite. Après une absence de plus de deux ans liée à sa suspension pour dopage et à ses blessures, Paul Pogba a disputé ses premières minutes avec Monaco ces derniers jours en Ligue 1. Un \"Pogback\" chaudement salué par son frère Mathias Pogba, qui a posté un long message pour le féliciter. Après sa deuxième apparition avec l’AS Monaco, samedi soir face au PSG (1-0), Paul Pogba est allé à la rencontre des supporters de l’ASM. L’occasion de leur demander de mettre un peu plus d’ambiance au stade Louis II. Longtemps devant face à Pafos, Monaco a fini par craquer en fin de match et concède le match nul en terre chypriote (2-2). En difficulté en Ligue 1, l\'ASM ne rassure pas non plus en Ligue des champions avec seulement 6 points en 5 journées. Paul Pogba s\'est longuement échauffé sans entrer en jeu. Avant le déplacement à Pafos en Ligue des champions mercredi (21h), Sébastien Pocognoli et Denis Zakaria ont loué le retour de Paul Pogba, qui a joué ses premières minutes le week-end dernier à Rennes. Au lendemain de ses débuts avec l\'AS Monaco, et de son premier match depuis septembre 2023, Paul Pogba est revenu ce dimanche sur une soirée pas comme les autres, et a remercié tous ses soutiens. Longtemps divisés par une affaire \"d\'extorsion en bande organisée\", les frères Pogba se sont récemment réconciliés. Alors, quand Paul Pogba a foulé ce samedi le terrain de Rennes pour son grand retour après sa suspension, ses frères Florentin et Mathias se sont réjouis sur leurs réseaux sociaux. Entré en jeu à la 85e minute ce samedi 22 novembre lors de Rennes-Monaco en Ligue 1, Paul Pogba a effectué son grand retour sur un terrain de football, 811 jours après son dernier match. Une première étape pour la Pioche, qui veut désormais enchaîner. Après plus de deux ans sans jouer, Paul Pogba est redevenu un joueur de football samedi lors du match Rennes-Monaco, comptant pour la 13e journée de Ligue 1. L’international français est entré en seconde période. Paul Pogba est du déplacement de l\'AS Monaco à Rennes ce samedi (19h). Rétabli, celui qu\'on surnomme \"la Pioche\" devrait y jouer les premières minutes de sa carrière monégasque après 26 mois éloignés des terrains. Une bonne nouvelle pour son club mais aussi pour la Ligue 1. et potentiellement l’équipe de France. Plus de deux ans après son dernier match officiel, Paul Pogba est bien parti pour rejouer avec Monaco ce samedi. Pour la première fois de la saison, le champion du monde 2018 fait partie du groupe retenu pour affronter Rennes. Cinq mois après sa signature à Monaco et vingt-six après ses dernières minutes en pro, Paul Pogba va faire, sauf pépin de dernière minute, son retour sur une feuille de match à Rennes. Un peu plus d\'un mois', 'https://rmcsport.bfmtv.com/football/paul-pogba_DN-202108310555.html', NULL, '2021-09-01 00:00:00', '2026-05-01 20:20:16', 'Football', 1, 3, 'fr', 'https://images.bfmtv.com/K6nVOK2qHwdNWD6TgQ5WwnaamEA=/0x36:2048x1188/images/Paul-Pogba-1163983.jpg', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 6),
(84, 'Metz-Monaco: et si Pogba débutait?', 'Ce vendredi à La Turbie, lors de la dernière séance avant de prendre la direction de Metz, Paul Pogba a été essayé parmi les titulaires lors de la mise en place tactique de Sébastien Pocognoli. L\'entraineur belge pourrait en effet offrir à \"La Pioche\", ce samedi en Lorraine lors du match Metz-Monaco, sa première titularisation depuis mai 2023 lors d\'un Juventus-Cremonese. Depuis plusieurs jours, le champion du monde 2018 ne porte plus de strap ou d\'attelle autour de son genou droit, comme ce fut le cas régulièrement ces dernières semaines. Après trois matchs sans victoire, Sébastien Pocognoli cherche la solution pour donner un sursaut à l\'ASM en cette fin de saison. Plusieurs dispositifs ont été travaillé lors des dernières séances, un changement de système n\'est pas à exclure et pourrait profiter à Paul Pogba. Entré en jeu à cinq reprises cette saison, il devrait voir son nom être couché parmi les onze premiers cette fois-ci à Saint-Symphorien. \"Il ne fait rien d’autre, il n’est concentré que sur ça\": comment Ciryl Gane prépare depuis Paris son combat contre Alex Pereira, à deux mois de l\'UFC Maison-Blanche', 'https://rmcsport.bfmtv.com/football/ligue-1/metz-monaco-et-si-pogba-debutait_AP-202605010677.html', NULL, '2026-05-01 20:20:15', '2026-05-01 20:20:16', 'Football', 1, 3, 'fr', 'https://images.bfmtv.com/naRCN1DeGwGk5Buzr2vAG7EJRwE=/0x106:2048x1258/images/Paul-Pogba-sur-le-banc-de-l-AS-Monaco-5-avril-2026-2265346.jpg', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 6),
(85, '\"Je ne veux pas de gens près de moi qui pleurent\", le message musclé de De Zerbi à ses joueurs avant Aston Villa-Tottenham', 'L\'entraîneur de Tottenham, Roberto De Zerbi, veut \"faire taire la petite voix\" interne qui s\'attarde sur les nombreux blessés plutôt que sur les qualités de l\'équipe, a-t-dit vendredi, à deux jours d\'un déplacement à Aston Villa crucial pour le maintien en Premier League. L\'actuel dix-huitième et premier relégable doit finir la saison sans le milieu offensif Xavi Simons, gravement blessé le week-end dernier, et il n\'aura pas récupéré à temps le gardien Guglielmo Vicario et l\'attaquant Dominic Solanke pour le match à Birmingham, dimanche. Mais De Zerbi, nommé fin mars, a voulu chasser le vent de négativité qui balaye le club du nord de Londres dans un long monologue au début de sa conférence de presse vendredi. \"Le défi le plus important maintenant, c\'est de faire taire la petite voix qui est en nous, les joueurs, le staff, les supporters. Ces voix produisent des pensées négatives et disent que nous n\'avons pas de chance, que nous avons trop de blessés (.), que notre staff médical n\'est pas assez bon, que la pelouse du stade n\'est pas bonne, que celle du centre d\'entraînement non plus, qu\'il est impossible de gagner deux ou trois matches de suite\", a-t-il dit, six jours après avoir enregistré la première victoire de l\'année 2026 en championnat, contre Wolverhampton. \"Si Solanke et Xavi Simons sont blessés, nous pouvons jouer avec Kolo Muani, Mathys Tel, Richarlison (.), ils sont différents dans leurs caractéristiques mais ce sont de très bons joueurs\", a-t-il dit. A écouter certains médias, \"on a l\'impression que tout le monde pleure et que nous sommes déjà relégués. Non, pas encore. Il faut mourir sur le terrain\", a-t-il dit, en visant spécifiquement un reporter de Sky Sports présent à la conférence de presse. Certes, \"c\'est un moment difficile, mais les perdants, eux, pleurent, ils pensent négativement. Je ne veux pas de gens près de moi qui pleurent et qui pensent différemment de moi. Nous sommes assez bons pour gagner des matches et assez bons pour nous maintenir\", a-t-il assuré. Tottenham compte deux points de moins que l\'actuel premier non relégable, West Ham (qui joue samedi à Brentford), avant les quatre dernières journées. \"Il ne fait rien d’autre, il n’est concentré que sur ça\": comment Ciryl Gane prépare depuis Paris son combat contre Alex Pereira, à deux mois de l\'UFC Maison-Blanche', 'https://rmcsport.bfmtv.com/football/premier-league/je-ne-veux-pas-de-gens-pres-de-moi-qui-pleurent-le-message-muscle-de-de-zerbi-a-ses-joueurs-avant-aston-villa-tottenham_AD-202605010645.html', NULL, '2026-05-01 20:20:15', '2026-05-01 20:20:16', 'Football', 1, 3, 'fr', 'https://images.bfmtv.com/DAi8vFIkC15EIoHi-UBrtEAoZVc=/0x0:1680x945/images/L-entraineur-de-Tottenham-Roberto-De-Zerbi-face-a-Wolverhampton-le-25-avril-2026-2279483.jpg', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 6),
(86, 'Roberto De Zerbi', 'En grand danger en Premier League, Tottenham, 18e du classement, jouera gros dimanche soir lors d’un déplacement sur la pelouse d’Aston Villa (20h). L’entraîneur italien des Spurs Roberto De Zerbi a prévenu ses joueurs : il n’y aura pas de place pour des états d’âme. À Marseille, le début de semaine a été explosif entre le départ de Roberto De Zerbi et la proposition de démission de Medhi Benatia, qui a été refusée par sa direction. Si le nom de Habib Beye revient en boucle, aucun nouvel entraîneur n\'a encore été nommé. Et c\'est Pancho Abardonado qui assurera l\'intérim samedi contre Strasbourg. Suivez en live toutes les infos et réactions après l\'annonce du départ de Roberto De Zerbi de son poste d\'entraîneur de l\'OM dans la nuit de mardi à mercredi. Après l’éviction de Roberto De Zerbi dans la nuit de mardi à mercredi, l’Olympique de Marseille cherche un entraîneur pour lui succéder. Selon les informations de RMC Sport, des techniciens prestigieux sont suivis de près ou proposés à la direction phocéenne. Roberto De Zerbi n\'est plus l\'entraîneur de l\'Olympique de Marseille depuis le milieu de la nuit de ce mercredi. D\'après nos informations, le départ du technicien italien a été facilité par un effort financier de sa part. Roberto De Zerbi et l’OM ont acté la fin de leur collaboration, mais cela ne s’est pas fait de gaité de cœur. Les joueurs sont désormais, aussi, en première ligne. Pier Gauthier, préparateur mental, estime que le départ de Roberto De Zerbi de l’OM va soulager une partie de l’effectif, usé par des décisions étonnantes et des ressorts psychologiques assez peu lisibles. Roberto De Zerbi a été écarté de ses fonctions d\'entraîneur de l\'Olympique de Marseille dans la nuit de mardi à mercredi. Si l\'Italien n\'a pas gagné de trophée avec le club phocéen, il possède le meilleur pourcentage de victoire d\'un technicien marseillais depuis le début des années 2000. L’annonce du départ de Roberto De Zerbi de l’OM dans la nuit de mardi à mercredi met déjà en alerte la Premier League où plusieurs clubs apprécient le profil de l’Italien après son passage à Brighton (2022-2024). Comme annoncé par RMC Sport quelques heures plus tôt, l\'OM a officialisé le départ de son entraîneur Roberto De Zerbi dans un communiqué publié dans la nuit de mardi à mercredi. L\'Italien quitte le club un an et demi après son arrivée. L’entraînement du jour et les échanges avec les joueurs et les dirigeants sont sur le point de sceller le sort de Roberto De Zerbi à l\'OM. Le départ de l’entraîneur italien est proche. Deux jours après la claque reçue par l\'Olympique de Marseille face au PSG (5-0), Roberto De Zerbi a bien animé la séance d\'entraînement ce mardi à la Commanderie. Le technicien a travaillé normalement malgré les doutes autour de son avenir à la tête de l\'équipe phocéenne. La déconvenue infligée par le Paris Saint-Germain au Parc des Princes (5-0) plonge de nouveau l’Olympique de Marseille dans la crise. Roberto De Zerbi se sent trahi par ses joueurs et donne le sentiment de se trouver dans une impasse. Alors que Roberto De Zerbi est la cible des critiques depuis l’élimination de l’Olympique de Marseille en Ligue des champions, son homologue parisien Luis Enrique a tenu à le défendre samedi à la veille du Classique PSG-OM dimanche au Parc des Princes. Roberto De Zerbi est revenu ce vendredi sur la très bonne passe de Mason Greenwood sur les derniers matchs de l’Olympique de Marseille. Selon l’entraîneur italien, la star anglaise a compris les critiques contre lui et est devenu plus humain au quotidien. Présent en conférence de presse ce vendredi, à deux jours du Classique face au PSG (dimanche à 20h45), Roberto De Zerbi en a remis une couche sur le devoir d\'exemplarité qu\'il attend de ses joueurs. Actuel troisième de Ligue 1, l\'Olympique de Marseille se rendra dimanche au Parc des Princes pour y défier le PSG, en clôture de la 21e journée. Avant ce Classique, Roberto De Zerbi a pris la parole en conférence de presse ce vendredi. L\'entraîneur phocéen a notamment rappelé le besoin de tout donner et d\'avoir faim sur le terrain. L\'OM s\'est de nouveau montré très actif dans la dernière ligne droite du mercato hivernal, que ce soit dans le sens des arrivées comme des départs. Présent en conférence de presse ce lundi, Roberto De Zerbi a expliqué qu\'une partie de ces mouvements étaient liée à des considérations économiques. A la veille d’un OM-Rennes sous haute tension en 8es de finale de la Coupe de France, Roberto De Zerbi est revenu sur un vif échange entre Geoffrey Kondogbia et Arthur Vermeeren dimanche à l’entraînement. Non seulement le coach marseillais ne leur en veut pas mais il encourage ses joueurs à se fâcher, mais seulement sur le terrain. Ce lundi, Roberto De Zerbi est revenu sur sa décision de mettre à l\'écart Amir Murillo. Selon le coach de l\'OM, le latéral panaméen paye son manque d\'implication. En pleine crise, l\'Olympique de Marseille a décidé d\'accéder à la demande des supporters, qui ont réclamé une réunion a', 'https://rmcsport.bfmtv.com/football/roberto-de-zerbi_DN-202508100322.html', NULL, '2025-08-11 00:42:25', '2026-05-01 20:20:16', 'Football', 1, 3, 'fr', 'https://images.bfmtv.com/zMyOVSqcUfP-3bmT8opzV6Lo2pQ=/0x83:2048x1235/images/Roberto-De-Zerbi-a-l-entrainement-de-l-OM-28-fevrier-2025-2059578.jpg', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 6),
(87, 'Lionel Messi', 'Dans le podcast Stick To Football, le sélectionneur de Team USA Mauricio Pochettino est revenu sur un épisode marquant de son passage sur le banc du PSG : le jour où il a décidé de sortir Lionel Messi avant la fin d\'un match face à Lyon au Parc des Princes. Lionel Messi a inscrit mercredi le 900e but de sa carrière, en marquant pour l\'Inter Miami contre Nashville en 8e de finale aller de la Ligue des champions Concacaf. Selon un sondage effectué par un média catalan, seulement 10% des votants souhaitent un retour de Lionel Messi au FC Barcelone comme joueur, près de cinq ans après son départ du club pour le PSG. Ce dimanche, les socios éliront le nouveau président du FC Barcelone. L’homme d’affaires Victor Font va faire face au président sortant, Joan Laporta, et promet une rupture totale avec la gestion menée par son rival. Après avoir racheté les droits du championnat saoudien et ceux de l\'équipe de France espoir, l\'influenceur Zack Nani, s\'attaque à l\'Inter Miami de Lionel Messi. Le Lyonnais diffusera tous les matchs de l\'équipe américaine lors des phase finale de la CONCACAF sur sa chaine Twitch et Youtube, et ça débute dès cette nuit face à Nashville. Dans une interview livrée à ESPN, Ronald Koeman, ancien coach du FC Barcelone entre 2020 et 2021, raconte comment s\'est déroulée l\'arrivée de Pedri en Catalogne et le lien qu\'il a rapidement développé avec la légende du club, Lionel Messi. Au cours d\'une interview au média Bloomberg, Jorge Mas, le co-propriétaire de l\'Inter Miami, a révélé la somme donnée à Lionel Messi chaque année. Si le salaire de l\'Argentin est d\'environ 20 millions de dollars, il coûte en réalité bien plus que ça à la franchise floridienne. Dans une interview au journal espagnol la Vanguardia, Xavi, ancien entraîneur du FC Barcelone, a lourdement réglé ses comptes contre son ancien président Joan Laporta, qu’il a accuse notamment de s’être opposé au retour de Lionel Messi en 2023. Champions des Etats-Unis en MLS, les joueurs de l’Inter Miami, emmenés par leur star Lionel Messi, ont été reçus par le président américain Donald Trump jeudi à Washington. À 38 ans, Lionel Messi s\'est illustré ce dimanche avec son club de l\'Inter Miami, tombeur d\'Orlando en MLS. La légende argentine a inscrit un doublé dont un coup franc dont il a le secret. Disputé à Puerto Rico, un match amical ce jeudi soir entre l\'Inter Miami et l\'Independiente del Valle a été marqué par un incident. Plusieurs supporters sont entrés sur le terrain en fin de match et l\'un d\'entre eux a provoqué la chute de Lionel Messi. Les prochaines élections présidentielles du FC Barcelone auront lieu le 15 mars. Parmi les opposants à Joan Laporta, l’homme d’affaires barcelonais Marc Ciria promet aux socios de tout mettre en œuvre pour faire revenir Lionel Messi. Invité exceptionnel de Rothen s’enflamme ce jeudi sur RMC, il a détaillé son projet, ses ambitions et sa vision pour le club catalan. Dans son livre Voici comment nous avons sauvé le Barça, Joan Laporta revient notamment sur l\'échec de la prolongation et le départ de Lionel Messi en 2021, puis son retour avorté en 2023 après son aventure au PSG. L\'ancien président du Barça a révélé une anecdote qui dit beaucoup de sa relation avec l\'icône argentine. En marge de la cérémonie du Ballon d\'Or 2023, Lionel Messi aurait refusé de saluer Laporta. Frustré par des décisions arbitrales après la claque reçue face au Los Angeles FC (3-0) samedi soir en ouverture de la MLS, Lionel Messi avait tenté d\'entrer dans la salle réservée aux arbitres. Les instances du football nord-américain ne sanctionneront pas le joueur de l\'Inter Miami néanmoins. Champion en titre, l\'Inter Miami a subi une défaite cinglante 3-0 face au Los Angeles FC de Hugo Lloris samedi lors de la 1ere journée de la MLS. Décevant et diminué physiquement, Lionel Messi n\'a pas pesé lors de la rencontre. Candidat à la présidence du FC Barcelone contre Joan Laporta, Marc Ciria a déployé ce mercredi une affiche sur un bâtiment de la ville, où l\'on voit Lionel Messi en train de brandir son maillot numéro 10 et ce slogan: \"Au plaisir de vous revoir\". La sortie de terrain de plusieurs joueurs sénégalais dimanche lors de la finale de la CAN 2025 a rappelé un précédent quand Lionel Messi avait refusé de débuter un match de l’Argentine contre le Brésil en raison de violences policières contre les supporters en tribunes. Elu personnalité de l\'année par le journal portugais A Bola, Vitinha est revenu sur sa première saison compliquée au PSG. Le milieu de terrain de 25 ans en a profité pour désamorcer de prétendues relations tendues avec Neymar et Lionel Messi. Maria Sol Messi, sœur de Lionel Messi, a été victime d\'un grave accident de la route à Miami. Bien que hors de danger, la sœur de la Pulga a dû reporter son mariage initialement prévu dans dix jours. L’Espagne, championne d’Europe 2024, et l’Argentine, lauréate de la Copa America 2024 et tenante du titre mondial, se retrouveront le 27 mars au Qatar pour disputer la Finalissima lo', 'https://rmcsport.bfmtv.com/football/lionel-messi_DN-201411260316.html', NULL, '2014-11-26 16:06:00', '2026-05-01 20:20:16', 'Football', 1, 3, 'fr', 'https://images.bfmtv.com/wSz-TLhBIJIx6s5ctRnCe8yxZ_0=/4x57:1044x642/images/-876424.jpg', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 6);
INSERT INTO `articles` (`id`, `title`, `content`, `url`, `author`, `published_at`, `collected_at`, `sport_category`, `sport_id`, `importance_score`, `langue`, `image_url`, `nb_mots`, `status`, `sentiment`, `metadata`, `source_id`) VALUES
(88, '\"En Argentine, ils sont en train de te détruire\": les souvenirs de Pochettino quand il a sorti Messi avec le PSG', '19 septembre 2021 : le Paris Saint-Germain accueille l’Olympique Lyonnais au Parc des Princes pour le compte de la 6e journée de Ligue 1. Si les Parisiens s’imposent à la dernière seconde grâce à un but de Mauro Icardi (2-1), le fait du match se déroule à 76e lorsque Mauricio Pochettino décide de faire sortir Lionel Messi, remplacé par Achraf Hakimi. Une décision très commentée, la Pulga n’ayant pas pour habitude d’être sortie avant le coup de sifflet final. L’Argentin était d’ailleurs sorti du terrain le visage fermé, signe qu’il avait peut-être peu gouté le choix de son entraîneur. Cinq ans plus tard, Mauricio Pochettino n’a rien oublié de cet épisode marquant de son son passage au PSG (2021-2022). S’il regrette aujourdhui de ne pas avoir demandé l’avis de sa star, l’actuel sélectionneur des Etats-Unis justifie son choix, comme il y a cinq ans, en expliquant avoir voulu protéger Lionel Messi, touché au genou. \"Mon intention était de le préserver en vue de la Ligue des champions\", a confirmé Mauricio Pochettino, invité du podcast Stick To Football. \"Si je n’avais pas fait ce choix, il se serait blessé, ce qui aurait eu des conséquences sur la Coupe du monde 2022.\" Ce soir-là, dans les couloir du Parc des Princes, la décision de sortir Lionel Messi passe assez mal, notamment auprès de Leonardo, l’ex-directeur sportif du club parisien. Pochettino se souvient avoir été interpellé par le Brésilien après le match: \"\"Mauri\" pourquoi? J’en ai parlé à Léo et il m’a dit qu’il s’en fichait. Les gens payent pour le voir jouer 90 minutes.\" Si l’entraîneur parisien pensait en avoir terminé avec cette affaire ce soir-là en rentrant à son domicile, erreur. Sa femme, elle aussi, a remis une pièce dans la machine: \"En Argentine, ils sont en train de te détruire. Et en France aussi\", lui a-t-elle lancé. Des critiques qui n\'ont pas affecté plus que ça le technicien argentin: \"Je ne voulais pas prouver que j\'étais plus courageux que n\'importe quel autre entraîneur, mais sur le moment, cela me semblait être la meilleure chose à faire pour lui\", conclut Pochettino.', 'https://rmcsport.bfmtv.com/football/clubs/paris-saint-germain/en-argentine-ils-sont-en-train-de-te-detruire-les-souvenirs-de-pochettino-quand-il-a-sorti-messi-avec-le-psg_AV-202605010619.html', NULL, '2026-05-01 20:20:15', '2026-05-01 20:20:16', 'Football', 1, 3, 'fr', 'https://images.bfmtv.com/gx6-W3o3v13k59OXYSAWX6kZ8VI=/0x0:2048x1152/images/Aux-cotes-de-Mauricio-Pochettino-Lionel-Messi-fait-la-moue-apres-son-remplacement-lors-de-PSG-Lyon-le-19-septembre-2021-2279461.jpg', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 6),
(89, 'Allen and Wu play out longest Crucible frame amid World Championship chaos', 'A mammoth afternoon session between Wu Yize and Mark Allen saw the longest frame in World Championship history completed. The 2026 World Snooker Championship continues in Sheffield with the semi-finals as the remaining four players battle for a spot in the final. Zhao Xintong produced an incredible \'hat-trick shot\' to pot three balls at once during his thrilling quarter-final tie against Shaun Murphy on Tuesday at the World Snooker Championship. Gerwyn Price says he intends to take up an offer to compete at the UK Open Pool Championship in May regardless of whether it clashes with the Premier League Darts Play-Offs. Neil Robertson called for the World Snooker Tour (WST) to ban a contentious type of chalk used by Ronnie O\'Sullivan, claiming the abrasive compound is \"hated\" by most professional players because it creates \"kicks\" that can be \"unfair on players who aren\'t using it\". Ronnie O\'Sullivan\'s bid for a record-breaking eighth Crucible title was ended as John Higgins secured a remarkable comeback win at the World Snooker Championship, while world No 1 Judd Trump was dumped out by first-time quarter-finalist Hossein Vafaei. Ronnie O\'Sullivan revealed he had a flight home booked for Monday morning in anticipation of losing his World Snooker Championship match against John Higgins with a session to spare. Ronnie O\'Sullivan thumped the table in frustration as John Higgins fought back in the second session of their second round match at the World Snooker Championship on Sunday night. Ronnie O\'Sullivan carved out a 6-2 overnight lead against old foe John Higgins in the first session of their second-round showdown at the World Snooker Championship in Sheffield. Hossein Vafaei has claimed the Crucible must be respected and called it snooker\'s answer to Wimbledon two years on from his scathing criticism of the World Championship venue. \"I thought a bit of a roll of the dice, it was a gamble. I was a bit nervous because I thought you could look a bit silly.\" Ronnie O\'Sullivan wasted little time in wrapping up a comprehensive 10-2 victory over He Guoqiang to set up a blockbuster showdown with John Higgins in round two of the World Snooker Championship. Ronnie O’Sullivan started with a rare Crucible misstep but still emerged with a 7-2 lead after the opening session of his first-round match against China’s He Guoqiang at the World Snooker Championship in Sheffield. He is the most decorated snooker player in the history of the game and fans\' favourite, yet Ronnie O\'Sullivan, like other legendary sportspeople, seeks ultimate perfection. Shaun Murphy has criticised Ronnie O\'Sullivan and Judd Trump after the duo skipped the official media day on the eve of the World Snooker Championship in Sheffield. Ronnie O\'Sullivan has been drawn to face Chinese debutant He Guoqiang as he attempts to win a record eighth World Snooker Championship title at The Crucible. Michal Szubarczyk became the youngest winner of a World Snooker Championship match in the first qualifying round. Mark Selby says he would like to see the World Snooker Championship stay in the UK when the Crucible is being refurbished. Snooker World Championship is set to stay at the iconic Crucible Theatre in Sheffield until 2045 with venue also set to benefit from a major refurbishment after 2028. Ronnie O\'Sullivan has revealed he was \"probably\" not going to enter this year\'s World Snooker Championship prior to his impressive run to Sunday\'s final at the World Open.', 'https://www.skysports.com/snooker/news/12040/13538999/world-snooker-championship-mark-allen-and-wu-yize-play-out-longest-crucible-frame-amid-chaos', NULL, '2026-05-01 20:20:15', '2026-05-01 20:20:16', 'Football', 1, 4, 'en', NULL, NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 7),
(90, 'Leclerc fastest in upgraded Ferrari as Mercedes hit trouble before Sprint Qualifying', 'Ferrari\'s Charles Leclerc set the pace in the only practice session in Miami as Mercedes ran into power unit issues on F1\'s return after no races in April; watch Sprint Qualifying later on Friday evening at 9.30pm, with build-up from 8.40pm, live on Sky Sports F1 Charles Leclerc was fastest in Miami Grand Prix Practice in a heavily-upgraded Ferrari as both Mercedes drivers suffered problems on Formula 1\'s return. Leclerc set two lap times quick enough to top the only practice session to beat Red Bull\'s Max Verstappen by 0.297s, with the early indications suggesting Mercedes no longer have the outright fastest car going into Sprint Qualifying at 9.30pm later on Friday, live on Sky Sports F1. Oscar Piastri was third but his McLaren team-mate Lando Norris appeared to be more competitive and would have been close to Leclerc without traffic and a near-miss with Williams\' Alex Albon. Lewis Hamilton was 0.467s adrift of Leclerc and trailed his Ferrari team-mate throughout the 90-minute practice session - a continuation of the last F1 race weekend in Japan at the end of March. Mercedes have won the opening three Grands Prix and are unbeaten in competitive sessions this year, but have brought the fewest upgrades of the top teams. The Silver Arrows only have a revised front corner and new tailpipe compared to the new floors on the McLarens, Red Bulls and Ferraris. Russell was nearly eight tenths off the pace in sixth, behind Antonelli who set his best time on the hard tyres as a power unit problem prevented him from doing a soft tyre run. That power unit issue will be Mercedes\' biggest concern after Russell earlier reported a strange noise from the turbo that sounded like a \"steam engine\". Antonelli leads Russell by nine points in the Drivers\' Championship but the two Mercedes may not have everything their own way this weekend in Miami. \"That\'s the question mark coming out of this session as, otherwise, we\'ve suddenly got three other teams in that fight.\" The five-week gap since the last F1 race in Japan has given the teams the opportunity to work hard on development and every team, apart from Aston Martin, have brought upgrades to Miami. Ferrari have the most, with 11 new parts, and it seems to have paid off given Leclerc\'s blistering pace in a car that was already strong in the corners. The new floor and suspension on the Ferrari appears to have given them even more downforce, while McLaren and Red Bull have also come to Miami with effectively new cars. McLaren already made gains on Mercedes at the last race in Japan, but Norris in particular shone in practice on Friday in Miami and will be hopeful of a second victory at the track he took his maiden Grand Prix win at back in 2024. Red Bull were, on average, just over one second off the pace, but may have closed down that deficit to give Verstappen a more balanced car which he can push harder. Team principal Laurent Mekies told Sky Sports F1: \"Honestly, we only looked at ourselves during that session. It was so important after the big break and with all the big changes on the car to try to assess us against us, really that was the main purpose. \"In China and Japan, regardless of where the competition was, there were a lot of things that were stopping Max and Isaac from pushing, and that\'s what we\'re trying to fix. \"The gap to competition we\'ll look at a bit later, but certainly on Max\'s side there is a sign that we have something he can push a bit more with.\" Friday May 17.25pm: F2 Qualifying8.10pm: Team Bosses\' Press Conference8.40pm: Miami GP Sprint Qualifying (session starts at 9.30pm) Saturday May 22.55pm: F2 Sprint4pm: Miami GP Sprint build-up5pm: MIAMI GP SPRINT6.30pm: Ted\'s Sprint Notebook8pm: Miami GP Qualifying build-up*9pm: MIAMI GP QUALIFYING*11pm: Ted\'s Qualifying Notebook* Sunday May 35.25pm: F2 Feature Race7pm: Miami GP build-up: Grand Prix Sunday*9pm: THE MIAMI GRAND PRIX*11pm: Miami GP reaction: Chequered Flag*12am: Ted\'s Notebook* Formula 1 is in Miami for a Sprint weekend as the 2026 season resumes, watch live on Sky Sports F1 with Sunday\'s Grand Prix at 9pm. Stream Sky Sports with NOW - no contract, cancel anytime', 'https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12040/13538900/miami-gp-charles-leclerc-fastest-in-upgraded-ferrari-as-mercedes-hit-power-unit-problems-ahead-of-sprint-qualifying', NULL, '2026-05-01 20:20:15', '2026-05-01 20:20:16', 'Football', 1, 3, 'en', 'https://e0.365dm.com/26/05/1600x900/skysports-ferrari-f1-charles-leclerc_7236367.jpg?20260501174614', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 7),
(91, 'Raducanu warms up for Rome by reuniting with US Open winning coach Richardson', 'Emma Raducanu is back working with Andrew Richardson, the coach she won her US Open title with in 2021 ahead of the Internazionali BNL d\'Italia in Rome; Watch the ATP and WTA Tours live on Sky Sports Tennis and Sky Sports+, streaming service NOW and the Sky Sports app Emma Raducanu has returned working with Andrew Richardson, the coach she won her US Open title with in 2021, as she looks set to begin her clay-court season at the Internazionali BNL d\'Italia in Rome. The British No 1 was heavily criticised for parting ways with Andrew Richardson following her incredible success in New York in 2021. And Raducanu\'s camp confirmed she spent time training last week in Spain with Richardson at the Ferrer Tennis Academy near Alicante, where he is based. The 23-year-old last played a match at Indian Wells when she won just two games in a 52-minute defeat to Amanda Anisimova. She also pulled out of the WTA Tour events in Miami and Linz as she prioritised her rehabilitation from post-viral symptoms on the back of an illness she picked up in Romania during early February. Raducanu - who also opted to sit out Great Britain\'s Billie Jean King Cup qualifier against Australia - and this week\'s Madrid Open as she continues to recover full fitness. Since splitting from her latest coach Francisco Roig in the wake of her second-round defeat at the Australian Open, she had been working on an informal basis with Mark Petchey. Since the split from Roig, Raducanu insisted she is happy working only with hitting partner Alexis Canter, a 27-year-old British former player who reached a career-high ranking of 779 last year. But now Raducanu has reportedly enlisted the help of the coach who famously guided her to the US Open title in New York, where she became the first qualifier to win a Grand Slam title, ahead of the WTA 1000 event in Rome which begins on Tuesday, May 5. Speaking to the Daily Mail in 2023, Richardson, who also coached Raducanu as a junior, revealed he had been keen to continue their short-term partnership after the US Open, but she chose to hire a more experienced tour coach in Torben Beltz. That proved to be one of a succession of brief coaching appointments Raducanu has made during her career. It was unclear whether she would make the Italian Open in Rome, which begins on Tuesday, but, having returned to training, Raducanu is hopeful of playing and will practise at the Foro Italico on Saturday. The news is a boost for British tennis, with Jack Draper missing the rest of the clay-court season because of a knee injury. Speaking in February, Sky Sports analyst Henman said Raducanu doesn\'t need a coach and should concentrate on working on her physicality to match the likes of fellow Grand Slam champions Aryna Sabalenka, Iga Swiatek, Elena Rybakina and Coco Gauff. \"I just wonder whether she\'s better off without a coach and that\'s nothing against Petch,\" said the four-time Wimbledon semi-finalist. \"He\'s someone I\'ve known for a long time and he\'s a very, very good coach but we know it\'s not going to be a full-time appointment because Petch has his broadcast commitments. \"Emma has talked about her identity, her game style and she wants to own it. She\'s been around long enough on the tour so I wonder whether that might be a good option for her but it\'s her prerogative. \"I worked with three coaches in 15 years. I like the consistency and continuity and we know that coaches don\'t last long working with Emma. \"An aggressive game style is how you have to play. You have got to be aggressive because if you don\'t your opponent will be and for me. I want to see her build her physicality: to get stronger, more resilient, to hit the ball harder. \"And I think if she does that, that\'ll mean that she has fewer interruptions and fewer setbacks physically. She\'ll be able to compete at a high level for longer periods, so if I could add one element it would be the physical side. \"Raducanu does work on her physical side. I think her tennis game is outstanding but when you think of the physicality of Sabalenka, Swiatek, Rybakina, Gauff, she\'s not in the same league. Petchey helped inspire the most productive period of Raducanu\'s season as she reached the quarter-finals at Queen\'s before running Sabalenka close in the third round of Wimbledon. Nigel Sears Best known for coaching former top five players Amanda Coetzer, Daniela Hantuchova, Anett Kontaveit and Ana Ivanovic, Sears joined her team in April 2021 and oversaw her incredible breakthrough run to the Wimbledon fourth round. Andrew Richardson Guided Raducanu to her historic Grand Slam title at the US Open as a qualifier. Raducanu opted not to extend his trial contract immediately after the victory. Torben Beltz Angelique Kerber\'s former coach lasted only five months. They split in April 2022 with Raducanu transitioning towards a new training model involving LTA coaching support. Dmitry Tursunov Raducanu took on the former pro on a trial basis during the summer of 2022 but Tursunov decided', 'https://www.skysports.com/tennis/news/12040/13538865/emma-raducanu-returns-to-us-open-winning-coach-andrew-richardson-ahead-of-internazionali-bnl-ditalia-in-rome', NULL, '2026-05-01 20:20:15', '2026-05-01 20:20:16', 'Football', 1, 3, 'en', 'https://e0.365dm.com/26/05/768x432/skysports-andrew-richardson_7236375.jpg?20260501175059', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 7),
(92, 'Kinsky reflects on CL nightmare and explains Spurs\' positivity in relegation battle', 'Antonin Kinsky reflects on his crucial save in the win at Wolves, learning from his Atletico Madrid errors, and how Roberto De Zerbi is helping Spurs take a positive approach to their relegation battle Watch the interview on Sky Sports News\' Premier League Friday from 5pm With Tottenham on the brink of a first Premier League win of 2026, Antonin Kinsky\'s 98th-minute, full-stretch dive to keep out what looked to be an inch-perfect Joao Gomes free-kick was pivotal to their victory at Wolves last weekend. With relegation rivals Nottingham Forest and West Ham also winning last weekend, Spurs didn\'t gain ground. But they did gain confidence and bolstered belief they have reached a turning point and can kick-on to overhaul their two-point gap to safety. A wonder-save? \"I\'m happy you say so,\" smiles Kinsky modestly, during an exclusive interview with Sky Sports. \"It was more also the weight of the moment. Everyone knows it\'s important, especially the last minute because then you don\'t have time to add another one.\" Follow Aston Villa vs Spurs with our live blog on the Sky Sports website and App for in-game updates and analysis plus FREE match highlights after full-time. On the value of the win, he says: \"It\'s very precious. If we wouldn\'t bring three points from there, of course, it would be much more difficult now. \"We are not closer but at least we didn\'t get further [away]. So the difference is still just two points.\" The belief within the Spurs squad that they can rescue themselves from this precarious situation with four games to go has been renewed. \"It\'s just positive,\" says Kinsky, when asked how he sees the relegation battle. \"I think if anyone from us would feel different, then there is no point of being within the squad. \"Where it all starts, it\'s here. And if you don\'t believe it, then you can\'t achieve it. So this is the most important thing. OK, do your best to be prepared but, first of all, you need to have the goal and believe it. Otherwise everything is pointless. That attitude has been strengthened by the arrival of new head coach Roberto De Zerbi. The charismatic Italian has had a quick impact on the pitch and across the group, lifting up Kinsky and his team-mates. \"By the way he speaks, what you read and what you hear from him is that he believes in us and that is a big message that he gives us overall: that the quality is there in the squad,\" says Kinsky. \"It\'s just not to speak about it but to show it. With the combination, with the style that he wants to play, I think our squad fits to that so I believe this is going to work. \"Now we have four points from three games, there is four left and I hope and I believe that this is the right way.\" Kinsky has a calm, focused and positive approach to Spurs\' situation. It is a mindset that also allowed him to overcome a major personal hurdle this season. Under former boss Igor Tudor, Kinsky endured a brutal Champions League debut at Atletico Madrid. There were two bad individual errors from the Czech goalkeeper and three goals conceded by the time he was hooked after just 17 minutes of the first leg of the last-16 tie. Kinsky had been a surprise selection ahead of regular No 1 Guglielmo Vicario, having appeared in just two Carabao Cup ties in the entire season before that match in March. While Kinsky admits there was plenty of self-reflection on his errors after the game, his performances this month, with Vicario sidelined by a hernia operation, have been notably impressive. He has put his nightmare in Madrid behind him to play an important role in Spurs\' run-in. \"It was a moment, debut in the Champions League, that I was dreaming of as a young boy. For me, this was the thing that I was going for. I was looking forward to it so much,\" says Kinsky. \"I have good people around me who always give me good feedback, what they really think about it and they are honest with me. So, I spoke to them a lot, I listened to them, then I compared it to my feelings and they were similar. \"So, upon me, it was just to keep going and make sure that when the next opportunity comes, I will be ready again.\" \"It\'s not like before I would feel weak, now I feel stronger because I made [that experience]. You make it because you are strong already and it makes you just stronger and it helps you just to grow. \"There is always so much things to improve, so it just shows you the things that you can get better at or mentally to adjust a little bit the approach towards the game.\" With time running out this season, Spurs must learn their lessons quickly. But the resilience of their goalkeeper Kinsky is a good inspiration for the challenges ahead, which will decide their Premier League status.', 'https://www.skysports.com/football/news/12040/13538547/spurs-antonin-kinsky-on-premier-league-relegation-battle-bouncing-back-from-champions-league-nightmare-and-his-super-save-at-wolves', NULL, '2026-05-01 20:20:15', '2026-05-01 20:20:16', 'Football', 1, 3, 'fr', 'https://e0.365dm.com/26/04/1600x900/skysports-antonin-kinsky-tottenham_7235455.jpg?20260430172741', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 7),
(93, 'How to watch Chelsea vs Nott\'m Forest at 3pm on Monday', 'Sky customers can watch Chelsea vs Nottingham Forest on Sky Sports from 2.30pm or via the Sky Sports app; non-Sky customers can stream the game with a NOW Day or Month pass; kick-off at Stamford Bridge is 3pm on Monday May 4 Chelsea host Nottingham Forest at Stamford Bridge in the Premier League on Monday May 4, live on Sky Sports. The Blues play their first league game since April 21 - the final game of Liam Rosenior\'s tenure - looking to end a run of five defeats in succession and climb back into European contention as a result. Depending on the results on Saturday and Sunday, in the best-case scenario for the west London club, a win could be enough to see them move up back up to sixth. Calum McFarlane is the man in charge in the interim, and started his second spell in charge this season with victory in last weekend\'s FA Cup semi-final against Leeds at Wembley. Meanwhile, Forest have boosted their survival hopes greatly over the last two months. Vitor Pereira\'s side are unbeaten since March 4 in the Premier League, having won three and drawn three of their last six games. They also have one foot in the Europa League final, having beaten Aston Villa 1-0 in the first leg at the City Ground. In the previous meeting between the two teams back in October, Josh Acheampong, Pedro Neto and Reece James scored in a 3-0 Chelsea win. Chelsea vs Nottingham Forest in the Premier League takes place on Monday May 4 at Stamford Bridge. Kick-off is 3pm UK and Ireland time. NOW is an instant streaming service offering access to all 12 Sky Sports channels, every Sky Sports+ stream, and much more. It\'s an app, so customers can sign up and stream instantly across over 60 devices. It offers contract-free memberships options, so customers can cancel anytime! Morgan Gibbs-White to score anytime at 100/30 with Sky Bet looks too big to ignore. The Forest playmaker is finishing the season like a man on a mission. Seven goals in his last seven Premier League appearances tells you everything you need to know about the level he\'s operating at right now. He\'s playing with freedom, conviction and, most importantly, end product - something that hasn\'t always been associated with his game. With an international summer on the horizon, Gibbs-White is making a very loud case to Thomas Tuchel for inclusion in England\'s World Cup squad. That kind of motivation can elevate a player\'s output and it\'s clear he\'s taking on more responsibility in the final third, getting into scoring positions and finding sublime quality at the right time. Reece James and Levi Colwill could return to Chelsea\'s squad for Monday\'s meeting with Nottingham Forest, interim head coach Calum McFarlane has revealed. Colwill has not played this season after suffering an anterior cruciate ligament injury on the first day of pre-season training, while James has been out since the middle of March with a hamstring problem, but both are now back in full training. Nottingham Forest will check on Murillo (hamstring), Dan Ndoye (knock), Jair Cunha (shoulder) and Ibrahim Sangare (undisclosed) ahead of kick-off, but Callum Hudson-Odoi (thigh) is definitely out. Tom from Southampton became a millionaire for free with Super 6! Could you be the next jackpot winner? Play for free!', 'https://www.skysports.com/football/news/12040/13538963/watch-spurs-vs-arsenal-tv-channel-live-stream-now-tv-team-news-and-score-prediction', NULL, '2026-05-01 20:20:15', '2026-05-01 20:20:16', 'Football', 1, 3, 'en', 'https://e0.365dm.com/26/05/1600x900/skysports-premier-league-how-to-watch_7236768.jpg?20260502121041', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 7),
(94, 'Klopp, Haaland, TAA plus many more pay homage to \'legend\' Salah', 'Liverpool forward Mo Salah watches on as players and managers dedicate video messages in homage to his legendary craft.', 'https://www.skysports.com/watch/video/13538970/mo-salah-watches-players-and-managers-pay-homage-to-his-legendary-craft', NULL, '2026-05-01 20:20:15', '2026-05-01 20:20:16', 'Autre', NULL, 2, 'en', 'https://e0.365dm.com/26/05/1600x900/skysports-football-salah_7236368.jpg?20260501174702', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 7),
(95, 'Fernandes chasing down De Bruyne and Henry record', 'Bruno Fernandes is chasing an assists record and the numbers show he is in a league of his own for creativity this season; Curtis Jones impressing in new role; watch Man Utd vs Liverpool live on Sky Sports from 2pm on Sunday; kick-off 3.30pm Welcome to The Radar, a Sky Sports column in which Nick Wright uses a blend of data and opinion to shed light on need-to-know stories from up and down the Premier League. This week: 🔴 Fernandes on assists mission🤔 Has Slot found a right-back solution?🔍 A player to watch this weekend Bruno Fernandes put himself on the brink of a Premier League record when he produced the assist for Benjamin Sesko\'s breakaway goal in Manchester United\'s 2-1 win over Brentford on Monday. He faces Liverpool on Super Sunday needing only one more to go level with Kevin De Bruyne for Manchester City in 2019/20 and Thierry Henry for Arsenal in 2002/03. With four games of the campaign still to play, he is well placed to beat their totals. Fernandes has been a creative force in the Premier League since his arrival at Old Trafford from Sporting in January 2020 but his current haul of 19 assists is by far his highest in a single season. Carry on at the same rate across Manchester United\'s remaining games of the campaign, with Sunderland, Nottingham Forest and Brighton to come after Liverpool, and he will finish on 22. The numbers reveal a gulf between Fernandes and the rest in this season\'s Premier League. The 31-year-old\'s total of 19 assists is nearly twice as high as anyone else\'s, with Manchester City\'s Rayan Cherki and West Ham\'s Jarrod Bowen next on 10. The gap is similarly wide for chances created, with Fernandes on 114, way ahead of the next players on the list, in Liverpool\'s Dominik Szoboszlai and Arsenal\'s Declan Rice, on 61. He is well clear at the top for Opta-defined big chances created too, on 28. His set-piece delivery has been a significant contributor to his success this season. Ten of his 19 assists have come from free-kicks and corners compared to only two and three of Henry and De Bruyne\'s record totals respectively. But it is worth noting that, in the context of this season in the Premier League, Fernandes ranks comfortably top for open-play chances created too, reflecting his completeness as a creator. Assists are of course dependent on the ability of a team-mate to finish but Fernandes also comes out top for expected assists, which gives a truer reflection of the quality of chances created. In fact, he has the highest xA of any player since his Premier League debut. Liverpool need no reminding of what he can do. It was his brilliant volleyed cross, using the instep of his right boot during the second phase of a corner, that allowed Harry Maguire to head in the winning goal when the two sides met at Anfield in October. Another contribution of that type on Sunday would equal a record that has stood for 23 years, and strengthen his claim to be considered this season\'s Premier League\'s Player of the Year. Curtis Jones might not be a long-term solution to Liverpool\'s right-back problem but he will hope to keep his place there at Old Trafford having impressed against Crystal Palace and Everton. The 25-year-old became the sixth Liverpool player to start in the role in the Premier League this season after Connor Bradley, Dominik Szoboszlai, Jeremie Frimpong, Joe Gomez and Wataru Endo when he was thrown in at Goodison Park. He has embraced the challenge. \"He has hardly played in that position in his career,\" said head coach Arne Slot. \"The way he does it is a big compliment.\" Jones has plenty to learn in the position as a natural midfielder but he has certainly added value in possession. Trent Alexander-Arnold was of course unique in terms of his creativity from right-back but Jones is similarly comfortable with the ball at his feet and showed the quality of his passing with the through-ball assist for Andrew Robertson\'s goal against Palace. That pass came from a midfield position following a counter-attack and was one of 149 across the two games, the most by any Liverpool player. His composure under pressure, and ability to step into central zones, has helped smooth out the side\'s issues in build-up. Virgil van Dijk has certainly noticed the difference. \"Curtis I thought was outstanding against Everton,\" he said this week. \"Especially in possession, he was quite a big game-changer.\" Bournemouth\'s Junior Kroupi faces Crystal Palace in the earlier game on Sunday having scored three goals in his last four games. He is sure to be in-demand this summer. Arsenal and Fulham go head to head in the Saturday Night Football game, with coverage starting on Sky Sports Premier League and Sky Sports Main Event from 5pm ahead of the 5.30pm kick-off. Bournemouth and Crystal Palace meet at 2pm on Sky Sports+ before the big one on Super Sunday as Man Utd and Liverpool meet at Old Trafford, kicking off at the earlier time of 3.30pm. On Monday, Chelsea take on Nottingham Forest at 3pm. Everton then meet', 'https://www.skysports.com/football/news/12040/13538856/bruno-fernandes-closing-in-on-kevin-de-bruyne-and-thierry-henrys-premier-league-assists-record-the-radar', NULL, '2026-05-01 20:20:15', '2026-05-01 20:20:16', 'Football', 1, 3, 'fr', 'https://e0.365dm.com/19/07/75x75/skysports-nick-wright-football_4713429.jpg?20190709112251', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 7),
(96, 'الأهلي يكتسح الزمالك بثلاثية في الدوري', 'حقق فريق الأهلي فوزا كبيرا على نظيره الزمالك بنتيجة 3 / 0، اليوم الجمعة، ضمن منافسات الجولة الخامسة من مرحلة التتويج في الدوري المصري الممتاز لكرة القدم. وسجل المغربي أشرف بن شرقي هدف التقدم في الدقيقة 18، بينما أضاف حسين الشحات الهدف الثاني في الدقيقة 32، وعاد بن شرقي ليختتم الثلاثية في الدقيقة 74. ورفع هذا الفوز رصيد الأهلي إلى 47 نقطة في المركز الثالث، أما الزمالك فلديه 50 نقطة يتساوى بها في صدارة الترتيب مع بيراميدز، لكن الزمالك يتفوق بفارق المواجهات المباشرة بينهما. ‫‫من شروط النشر : عدم الإساءة للكاتب أو للأشخاص أو للمقدسات أو مهاجمة الأديان أو الذات الإلهية، والابتعاد عن التحريض العنصري والشتائم‬.', 'https://www.hesport.com/%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%a3%d9%87%d9%84%d9%8a-%d9%8a%d9%83%d8%aa%d8%b3%d8%ad-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%b2%d9%85%d8%a7%d9%84%d9%83-%d8%a8%d8%ab%d9%84%d8%a7%d8%ab%d9%8a%d8%a9-%d9%81%d9%8a-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%af%d9%88%d8%b1-437106.html', NULL, '2026-05-01 19:07:46', '2026-05-01 20:20:16', 'Autre', NULL, 3, 'en', 'https://i1.hesport.com/wp-content/overlay/2026/05/IMG_5787.jpeg?v2', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 9),
(97, 'عقوبات مرتقبة في حق الجيش والرجاء بعد أحداث شغب مركب مولاي عبد الله', 'تتجه أنظار لجان العصبة الوطنية لكرة القدم الاحترافية نحو الحسم في ملف أحداث الشغب التي رافقت مباراة الجيش الملكي والرجاء الرياضي، التي جرت أطوارها أمس الخميس بمركب مولاي عبد الله بالرباط، في أفق اتخاذ قرارات تأديبية في حق الفريقين. وتقوم لجان العصبة الاحترافية، وفق ما كشفه مصدر مطلع لـ”هسبورت”، بدراسة تفاصيل ما وقع داخل الملعب خلال هذه المواجهة، التي عرفت سلوكات غير رياضية من طرف فئات محسوبة على جماهير الناديين، وهو ما أدى إلى خلق أجواء مشحونة أثرت على السير العادي للمباراة. ويرتقب، وفق المصدر ذاته، أن تفضي هذه المعطيات إلى إصدار عقوبات في حق كل من الجيش الملكي والرجاء الرياضي، في خطوة تروم تعزيز الانضباط داخل الملاعب والحد من تكرار مثل هذه الأحداث، خاصة في المباريات ذات الحساسية الجماهيرية. وفي سياق متصل، أمرت النيابة العامة بالرباط بوضع 136 شخصا تحت تدابير الحراسة النظرية، مع الاحتفاظ بحدثين اثنين، وذلك على خلفية هذه الأحداث، بعد تدخلات ميدانية باشرتها مصالح الأمن لتفريق التجمعات وضبط المتورطين. وكانت عناصر الأمن قد أوقفت عددا من المشجعين الذين تم تحديد هوياتهم عبر كاميرات المراقبة، بعدما ثبت تورطهم في أعمال تخلّ بالأمن والنظام داخل محيط الملعب. ‫‫من شروط النشر : عدم الإساءة للكاتب أو للأشخاص أو للمقدسات أو مهاجمة الأديان أو الذات الإلهية، والابتعاد عن التحريض العنصري والشتائم‬.', 'https://www.hesport.com/%d8%b9%d9%82%d9%88%d8%a8%d8%a7%d8%aa-%d9%85%d8%b1%d8%aa%d9%82%d8%a8%d8%a9-%d9%81%d9%8a-%d8%ad%d9%82-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%ac%d9%8a%d8%b4-%d8%a7%d9%84%d9%85%d9%84%d9%83%d9%8a-%d9%88%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%b1%d8%ac-437109.html', NULL, '2026-05-01 19:00:57', '2026-05-01 20:20:16', 'Autre', NULL, 3, 'en', 'https://i1.hesport.com/wp-content/overlay/2026/05/IMG_5520.jpeg?v2', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 9),
(98, 'الجيش يدين أحداث الشغب أمام الرجاء', 'أصدر نادي الجيش الملكي بلاغا رسميا، أعرب فيه عن إدانته الشديدة ورفضه القاطع، لكل السلوكيات غير الرياضية التي رافقت مباراته أمام الرجاء الرياضي، مؤكدا أن هذه التصرفات لا تعكس الصورة المشرفة التي تستحقها كرة القدم الوطنية وسمعة المغرب الرياضية. وأوضح البلاغ، أن المواجهة دارت في ملعب عالمي يليق بمكانة المملكة، وكان من المفترض أن تكون عرسا رياضيا يجسد الروح الرياضية، بين فريقين كبيرين يمتلكان قاعدة جماهيرية عريضة، غير أن أحداث الشغب التي شهدها اللقاء أفسدت هذا المشهد، وشكلت تهديدا لسلامة الجماهير وإساءة بالغة للكرة المغربية. وشددت إدارة النادي “العسكري” على تمسكها الراسخ بقيم التنافس الشريف، ونبذ العنف بكل أشكاله، داعية جميع الأطراف المعنية من سلطات وفاعلين رياضيين، إلى تضافر الجهود لضمان تنظيم المباريات في أجواء آمنة، تعكس الوجه الحضاري للبلاد في إفريقيا والعالم. وفي ختام البلاغ، وجه النادي نداء إلى جماهيره، للتحلي بروح المسؤولية والوعي، والالتزام بسلوك حضاري راق داخل المدرجات وخارجها، مؤكدا التزام الجيش الملكي، بمواصلة الانخراط في المبادرات التي تعزز الأمن والسلامة داخل الملاعب والحفاظ على القيم النبيلة للرياضة. ‫‫من شروط النشر : عدم الإساءة للكاتب أو للأشخاص أو للمقدسات أو مهاجمة الأديان أو الذات الإلهية، والابتعاد عن التحريض العنصري والشتائم‬.', 'https://www.hesport.com/%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%ac%d9%8a%d8%b4-%d9%8a%d8%af%d9%8a%d9%86-%d8%a3%d8%ad%d8%af%d8%a7%d8%ab-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%b4%d8%ba%d8%a8-%d8%a3%d9%85%d8%a7%d9%85-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%b1%d8%ac%d8%a7%d8%a1-437095.html', NULL, '2026-05-01 18:21:01', '2026-05-01 20:20:16', 'Autre', NULL, 3, 'en', 'https://i1.hesport.com/wp-content/overlay/2026/05/IMG_5779.jpeg?v2', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 9),
(99, 'بعد شغب الرباط. توجه لمنع تنقل الجماهير لمساندة أنديتها خارج الميدان', 'يتجه القرار داخل دوائر تدبير الشأن الكروي إلى منع تنقل الجماهير لمساندة أنديتها خارج الميدان، وذلك على خلفية الأحداث التي شهدتها محيطات بعض الملاعب خلال الفترة الأخيرة، وآخرها ما وقع بمركب مولاي عبد الله بالرباط يوم أمس الخميس، خلال مباراة فريقي الجيش الملكي وضيفه الرجاء الرياضي. ويأتي هذا التوجه، حسب ما كشفه مصدر مطلع لـ”هسبورت”، في سياق إعادة تقييم تجربة تنقل الجماهير التي عرفت خلال السنوات الماضية نوعا من الانفتاح، سمح بانتقال الأنصار بين مختلف المدن وأسهم في إنعاش المدرجات وإضفاء أجواء تنافسية على عدد من المباريات، غير أن هذه المكتسبات باتت اليوم محل مراجعة بسبب تكرار مظاهر الشغب في العديد من المباريات. وتطرح هذه المستجدات من جديد إشكالية الموازنة بين ضمان الأمن داخل الملاعب ومحيطها والحفاظ على أجواء الفرجة الكروية، في ظل استمرار تسجيل سلوكيات غير رياضية تؤثر على السير العادي للمنافسات وتثير قلق المتتبعين. وشهد مركب مولاي عبد الله بالرباط، مساء أمس الخميس، أحداث شغب وعنف بين جماهير الفريقين خلال المباراة التي جمعت الجيش الملكي بالرجاء الرياضي، برسم الجولة 17 من الدوري الاحترافي، وهو ما أعاد ملف تنقل الجماهير إلى واجهة النقاش، في انتظار ما ستسفر عنه القرارات المرتقبة في هذا الصدد. ‫‫من شروط النشر : عدم الإساءة للكاتب أو للأشخاص أو للمقدسات أو مهاجمة الأديان أو الذات الإلهية، والابتعاد عن التحريض العنصري والشتائم‬.', 'https://www.hesport.com/%d8%a8%d8%b9%d8%af-%d8%b4%d8%ba%d8%a8-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%b1%d8%a8%d8%a7%d8%b7-%d8%aa%d9%88%d8%ac%d9%87-%d9%84%d9%85%d9%86%d8%b9-%d8%aa%d9%86%d9%82%d9%84-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%ac%d9%85%d8%a7%d9%87%d9%8a%d8%b1-437099.html', NULL, '2026-05-01 17:30:55', '2026-05-01 20:20:16', 'Autre', NULL, 3, 'en', 'https://i1.hesport.com/wp-content/overlay/2026/05/IMG_5517.jpeg?v2', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 9),
(100, 'الشغب الكروي يودع 22 شخصا السجن', 'قرر وكيل الملك لدى المحكمة الزجرية بالدار البيضاء، إيداع 22 شخصا السجن، على خلفية أحداث الشغب التي عرفتها مباراة الوداد الرياضي واتحاد يعقوب المنصور يوم 29 أبريل. ‫‫من شروط النشر : عدم الإساءة للكاتب أو للأشخاص أو للمقدسات أو مهاجمة الأديان أو الذات الإلهية، والابتعاد عن التحريض العنصري والشتائم‬.', 'https://www.hesport.com/%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%b4%d8%ba%d8%a8-%d8%a7%d9%84%d9%83%d8%b1%d9%88%d9%8a-%d9%8a%d9%88%d8%af%d8%b9-22-%d8%b4%d8%ae%d8%b5%d8%a7-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%b3%d8%ac%d9%86-437092.html', NULL, '2026-05-01 17:26:13', '2026-05-01 20:20:16', 'Autre', NULL, 2, 'en', 'https://i1.hesport.com/wp-content/overlay/2026/05/IMG_5777.webp?v2', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 9),
(101, 'مواجهات ساخنة تشعل الجولة 18', 'تعود عجلة الدوري المغربي لكرة القدم للدوران بوتيرة متسارعة بعد يوم راحة واحد فقط من جولة منتصف الأسبوع، حيث تنطلق غدا السبت منافسات الجولة الجديدة التي تمتد حتى الاثنين القادم. وتأتي هذه الجولة في ظل جدولة زمنية مضغوطة تضع الأندية أمام اختبارات بدنية وذهنية شاقة، حيث تتصدر المشهد قمة كلاسيكية ساخنة بين مكناس وفاس، وصراع مرير في أسفل الترتيب. تقام مباراة واحدة غدا تجمع النادي المكناسي بجاره المغرب الفاسي في قمة محلية تحمل عبق الماضي تعيد للأذهان مواجهات تاريخية طبعت ثمانينيات القرن الماضي، حين كان الفريقان من أعمدة الكرة المغربية. ويتصدر المغرب الفاسي الترتيب برصيد 37 نقطة، ويدخل المواجهة منتشيا بمساره الإيجابي هذا الموسم، حيث تحول من فريق يعاني في وسط الترتيب إلى منافس فعلي على قمة الترتيب، مستفيدا من استقرار فني وتجانس واضح في خطوطه. في المقابل، يخوض النادي المكناسي، صاحب المركز السابع، المباراة تحت ضغط النتائج، إذ يسعى لتأمين بقائه بين الكبار بعد عودة صعبة من أقسام الهواة معولا على عامل الأرض لحسم المواجهة مع جاره. وسيكون الوداد الرياضي، صاحب المركز الرابع بـ31 نقطة، في مهمة استعادة الهوية بقيادة مدربه المؤقت ولاعبه السابق محمد بن شريفة، الذي تسلم المهمة خلفا للمقال باتريس كارتيرون، وذلك حينما يواجه مضيفه نهضة الزمامرة، صاحب المركز الحادي عشر بـ16 نقطة، بعد غد الأحد. وفشل كارتيرون في تحقيق الإقلاع المطلوب، حيث حصل على نقطتين فقط في خمس مباريات، ليشكل ضربة قوية لآمال الوداد في المنافسة على القمة هذا الموسم. أما نهضة الزمامرة، فيدخل المواجهة مثقلا بهزيمتين متتاليتين زجتا به في حسابات النزول، مما يفرض عليه البحث عن نتيجة إيجابية بأي ثمن نظرا لكون خمس نقاط الفاصلة عن المركز الأخير تجعله في وضع تهديد دائم. وفي الدار البيضاء، يسعى الرجاء البيضاوي، صاحب المركز الثالث بـ33 نقطة، لاستعادة توازنه حين يستضيف الدفاع الحسني الجديدي، الذي يتواجد في المركز السادس بـ27 نقطة. الرجاء، الذي تلقى ضربة معنوية بعد خسارته في قمة الجولة الماضية، يجد نفسه مطالبا برد فعل سريع للحفاظ على حظوظه في سباق اللقب، غير أن الدفاع الجديدي، الذي حقق انتصارين متتاليين مكناه من التقدم في الترتيب، يراهن على صلابته الدفاعية وخبرته في إرباك أندية الدار البيضاء، مما يجعل المواجهة تكتيكية بامتياز. وفي العاصمة الرباط، يحتضن ديربي رباطي خاص مواجهة اتحاد تواركة والفتح الرباطي، في مباراة تغلب عليها الحسابات أكثر من الجانب الفني. اتحاد تواركة، صاحب المركز الرابع عشر، الذي حقق أول فوز له في الموسم خلال الجولة الماضية، يسعى للبناء على هذه النتيجة للهروب من منطقة الخطر. من جانبه، يدخل الفتح، صاحب المركز الثامن، اللقاء بمعنويات مرتفعة بعد سلسلة نتائج إيجابية (أربعة انتصارات في آخر خمس مباريات)، أعادت له توازنه وجعلته قريبا من تأمين موقع مريح في وسط الترتيب. وفي طنجة، يصطدم اتحاد طنجة، الذي يحتل المركز العاشر بـ17 نقطة، بطموح الجيش الملكي، صاحب المركز الثاني بـ35 نقطة، في واحدة من أبرز مباريات الجولة، بعد غد. الفريق الطنجاوي كسر سلسلة نتائجه السلبية بفوز مهم في الجولة الماضية في قلب مدينة أسفي، لكنه لا يزال في وضعية حرجة تتطلب الاستمرارية. أما الجيش الملكي، فيعيش فترة زاهية، خاصة بعد فوزه في قمة الرجاء، معززا حظوظه في مواصلة الضغط على المتصدر، ويرحل إلى الشمال بحثا عن فوزه العاشر هذا الموسم. وتتواصل المباريات يوم الاثنين القادم بمواجهة ساخنة بين حسنية أغادير صاحب المركز الثالث عشر، وأولمبيك آسفي، الذي يقبع في المركز قبل الأخير، في صراع مباشر لتفادي مراكز الهبوط. ويعيش الفريقان موسما صعبا، ما يجعل هذه المباراة بمثابة ست نقاط أكثر منها ثلاث، حيث قد تحدد نتيجتها ملامح البقاء في الجولات المقبلة. وفي مباراة أخرى، يواجه اتحاد يعقوب المنصور (متذيل الترتيب) اختبارا صعبا أمام نهضة بركان، صاحب المركز الخامس برصيد 30 نقطة. ويخوض اتحاد يعقوب المنصور المواجهة منتشيا بفوز ثمين على الوداد خارج الديار، في حين يسعى نهضة بركان (حامل اللقب)، للخروج من فترة فراغ أثرت على نتائجه وأبعدته نسبيا عن الصدارة، مما يضعه أمام ضرورة استعادة نجاعة الأداء. وتختتم الجولة بمباراة لا تقل أهمية بين الكوكب المراكشي، الذي يحتل المركز التاسع، وأولمبيك الدشيرة، صاحب المركز الثاني عشر حيث يفرض هاجس البقاء نفسه بقوة. أولمبيك الدشيرة يدخل اللقاء في وضعية صعبة بعد أربع هزائم متتالية، بينما يظهر الكوكب المراكشي تماسكا نسبيا في الجولات الأخيرة توج بفوز مهم في رحلته الطويلة إلى بركان، منحه أفضلية نفسية مهمة قبل هذه المواجهة الحاسمة. الجولة تبدو مفتوحة على سيناريوهات متعددة، حيث يتقاطع صراع القمة مع معركة البقاء، في وقت قد تعيد فيه بعض النتائج ترتيب موازين القوى سواء في مقدمة الترتيب أو أسفله، مع اقتراب الموسم من مراحله الحاسمة. ‫‫من شروط النشر : عدم الإساءة للكاتب أو للأشخاص أو للمقدسات أو مهاجمة الأديان أو الذات الإلهية، والابتعاد عن التحريض العنصري والشتائم‬.', 'https://www.hesport.com/%d9%85%d9%88%d8%a7%d8%ac%d9%87%d8%a7%d8%aa-%d8%b3%d8%a7%d8%ae%d9%86%d8%a9-%d8%aa%d8%b4%d8%b9%d9%84-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%ac%d9%88%d9%84%d8%a9-18-437033.html', NULL, '2026-05-01 17:14:11', '2026-05-01 20:20:16', 'Autre', NULL, 3, 'en', 'https://i1.hesport.com/wp-content/overlay/2026/04/IMG-20260426-WA0005.jpg?v2', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 9),
(102, 'Celtics, 76ers will add to their long playoff history with a Game 7 matchup in Boston', 'Boston Celtics’ Jayson Tatum, left, tries to get past Philadelphia 76ers’ Paul George during the first half of Game 6 in a first-round NBA basketball playoff series Thursday, April 30, 2026, in Philadelphia. (AP Photo/Matt Slocum) BOSTON (AP) — The Celtics appeared to be skipping toward the second round of the NBA playoffs following a 32-point road win in Game 4 at Philadelphia. But back-to-back convincing wins by the 76ers in Game 5 and Game 6 have left a Boston team that once looked like a favorite to emerge from the Eastern Conference on the brink of an epic collapse. A loss in Saturday’s Game 7 would be the No. 2 seed Celtics’ earliest exit from the playoffs since the 2020-21 season. They may have to do it with star Jayson Tatum dealing with a new ailment after he briefly left Game 6 in the third quarter for unspecified treatment to an apparent left calf injury. Tatum, of course, is just 22 games into his return from the torn right Achilles tendon injury he suffered in last season’s playoffs. The Celtics downplayed the current situation, with Tatum saying afterward that his leg was only feeling “a little stiff.” He said following a quick assessment and some time on the exercise bike he didn’t return because the game was out of hand and the starters had already been pulled. The recent history for winner-takes-all games for Philadelphia teams isn’t exactly on the 76ers side, though. The Flyers’ return to the NHL playoffs served as a reminder they are the last Philadelphia sports team to win a Game 7, beating, yes, Boston, in the 2010 Eastern Conference semifinal. Since then, the 76ers in 2012, 2019, 2021 and 2023 have all lost Game 7s; the Flyers lost one in 2014 and 2020; and the Phillies lost Game 7 of the NLCS in 2023. The Celtics have long had the Sixers’ number in the playoffs, winning the last six series. The 76ers last eliminated the Celtics in the 1982 Eastern Conference semis. “I’ve been playing these guys for so long,” 76ers star Joel Embiid said. “I’m tired of losing to them. We have a chance to accomplish something special.” What to Know: The Celtics are 27-10 all-time in Game 7s, the 76ers are 6-12 in such games and are 0-4 in them since 2001. It’ll be the ninth Game 7 between these two franchises, with Boston going 6-2 in the previous ones. Philadelphia is the 37th team in league history to force a Game 7 after trailing 3-1. Only 13 teams have overcome that deficit and won the series. If Boston is going to prevent the 76ers from becoming the 14th, its shooting must improve. The 76ers have held the NBA’s No. 2 rated offense during the regular season to under 100 points per game in back-to-back games. The Celtics also combined to shoot just 30.5% (22/72) from 3-point range, with 11 makes in each of those games. They led the league in the regular season, averaging 16 3s per game.', 'https://apnews.com/article/nba-playoffs-76ers-celtics-5af49866fe280835885a5c65b875dfd1', NULL, '2026-05-01 19:07:15', '2026-05-01 20:33:51', 'Football', 1, 3, 'en', 'https://dims.apnews.com/dims4/default/4465387/2147483647/strip/true/crop/3618x2412+0+0/resize/599x399!/quality/90/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fassets.apnews.com%2F9c%2Fdb%2F17a2b7b7932cf70b357365fa45f9%2F3d2b854e436a440b811eef1404ed59b4', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 2);
INSERT INTO `articles` (`id`, `title`, `content`, `url`, `author`, `published_at`, `collected_at`, `sport_category`, `sport_id`, `importance_score`, `langue`, `image_url`, `nb_mots`, `status`, `sentiment`, `metadata`, `source_id`) VALUES
(103, 'The NHL playoffs feature a bunch of new blood in the second round, from Philadelphia to Anaheim', 'Anaheim Ducks center Leo Carlsson, left, celebrates his empty net goal with left wing Chris Kreider during the third period of Game 6 in the first round of the NHL hockey Stanley Cup playoffs series against the Edmonton Oilers, Thursday, April 30, 2026, in Anaheim, Calif. (AP Photo/Mark J. Terrill) Philadelphia Flyers’ Dan Vladar reacts after the Flyers won Game 6 against the Pittsburgh Penguins in the first round of the NHL hockey Stanley Cup playoffs series Wednesday, April 29, 2026, in Philadelphia. (AP Photo/Matt Slocum) Minnesota Wild players celebrate after wining Game 6 in the first round of the NHL hockey Stanley Cup playoff series against the Dallas Stars, Thursday, April 30, 2026, in St. Paul, Minn. (AP Photo/Bailey Hillesheim) Colorado Avalanche’s Devon Toews (7) celebrates his goal with Nathan MacKinnon (29) and Martin Necas (88) against the Los Angeles Kings during the third period of Game 4 in the first round of an NHL hockey Stanley Cup playoff series Sunday, April 26, 2026, in Los Angeles. (AP Photo/Scott Strazzante) The Stanley Cup Playoffs are full of new blood, and so far three teams have advanced to the second round after not even making the postseason last year. Colorado, Minnesota, Philadelphia and Anaheim have advaanced from the first round, with the Flyers (six years) and the Ducks (eight) enjoying their first playoff trips in a long while. The Avalanche and Wild, who will face each other, each lost in the first round a year ago. More newcomers are on the way, too: Whoever wins the Boston-Buffalo and Montreal-Tampa Bay series didn’t make the second round last year either. The Sabres ended the longest drought in NHL history at 14 seasons and the Bruins are back after a one-year blip, while the Canadiens and Lightning each had first-round exits in 2025. Incredibly, the second round could see seven out of eight new teams this season if Utah rallies to defeat Vegas. Carolina, which will host the Flyers in Game 1 on Saturday, made it that far a year ago. “That’s the exciting part of where the league is at and where these teams are at,” Hall of Fame defenseman Chris Pronger said recently. “New teams (are) getting into the playoffs and showcasing some of these young players that are on the rise that maybe haven’t had that experience. And now they get a chance to kind of understand what it’s all about and what it means to play in the playoffs.” A new Cup winner was guaranteed last month when back-to-back champion Florida was eliminated from contention late in a season derailed by injuries. There will now be two new finalists after Edmonton got knocked out in the first round by the Ducks. Oilers captain Connor McDavid said they “were an average team all year” and did not live up to high expectations. The Hurricanes, who have advanced in each of the past eight years since Rod Brind’Amour took over as coach in 2018, host one of the upstart teams in the field: Philadelphia last reached the playoffs during 2020 pandemic. “There was never a doubt,” said Flyers goaltender Dan Vladar, who had a 42-save shutout in the Game 6 overtime victory against Pittsburgh. “Good things happen to good people, and we are good people here.” In the West, the Presidents’ Trophy-winning Avalanche have been waiting around since sweeping Los Angeles. In the playoffs for a ninth year in a row, they next face the Wild, who beat Dallas in a six-game showdown of Central Division powerhouses. “It’s going to be a hard-fought series,” Colorado captain Gabriel Landeskog said. “High-quality teams, high-quality players, good goaltending and special teams. It’s going to be a battle.” Minnesota finally won its opening series after losing its past eight, reaching the second round for the first time since 2015. Rookie goalie Jesper Wallstedt noticed a fan crying in the stands during the clinching Game 6 win, and it made him realize how much it meant beyond the locker room. “There’s so many more people who are with us on this road and this journey,” Wallstedt said. “The excitement and joy to get past the first round is huge.” The Ducks in coach Joel Quenneville’s debut season advanced for the first time since a run to the Western Conference Final in 2017. “Now we’ve got a taste of playoff hockey,” Quenneville said. “I think we can feel at this moment that it’s so much fun playing games that have the meaning and the building being as loud and excited as it is. It seems to grow from this level on.” AP Sports Writers Dan Gelston in Philadelphia, Dave Campbell in St. Paul, Minnesota, Greg Beacham in Anaheim, California, and Pat Graham in Denver contributed.', 'https://apnews.com/article/nhl-playoffs-second-round-4e64e20793d44e6faf03edfd9f29dfb6', NULL, '2026-05-01 19:25:08', '2026-05-01 20:33:51', 'Football', 1, 3, 'en', 'https://dims.apnews.com/dims4/default/41d4746/2147483647/strip/true/crop/5744x3827+0+1/resize/980x653!/quality/90/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fassets.apnews.com%2Fe1%2F13%2Fa30ce48f44f9bd9432282e903e1a%2F458ec981c5064f1d9cb6af3d1b5043ce', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 2),
(104, 'PSG: le troisième gardien Renato Marin pourrait jouer face à Lorient ce samedi', 'Verra-t-on une nouvelle tête dans les buts du PSG ce samedi, lors de la réception de Lorient (17h au Parc des Princes)? Selon les informations du Parisien, confirmées par RMC Sport, Renato Marin pourrait faire ses grands débuts en Ligue 1 pour la 32e journée de Ligue 1. Aligné à une seule reprise cette saison, face à Fontenay en 32e de finale de la Coupe de France, le gardien de 19 ans pourrait profiter de la blessure de Lucas Chevalier pour garder les cages parisiennes face aux Merlus, Matvey Safonov pouvant être préservé à quatre jours de la demi-finale retour de Ligue des champions face au Bayern Munich. Ce vendredi en conférence de presse, Luis Enrique n\'a rien voulu confirmer à propos de l\'identité du titulaire. \"J’ai tout fait avec les gardiens. Au Barça B chacun a joué sept matchs et j’ai choisi, je suis ouvert aux changements dans le foot. Le monde a changé, c’est une position différente mais je suis ouvert à changé les choses. Il faut attendre demain (samedi) pour le gardien. On arrive à la fin de la saison. Je ne veux donner aucune information. Toutes les options que vous dites sont possibles. Il faut valoriser, juger ça, parler aux joueurs. C’est un peu tétris car on a besoin de gagner trois points\", a expliqué le technicien espagnol. La réception de Lorient - coincée entre la double confrontation face au Bayern en Ligue des champions - intervient alors que Paris n\'est pas encore mathématiquement assuré d\'un 14e titre en Ligue 1. Le PSG n\'a pas encore totalement distancé Lens, six points derrière lui avant le choc entre les deux équipes le 13 mai à Bollaert. Mais comme face à Angers le week-end dernier, Luis Enrique pourrait être tenté de faire tourner son effectif tout en s\'évitant un revers qui relancerait la course au titre et ferait mal à la tête et à la confiance avant le voyage en Bavière, où le club de la capitale cherchera à valider une qualification pour une deuxième finale européenne de rang, huit jours après une demi-finale aller légendaire saluée par le monde du football. \"Il ne fait rien d’autre, il n’est concentré que sur ça\": comment Ciryl Gane prépare depuis Paris son combat contre Alex Pereira, à deux mois de l\'UFC Maison-Blanche', 'https://rmcsport.bfmtv.com/football/clubs/paris-saint-germain/psg-le-troisieme-gardien-renato-marin-pourrait-jouer-face-a-lorient-ce-samedi_AV-202605010692.html', NULL, '2026-05-01 20:51:44', '2026-05-01 20:51:44', 'Football', 1, 55, 'fr', 'https://images.bfmtv.com/etHPqL3EBl_bDYwl0IXDF992f48=/0x106:2048x1258/images/Renato-Marin-a-l-echauffement-en-fevrier-2026-2279518.jpg', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 6),
(105, 'Arsenal opens up 6-point lead in Premier League title race to pile pressure on Man City', 'Arsenal’s Viktor Gyoekeres celebrates after scoring his side’s opening goal during the English Premier League soccer match between Arsenal and Fulham in London, England, Saturday, May 2, 2026. (AP Photo/Kin Cheung) Arsenal’s Bukayo Saka celebrates after scoring his side’s second goal during the English Premier League soccer match between Arsenal and Fulham in London, England, Saturday, May 2, 2026. (AP Photo/Kin Cheung) Arsenal’s Bukayo Saka celebrates with teammates after scoring his side’s second goal during the English Premier League soccer match between Arsenal and Fulham in London, England, Saturday, May 2, 2026. (AP Photo/Kin Cheung) Brentford’s Igor Thiago scores his sides second goal from the penalty spot during their English Premier League soccer match against West Ham in London, Saturday, May 2, 2026. (John Walton/PA via AP) Sunderland’s Daniel Ballard pulls the hair of Wolverhampton Wanderers’ Tolu Arokodare resulting in a red card during their English Premier League soccer match in Wolverhampton, England, Saturday, May 2, 2026. (Mike Egerton/PA via AP) In one of its most dominant performances for weeks, Arsenal overpowered Fulham in a 3-0 win on Saturday that transferred the title-race pressure to second-place City. All of the goals came in the first half, with Viktor Gyokeres scoring twice and setting up the other for Bukayo Saka. City has two games in hand, the first coming at Everton on Monday. Significantly, Arsenal now has a superior goal difference of 4 compared to City in a title fight that could yet come down to that tiebreaker if both teams win all of their remaining matches. Arsenal has three left — West Ham away, Burnley at home and Crystal Palace away — in an easier run-in on paper than City’s. It was only 10 days ago that City ended Arsenal’s 200-day stay at the top of the league to become, for many, the title favorite. Pep Guardiola’s team hasn’t played in the league since and the momentum might just have swung Arsenal’s way after its wins over Newcastle last weekend and now a Fulham team which arrived at Emirates Stadium with aspirations of qualifying for a European competition. Saka, making his first start in six weeks after an Achilles injury, set up Gyokeres for a ninth-minute tap-in before the roles were reversed in the 40th. Gyokeres held up the ball and slipped in Saka, who drove home a finish inside the near post. Gyokeres grabbed his second goal — and 21st of the season in all competitions — by heading home Leandro Trossard’s cross in first-half stoppage time. West Ham’s survival bid was damaged by a 3-0 loss at Brentford, for whom Brazil striker Igor Thiago — with a penalty for his 22nd goal of the season — was among the scorers. It meant West Ham stayed two points above Tottenham, which is in third-to-last place — the final relegation spot. Spurs, who played in the Champions League this season and have been in the top flight since the late 1970s, visit Aston Villa on Sunday and then there are three more rounds remaining. Brentford climbed to sixth place, seven points behind fifth-place Aston Villa. The top five qualify automatically for the Champions League. Newcastle eased some of the pressure on manager Eddie Howe by beating Brighton 3-1 to end a four-match losing run in the league. “It’s been hard for my family because they see the intimate side of me behind closed doors,” Howe said. “I haven’t been a bundle of joy the past few weeks.” William Osula and Dan Burn were Newcastle’s scorers in the first half before Jack Hinshelwood replied for Brighton after the break. Harvey Barnes scored Newcastle’s third in stoppage time. There have been three red cards for hair-pulling in the Premier League this season. Twice, the recipient of the pull has been Tolu Arokodare. The Wolverhampton striker had his hair tugged by Sunderland defender Dan Ballard, resulting in another sending-off for an infringement that has become an increasingly common sight in soccer over the past year. Sunderland was leading 1-0 at the time through Nordi Mukiele’s header at a corner. Santiago Bueno equalized for already-relegated Wolverhampton, the league’s last-place club, and it finished 1-1.', 'https://apnews.com/article/arsenal-fulham-premier-league-title-west-ham-ballard-514a8ca259c4c62fefe5f972321ee926', NULL, '2026-05-02 16:11:33', '2026-05-02 20:43:55', 'Football', 1, 30, 'en', 'https://dims.apnews.com/dims4/default/81b5ea7/2147483647/strip/true/crop/1733x1155+0+0/resize/980x653!/quality/90/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fassets.apnews.com%2F1a%2F64%2F02e721479e69e851800a853ea6a4%2Fb2b2868597ef41db95ec2fb502703167', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 2),
(106, 'Ryan Reynolds \'gutted\' as Wrexham misses out on playoffs to put Premier League dream on hold', 'Wrexham’s Josh Windass reacts at the end of the EFL Championship soccer match between Wrexham and Middlesbrough, in Wrexham, Wales, Saturday May 2, 2026. (Cody Froggatt/PA via AP) Wrexham manager Phil Parkinson applauds the fans following the EFL Championship soccer match between Wrexham and Middlesbrough, in Wrexham, Wales, Saturday May 2, 2026. (Cody Froggatt/PA via AP) Wrexham’s Josh Windass, second left, celebrates scoring his side’s first goal of the game with teammates, during the EFL Championship soccer match between Wrexham and Middlesbrough, in Wrexham, Wales, Saturday May 2, 2026. (Cody Froggatt/PA via AP) Wrexham’s Josh Windass, left, scores their side’s first goal of the game during the EFL Championship soccer match between Wrexham and Middlesbrough, in Wrexham, Wales, Saturday May 2, 2026. (Cody Froggatt/PA via AP) Middlesbrough’s Tommy Conway, left, celebrates scoring the opening goal during the EFL Championship soccer match between Wrexham and Middlesbrough, in Wrexham, Wales, Saturday May 2, 2026. (Peter Byrne/PA via AP) “I am completely gutted by today’s result but incredibly proud of our season,” the actor wrote on X after the Welsh club he co-owns missed out on a place in the playoffs in the second-tier Championship by drawing 2-2 with Middlesbrough in a dramatic final round of the regular season on Saturday. That allowed Hull to jump ahead of Wrexham and into sixth place — the fourth and final spot in the playoffs — courtesy of a 2-1 win over Norwich in a match played at the same time. The winning goal for Hull, by Oli McBurnie in the 67th, appeared to be scored from an offside position but there are no video reviews in the English Football League. It ended Wrexham’s unprecedented run of three straight promotions under its famous owners — a streak that began by getting out of the fifth tier in the 2022-23 season and has been documented in the globally popular, Emmy Award-winning “Welcome to Wrexham” series. Still, seventh place marked the Wrexham’s highest finish in its history, bettering the 15th position it achieved in the second tier in the 1978–79 season. “We’ve come a long way in five years and this was the best result in our 150+ year history,” Reynolds wrote alongside a graphic that showed how Wrexham has risen from the National League. “More to do. But for now, we have so much to be proud of, Reds.” Elsewhere, Ipswich secured the second automatic promotion spot behind champion Coventry — and an immediate return to the Premier League — by beating Queens Park Rangers 3-0. Ipswich is owned by U.S. investment group Gamechanger 20 Limited and counts pop star Ed Sheeran as a minority shareholder. Joining Hull in the playoffs, which begin next week and are over two legs, are Millwall, Southampton and Middlesbrough. However, the short-term pain was acute, and Wrexham’s players sat on the ground and looked disconsolate after the final whistle — even though the Hull-Norwich match hadn’t finished. Wrexham started the day in sixth place, ahead of Hull on goal difference, and conceded in the fourth minute to Middlesbrough, only to score through Josh Windass and Sam Smith for a 2-1 lead by the 41st. Middlesbrough hit back immediately with a 43rd-minute equalizer but Wrexham finished the stronger, squandering a string of great late chances for a winner that would have secured a playoff place on goal difference. “This squad as it stands, with a preseason together, will be even stronger next year,” said Wrexham manager Phil Parkinson, who oversaw a summer spend of around $40 million last year. “Of course we’ll always look to add to that to try and give ourselves an even better chance ... we know where we’d like to strengthen and what we need to improve on. We’ll do that and we’ll make this squad as strong as we possibly can to mount a challenge next year.”', 'https://apnews.com/article/wrexham-championship-final-day-ipswich-01de8412e449a1e4f5184cc4e720e990', NULL, '2026-05-02 13:38:24', '2026-05-02 20:43:55', 'Hockey', NULL, 30, 'en', 'https://dims.apnews.com/dims4/default/590da88/2147483647/strip/true/crop/750x750+0+469/resize/60x60!/quality/90/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fassets.apnews.com%2F7b%2Fb0%2Fbb1aaaed4a98a31fffb224b98066%2Fsteve-douglas-photo-2024-steve-douglas.png', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 2),
(107, 'Kentucky Derby is down to 19 horses after The Puma gets scratched', 'Kentucky Derby entrant The Puma works out at Churchill Downs Friday, May 1, 2026, in Louisville, Ky. (AP Photo/Charlie Riedel) A horse heads to the track for a workout at Churchill Downs Friday, May 1, 2026, in Louisville, Ky. (AP Photo/Charlie Riedel) LOUISVILLE, Ky. (AP) — The Puma has been scratched from the Kentucky Derby, so the 152nd edition of the race will be run Saturday with 19 horses instead of the maximum 20. Churchill Downs officials announced The Puma was out because of a swollen leg from a skin infection. He was ruled out less than 12 hours before the 6:57 p.m. EDT post time, past the deadline for Corona de Oro to draw into the field off the also-eligible list. The horse trained by Gustavo Delgado Sr. and son Gustavo Delgado Jr. opened at odds of 10-1 and was bet down to 8-1 by Friday. “It’s incredibly disappointing, but the swelling should go down within a day or two,” Delgado Jr. said. “It’s just really bad timing.” The father-son training duo was looking to win its second Derby after doing so with Mage in 2023. Another father-son duo, Bill and Riley Mott, is the first to each have a horse in the race since 1964. The Puma is the fourth scratch from the field this week, with one coming each of the past four days. Silent Tactic was ruled out Wednesday, Fulleffort on Thursday and Right to Party on Friday, with Great White, Ocelli and Robusta getting in. Renegade remains the favorite after opening as such on the morning line a week ago. The Todd Pletcher-trained colt would be the first to win the Derby out of the inside No. 1 post position in four decades.', 'https://apnews.com/article/kentucky-derby-winner-14da4af938ae3a3201f4d17a80d052c0', NULL, '2026-05-02 13:48:07', '2026-05-02 20:43:55', 'Équitation', NULL, 15, 'en', 'https://dims.apnews.com/dims4/default/3ace8ac/2147483647/strip/true/crop/2316x2316+0+0/resize/60x60!/quality/90/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fassets.apnews.com%2Fd6%2F06%2F559e97cd425999c3ef10259051ff%2Fwhynomug-stephen-whyno.jpeg', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 2),
(108, 'DIRECT. Nice-Lens: les Sang et Or démarrent bien, le Gym peut valider son maintien', 'Il prend d\'abord le ballon mais ensuite il y a un vrai contact avec Mendy. Les Niçois réclament un deuxième jaune pour Sarr, l\'arbitre tente d\'apaiser. Il était en train de reculer mais il réussit à cadrer. Diouf s\'en saisit assez facilement malgré tout. Avertissement largement évitable pour le défenseur lensois, venu garder le ballon dans ses mains alors qu\'il était pour les Niçois. L\'appel de Thomasson était excellent, le centre ausis mais Bard est le plus prompt pour depousser le danger. L\'arbitre signale un hors-jeu, mais ce n\'était pas du tout le cas. Le but aurait été accepté si Udol était parvenu à conclure. Il avait sans doute mieux à faire en servant un partenaire, mais le meneur niçois décide d\'y aller seul et se heurte à la défense. SUR UNE TETE DE JUMA BAH ! Le gardien lensois détourne en corner, de nouveau, pour le Gym. Super arrêt de Risser, Bah était complètement seul. Même si Lens a déjà eu deux grosses occasions, Nice se projette aussi et réussit à approcher rapidement la surface des Sang et Or. C\'est un début de match intéressant. Boudache lance bien son attaquant. Ganiou se fait éliminer avec un contre favorable. Cho réussit à frapper mais Baidoo contre et met en corner. Sur le corner lensois, le défenseur réclame un pénalty. Il a pris un bras dans le visage, mais pas assez pour siffler d\'après l\'arbitre. Premier corner du match pour Lens, après un redoublement de passes et une frappe contrée de Sangaré. Lens attaque fort dans cette rencontre. Premier avertissement pour Nice ! Sur une attaque placée, Edouard reçoit le ballon dans la surface. Il frappe en pivot, c\'est dévié et tout proche de tromper Diouf, qui se reprend in extremis pour sauver juste devant sa ligne. Le coup d\'envoi est donné par le RC Lens, face à des Niçois en quête de points pour valider leur maintien. Lens: Risser – Ganiou, Baidoo, Sarr – Abdulhamid, Thomasson, Sangaré, Udol – Thauvin, Saint-Maximin – Edouard. Même si la demi-finale de Coupe de France contre Toulouse a été très réussie, Lens n\'a gagné qu\'un seul de ses trois derniers matchs de Ligue 1, battu contre Lille et concédant le nul face à Brest. Les hommes de Pierre Sage doivent donc relancer la machine ce soir. La dernière victoire du Gym en Ligue 1 devant son public remonte au mois... d\'octobre. C\'était à l\'époque contre le LOSC. Après le nul du PSG contre Lorien ce samedi, les Sang et Or peuvent encore rêver du titre. S\'ils remportent tous leurs matchs jusqu\'à la fin de saison, y compris le choc face aux Parisiens à Bollaert, et que Paris trébuche face à Brest ou au PFC, alors les Lensois seront champions. La composition de Lens: Risser – Ganiou, Baidoo, Sarr – Abdulhamid, Thomasson, Sangaré, Udol – Thauvin, Saint-Maximin – Edouard Pas de Clauss ni de Kevin Carlos. Boudache est titulaire malgré la visite médicale lundi passée à Lyon. La composition de Nice: Diouf - Mendy, Bah, Oppong - Louchet, Boudaoui, Sanson (c), Bard - Boudache, Cho, Diop. Un avant-goût de finale. Avant de s\'affronter en finale de Coupe de France le 22 mai prochain, l\'OGC Nice accueille le RC Lens pour la 32e journée de Ligue 1.', 'https://rmcsport.bfmtv.com/football/ligue-1/direct-nice-lens-suivez-le-match-de-la-32e-journee-de-ligue-1-en-live-repetition-avant-la-finale-de-la-coupe-de-france_LS-202605020273.html', NULL, '2026-05-02 20:43:55', '2026-05-02 20:43:55', 'Football', 1, 65, 'fr', 'https://images.bfmtv.com/DwvMB7JUg_RB0qM1A6EEYsefY38=/0x212:2048x1364/images/Saud-Abdulhamid-et-Ismaelo-Ganiou-avec-Lens-2-mai-2026-2279758.jpg', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 6),
(109, 'DIRECT. Metz-Monaco: les Messins sont relégués, les Monégasques restent en course pour le podium', 'C\'est la fin de cette rencontre! Monaco s\'impose sur la pelouse de Metz (1-2), avec un but du milieu de terrain français Jessy Deminguet (49e) d\'un côté, contre des réalisations des attaquants américain Folarin Balogun (61e) et espagnol Ansu Fati (90e+1) de l\'autre. Au classement du championnat de France, Monaco gagne une place et prend la sixième position, à trois points du podium. De son côté, Metz, lanterne rouge, est officiellement rélégué en Ligue 2. Les Messins multiplient les coups de pied arrêté et tentent de s\'offrir une fin de match de folie. Ce nouveau corner est obtenu par Hein. Trouvé par Caio Henrique, en une touche de balle, Fati, dans la surface, contrôle, avant de marquer, d\'une frappe du gauche! De loin, Sarr frappe du gauche, mais Zakaria le contre. Abuashvili obtient ensuite un nouveau corner. Henrique se charge du corner. Dans la surface, son ballon arrive sur la tête de Kehrer, qui ne cadre pas! Après un centre venu de la droite, Hein, dans la surface, met la tête, mais son ballon vient s\'écraser sur le poteau! Kvilitaia, après une feinte de frappe dans la surface, se retrouve au sol, au duel avec Kehrer. Derrière, Stambouli, dans la surface, frappe du droit. Son ballon file à côté! Après une faute sur Tsitaishvili, Coulibaly, tout juste entré en jeu, écope du premier jaune de ce match. Le speaker s\'est emparé de son micro pour faire passer un message, après cet incident. Les sifflets se font entendre. Les supporters monégasques ont allumé des fumigènes. L\'un d\'entre eux s\'est même retrouvé sur la pelouse! L\'arbitre est obligé d\'arrêter le jeu. Akliouche, de loin, dans l\'axe, choisit la frappe du gauche. Son ballon est renvoyé par Sy, avant de finir en corner, grâce à Adingra. Hein se charge d\'un nouveau coup franc, situé côté droit. Son ballon arrive dans la surface, au premier poteau. A la réception du ballon, Deminguet marque, d\'une tête décroisée! A droite, de loin, Zakaria prend sa chance du droit. Son ballon est contré par Gbamin, qui concède un nouveau corner. Après ce corner, Pogba, dans la surface, place sa tête. Son ballon est contré par Yegbe. Monaco réclame une main, mais l\'arbitre ne bronche pas. Après un coup franc, de loin, côté droit, Mbala prend sa chance du gauche, en force. Son ballon file au-dessus! Camara a subi une torsion à une cheville. Il s\'est, malgré tout, relevé. Coup franc, excentré côté droit, pour Monaco. Après un centre venu de la droite, Deminguet, dans la surface, met la tête, mais son ballon passe juste à côté! Trouvé en profondeur, Akliouche se défait de deux défenseurs. A l\'entrée de la surface, il frappe du gauche, mais son ballon file juste à côté! Bien frappé par Camara, ce coup franc arrive dans la surface, avant d\'être renvoyé par la défense messine. Après une faute de Deminguet sur Camara, Monaco s\'apprête à tirer un coup franc légèrement côté gauche. Sorti loin de son but, sur sa droite, Sy se couche sur le ballon et se tourne rapidement pour faire en sorte que le ballon reste dans la surface. Paul Pogba pourrait être titularisé. Le coach des Monégasques, Sébastien Pocognoli, a en tout cas testé cette option à l\'entraînement vendredi. Monaco doit réenclencher la marche avant. Après une défaite face au Paris FC et deux matchs nuls sur les trois derniers matchs, le club du Rocher se retrouve septième du classement de Ligue 1, à six points du podium, et sous pression dans la course à l\'Europe. Les joueurs de Sébastien Pocognoli se déplacent à Metz ce samedi, pour la 32e journée de Ligue 1. Les Messins, derniers du classements, peuvent eux être officiellement relégués ce soir.', 'https://rmcsport.bfmtv.com/football/ligue-1/direct-metz-monaco-suivez-le-match-de-la-32e-journee-de-ligue-1-en-live_LS-202605020057.html', NULL, '2026-05-02 20:43:55', '2026-05-02 20:43:55', 'Football', 1, 50, 'fr', 'https://images.bfmtv.com/fyqft0nd_OODCVroYNnMuQMUUW0=/0x156:2048x1308/images/Paul-Pogba-avec-ses-coequipiers-de-l-AS-Monaco-2-mai-2026-2279734.jpg', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 6),
(110, 'County Championship: Zak Crawley continues to struggle with bat for Kent while Emilio Gay impresses for Durham', 'Saturday\'s County Championship action sees England batter Zak Crawley struggle again for Kent, scoring just 15 against Derbyshire with his place as international opener continuing to come into question; Elsewhere, Durham batter Emilio Gay impressed with 75 not out against Middlesex Zak Crawley failed again for Kent in Saturday\'s County Championship as his chances of keeping his England place continue to diminish. After making a breezy 44 on day one of the Division Two clash with Derbyshire, the opener made just 15 in the second innings before being trapped lbw by Rory Haydon. Despite Crawley\'s low score, Kent are in a good position, ending day two on 38 for two with a second-innings lead of 86. Kent earlier bowled Derbyshire out for 304, with Keith Dudgeon taking four for 78. Emilio Gay has been touted as a possibility for a Test call-up and finished the day on 75 not out as Durham responded to Middlesex\'s hefty score of 430. Ryan Higgins converted an overnight fifty into 131, but Gay was in form as Durham made it to 135 for one at close. Ollie Pope will hope to make hay on Sunday in his bid to be involved in England\'s plans as Surrey look to force a sizeable first-innings lead against Sussex. Pope is not out on 14 as Surrey closed on 292 for two in response to Sussex\'s 358 for nine declared. Dominic Sibley is not out on 116, with opening partner Rory Burns adding 77. Yorkshire fought back against Somerset, bowling their hosts out for 274 from a position of 201 for four. They are still 99 behind, though, with 10 second-innings wickets in hand. Kiran Carlson turned his overnight century into a double as he posted 209 in Glamorgan\'s mammoth 536 for seven declared against Hampshire. Ricardo Vasconcelos scored a century as Northamptonshire batted out the day against Worcestershire.The opener scored 115 as Northamptonshire were 366 for five, with a first-innings lead of 60. Watch the Women\'s T20 World Cup live on Sky Sports with selected games streamed for free via the Sky Sports App. Not got Sky? Stream cricket contract-free on NOW.', 'https://www.skysports.com/cricket/news/12040/13539302/county-championship-zak-crawley-continues-to-struggle-with-bat-for-kent-while-emilio-gay-impresses-for-durham', NULL, '2026-05-02 20:43:55', '2026-05-02 20:43:55', 'Football', 1, 30, 'en', 'https://e0.365dm.com/26/05/1600x900/skysports-zak-crawley-cricket_7237551.jpg?20260502195848', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 7),
(111, 'Arsenal 3-0 Fulham: Viktor Gyokeres and Bukayo Saka on target as Gunners go six points clear of Man City', 'Report and free match highlights as Arsenal open up a six-point gap on Man City at the top of the Premier League with a 3-0 win over Fulham at the Emirates Stadium; Viktor Gyokeres scored twice and Bukayo Saka was also on the scoresheet Arsenal moved six points clear of Manchester City and boosted their goal difference with a dominant 3-0 win over Fulham. The Gunners scored all three goals during a rampant first-half display with Viktor Gyokeres netting twice and the fit-again Bukayo Saka also on target on his first start since the Carabao Cup final. Arsenal came into the game on the back of their gruelling 1-1 draw with Atletico Madrid in the Champions League semi-final first leg, but Saka\'s introduction inspired a slick attacking performance. Arsenal: Raya (7), White (7), Saliba (7), Gabriel (7), Calafiori (7), Rice (8), Lewis-Skelly (8), Eze (7), Saka (9), Trossard (8), Gyokeres (9) Subs: Madueke (6), Zubimendi (6), Jesus (6), Dowman (6), Mosquera (6) Fulham: Leno (5), Castagne (5), Andersen (6), Bassey (6), Robinson (5), Reed (5), Lukic (5), Wilson (5), Smith Rowe (6), Chukwueze (5), Jimenez (5). Subs: King (6), Cairney (6), Bobb (6), Muniz (6), Kasu-Asare (6) Player of the Match: Viktor Gyokeres The winger set up Gyokeres\'s close-range opener with a low cross after beating Raul Jimenez, then finished superbly at Bernd Leno\'s near post from the striker\'s pass for the second Gyokeres, scorer of Arsenal\'s penalty against Atletico, added his second goal, and 21st of the season in all competitions, when he guided home a header from Leandro Trossard\'s cross. The half-time scoreline allowed Mikel Arteta to withdraw Saka with Tuesday\'s second leg against Atletico in mind, while Gyokeres was also given a rest after being denied a hat-trick when Leno saved his one-on-one chance shortly before the hour-mark. Arsenal had chances to add to their lead against the lacklustre visitors, whose preparations for the game were impacted by a virus, with Gabriel seeing a close-range effort blocked on the line, Riccardo Calafiori hitting the bar, and substitute Max Dowman firing wide. But a three-goal margin of victory represents a potentially crucial boost to their goal difference nonetheless, putting them four goals ahead of second-placed Manchester City, who are now six points behind them, albeit with two games in hand. An eye-catching performance from academy graduate Myles Lewis-Skelly, on his first senior start in his natural midfield berth, added another positive for Arteta as the fans inside the Emirates Stadium celebrated a vital win in their title hunt. Bukayo Saka and Viktor Gyokeres hadn\'t combined for a goal all season going into the game. In the space of half an hour against Fulham, they did it twice. The pair have struggled to build chemistry on the pitch this term but it\'s better late than never. Arsenal have been cautious with Saka. There has been a concerted effort not to rush him back from his latest injury setback. And the approach appears to have paid off. He looked sharp right from the start of the game at the Emirates Stadium. \"I think the pain is gone,\" said Mikel Arteta when asked whether his Achilles injury was fully behind him in his press conference. \"That was something that was restricting his capacity to deliver certain actions. Today he felt loose, he felt relaxed.\" He certainly looked like his old self when he burst away from Raul Jimenez and put the opening goal on a plate for Gyokeres. His finish for the second goal, in at Bernd Leno\'s near post after shaping to shoot for the far post, was vintage Saka. That it came from a Gyokeres pass added to the sense of an understanding being built. \"They haven\'t played together much unfortunately because of the injuries that we had, but there were a lot of relationships that I really enjoyed today,\" said Arteta. Sky Sports\' Paul Merson described Viktor Gyokeres\'s performance as his best for Arsenal. \"It was the best I\'ve seen him play. It reminded me of [Erling] Haaland today - he went up against [Joachim] Andersen, he won free kicks. \"The prime example for me was the Saka goal, it showed what confidence he\'s playing with. \"I thought the players trusted him a lot more, they were passing it into him and he looked more confident.\" Arsenal boss Mikel Arteta in his press conference: \"I\'m very happy with the team performance, individual performances. \"We knew how difficult it would be, especially coming back from Madrid so late on Thursday afternoon, and the energy we spent in the game. \"And understanding that, even if you don\'t want to talk about it, you have a huge game in a few days here.', 'https://www.skysports.com/football/arsenal-vs-fulham/report/531469', NULL, '2026-05-02 20:43:55', '2026-05-02 20:43:55', 'Handball', NULL, 30, 'en', 'https://e0.365dm.com/26/05/1600x900/skysports-viktor-gyokeres-arsenal_7237368.jpg?20260502174911', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 7),
(112, 'العصبة تحدد ملعب مواجهة المنصور وبركان - هسبورت', 'كشفت العصبة الاحترافية لكرة القدم، يومه السبت، عن مكان إجراء مباراة اتحاد يعقوب المنصور وضيفه نهضة بركان، المقررة يوم الاثنين المقبل، ضمن الجولة 18 من البطولة الاحترافية. وسيكون الملعب الأولمبي بالرباط مسرحا لهذه المواجهة، انطلاقا من الساعة السابعة مساء، بعدما ظل الملعب غير محدد في البرنامج السابق. ويدخل اتحاد يعقوب المنصور اللقاء بمعنويات مرتفعة، عقب إطاحته بالوداد الرياضي في ميدانه خلال الدورة الماضية، حيث يسعى لمواصلة مفاجآته أمام أندية الصفوة. وفي المقابل، يطمح الفريق البركاني لتصحيح المسار وتجاوز كبوته الأخيرة، عقب تعثره داخل قواعده أمام الكوكب المراكشي، في رحلة البحث عن العودة لسكة الانتصارات من قلب العاصمة. ‫‫من شروط النشر : عدم الإساءة للكاتب أو للأشخاص أو للمقدسات أو مهاجمة الأديان أو الذات الإلهية، والابتعاد عن التحريض العنصري والشتائم‬.', 'https://www.hesport.com/%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%b9%d8%b5%d8%a8%d8%a9-%d8%aa%d8%ad%d8%af%d8%af-%d9%85%d9%84%d8%b9%d8%a8-%d9%85%d9%88%d8%a7%d8%ac%d9%87%d8%a9-%d8%a7%d9%84%d9%85%d9%86%d8%b5%d9%88%d8%b1-%d9%88%d8%a8%d8%b1%d9%83%d8%a7-437214.html', NULL, '2026-05-02 19:26:52', '2026-05-02 20:43:55', 'Football', 1, 0, 'ar', 'https://i1.hesport.com/wp-content/overlay/2026/05/IMG_5808.jpeg?v2', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 9),
(113, 'معما يتوّج بجائزة أفضل لاعب شاب في واتفورد بعد موسم مميز - هسبورت', 'توّج نادي واتفورد الإنجليزي لاعبه المغربي الشاب عثمان معما بجائزة أفضل لاعب واعد داخل الفريق، تقديرا لما بصم عليه من أداء مميز خلال الموسم الكروي الجاري. وجاء هذا التتويج بعد المستويات اللافتة التي قدمها معما، حيث استطاع فرض نفسه كأحد الأسماء الصاعدة داخل المجموعة، بفضل انسجامه السريع وتطوره الملحوظ في مختلف المباريات. وخاض اللاعب المغربي هذا الموسم 25 مباراة بقميص فريقه، تمكن خلالها من تسجيل 4 أهداف، في أرقام تعكس حضوره المتزايد ومساهمته الفعالة، رغم حداثة تجربته. ويُرتقب أن يشكل هذا التتويج حافزا إضافيا لمعما لمواصلة التألق، خاصة في ظل اقتراب الاستحقاقات الدولية، حيث يواصل لفت انتباه الطاقم التقني للمنتخب المغربي، طامحا لنيل فرصة ضمن صفوف “أسود الأطلس” مستقبلا. ‫‫من شروط النشر : عدم الإساءة للكاتب أو للأشخاص أو للمقدسات أو مهاجمة الأديان أو الذات الإلهية، والابتعاد عن التحريض العنصري والشتائم‬.', 'https://www.hesport.com/%d9%85%d8%b9%d9%85%d8%a7-%d9%8a%d8%aa%d9%88%d9%91%d8%ac-%d8%a8%d8%ac%d8%a7%d8%a6%d8%b2%d8%a9-%d8%a3%d9%81%d8%b6%d9%84-%d9%84%d8%a7%d8%b9%d8%a8-%d8%b4%d8%a7%d8%a8-%d9%81%d9%8a-%d9%88%d8%a7%d8%aa%d9%81-437202.html', NULL, '2026-05-02 18:15:50', '2026-05-02 20:43:55', 'Football', 1, 0, 'ar', 'https://i1.hesport.com/wp-content/overlay/2026/05/IMG_5803.jpeg?v2', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 9),
(114, 'الزمامرة يعلن توقيف بيع تذاكر الوداد - هسبورت', 'أعلن نادي نهضة أتلتيك الزمامرة، في بلاغ رسمي، عن توقيف عملية بيع التذاكر المخصصة لجماهير نادي الوداد الرياضي، وذلك تماشيا مع قرار العصبة الوطنية لكرة القدم الاحترافية، القاضي بمنع تنقل الجماهير الزائرة خلال المرحلة المقبلة من منافسات الدوري المغربي. ومن المرتقب أن تجرى هذه المواجهة القوية يوم غد الأحد، ابتداء من الساعة الخامسة مساء، على أرضية ملعب الشهيد أحمد شكري بمدينة الزمامرة، وذلك لحساب الجولة الـ18 من البطولة الوطنية الاحترافية في قسمها الأول. ودعت إدارة نادي الزمامرة كافة الجماهير الرياضية، إلى التحلي بروح المسؤولية والالتزام التام بالقوانين التنظيمية المعمول بها، مؤكدة حرصها الدائم على توفير كافة الظروف الملائمة لإنجاح هذا الموعد الرياضي، في أجواء يسودها الاحترام المتبادل والروح الرياضية العالية. ويأتي هذا القرار، في سياق التدابير الأمنية والتنظيمية التي اعتمدتها السلطات المختصة بالتنسيق مع العصبة الاحترافية، لتفادي أي اصطدامات أو أحداث قد ترافق تنقل الجماهير بين المدن، وضمان مرور مباريات البطولة الوطنية في أحسن الظروف. ‫‫من شروط النشر : عدم الإساءة للكاتب أو للأشخاص أو للمقدسات أو مهاجمة الأديان أو الذات الإلهية، والابتعاد عن التحريض العنصري والشتائم‬.', 'https://www.hesport.com/%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%b2%d9%85%d8%a7%d9%85%d8%b1%d8%a9-%d9%8a%d8%b9%d9%84%d9%86-%d8%aa%d9%88%d9%82%d9%8a%d9%81-%d8%a8%d9%8a%d8%b9-%d8%aa%d8%b0%d8%a7%d9%83%d8%b1-%d8%a7%d9%84%d9%88%d8%af%d8%a7%d8%af-437211.html', NULL, '2026-05-02 18:13:37', '2026-05-02 20:43:55', 'Football', 1, 10, 'ar', 'https://i1.hesport.com/wp-content/overlay/2026/05/IMG_5806.jpeg?v2', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 9),
(115, 'Padres announce agreement to sell team to investor group led by Kwanza Jones and José E. Feliciano', 'San Diego Padres’ Xander Bogaerts, center, and teammate stand line prior to a baseball game against Arizona Diamondbacks in Mexico City, Saturday, April 25, 2026. (AP Photo/Fernando Llano) Ripple of Hope award recipient Jose E. Feliciano poses at the Robert F. Kennedy Human Rights Ripple of Hope Award Gala at New York Hilton Midtown on Thursday, Dec. 9, 2021, in New York. (Photo by Evan Agostini/Invision/AP, File) San Diego Padres’ coach Craig Stammen, left, enters the field prior to a baseball game against Arizona Diamondbacks in Mexico City, Saturday, April 25, 2026. (AP Photo/Fernando Llano) San Diego Padres first baseman Ty France, left, and catcher Freddy Fermin, right, douse Gavin Sheets as he does a television interview after leading the Padres to a victory over the Colorado Rockies in a baseball game Thursday, April 23, 2026, in Denver. (AP Photo/David Zalubowski) The San Diego Padres have reached an agreement to sell control of the team to an investor group led by Kwanza Jones and José E. Feliciano. The family of late owner Peter Seidler formally announced the deal Saturday. The sale must still be approved by Major League Baseball. The deal with private equity billionaire Feliciano and his wife took shape last month at an MLB-record valuation of $3.9 billion. The Padres’ announcement of the deal didn’t give specifics on the members of the investor group or the purchase price. “The Padres are more than a baseball team; they are a unifying force in San Diego, rooted in community, connection and belonging,” Jones and Feliciano said in a joint statement. “As life and business partners, and as a family, we are honored to lead this next chapter together. We have worked hard for everything we have achieved, and we have built it together. We see that same spirit in this team and its fans, and we know what it takes to win. We are committed to showing up, listening and earning the trust of this community while building on the strong foundation established by the Seidler family. “This is about more than baseball — it’s about boosting the pride, energy, and connection that define the Padres, investing in community, deepening belonging and ensuring this team remains accessible and endures for generations. We are all in — with the goal of bringing a World Series championship to San Diego.” Seidler’s family began to explore a sale of the Padres last November, two years after the death of the popular Peter Seidler, who became the Padres’ primary owner in 2020. His brother, John Seidler, has served as the Padres’ chairman since his death. “When I became control person, my goal was to continue building on our recent success in pursuit of a World Series championship for the city of San Diego and our faithful fans,” John Seidler said in a statement. “As I pass the baton to Kwanza and José, I do so with full confidence that they share that vision as well as the Padres’ deep commitment to San Diego. It’s what the team, our fans and the community deserve. Our family loves this team.” Peter Seidler joined the Padres’ ownership group in 2012 when John Moores sold the team for $800 million to a group headed by Ron Fowler. Seidler took over and immediately endeared himself to San Diego’s fans with his aggressive financial backing of general manager A.J. Preller, who built a team that has reached the playoffs in four of the past six years. The Padres have been a hot ticket for several years as San Diego’s only team in the four biggest North American sports leagues, ranking second in the majors in attendance last season. Preller’s roster is off to another strong start this season, sitting second in the NL West at 19-12 heading into a home game against the Chicago White Sox on Saturday night. Jones and Feliciano already got a start on their new endeavor last month when they traveled to Mexico City to watch the Padres’ international series against the Arizona Diamondbacks. The couple was spotted sitting with Padres CEO Erik Greupner. Feliciano will become the second Latino owner in baseball, joining Los Angeles Angels owner Arte Moreno. Latino and Hispanic players comprise roughly 30% of major league rosters.', 'https://apnews.com/article/padres-sale-jose-feliciano-dead3ec4ce6413793ca3afed0583b043', NULL, '2026-05-02 20:08:37', '2026-05-02 21:42:49', 'Handball', NULL, 40, 'en', 'https://dims.apnews.com/dims4/default/530d3f4/2147483647/strip/true/crop/5211x3472+0+1/resize/980x653!/quality/90/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fassets.apnews.com%2F4a%2F0f%2F2f831a9481af624439d4bc573d11%2F8a3c4728c9214f068c17b7252ae27dff', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 2),
(116, 'Leur sort est scellé: battus par Monaco, les Messins sont officiellement relégués en Ligue 2', 'Ce n\'est pas en 2026 que le FC Metz mettra un terme à sa triste histoire récente. Sa 22e défaite de la saison (pour trois succès et sept nuls), ce samedi à domicile contre Monaco (1-2), a entériné une descente inéluctable pour le club lorrain, qui n\'aura passé que cinq journées de Ligue 1 hors de la dernière place. >> Revivez Metz-MonacoEn 25 ans, les Grenats sont descendus huit fois, plus que toute autre équipe au sein des cinq grands championnats européens, loin des 35 années consécutives passées au sein de l\'élite (1967-2002) qui avaient fait d\'eux un pilier de la première division. C\'est en grande partie à cause de sa défense, la plus mauvaise d\'assez loin (72 buts encaissés), que le club messin retrouvera la Ligue 2, un an seulement après l\'avoir quittée.\"C\'est un calvaire mais il faut que cela serve à tout le monde, aux joueurs, au club, il faut que le bon bilan soit fait, les bons constats et repartir\", soulignait Benoît Tavenot avant la rencontre en Normandie. Arrivé le 20 janvier pour remplacer Stéphane Le Mignan avec la lourde tâche de sauver le club de la relégation, l\'entraîneur n\'est pas parvenu à stopper sa chute sans fin. Entre sa première partie de saison à Bastia et sa deuxième à Metz, Benoît Tavenot a même établi un nouveau record de matches consécutifs sans victoire à la tête d\'une formation de Ligue 1 ou de Ligue 2: 25, battant les 23 de Faruk Hadzibegic sur le banc d\'Arles-Avignon en 2010-11.\"Depuis le départ, cela ne change rien\", constatait-il en amont du spectaculaire match nul 4-4 au Havre qui n\'a fait que retarder l\'échéance. \"J\'ai pris un groupe, une situation et j\'essaie au quotidien de l\'améliorer et de faire performer l\'équipe, cela n\'a pas marché. Depuis le 20 janvier, je suis en déficit, c\'est la course, on est en perpétuelle réadaptation, on gère l\'urgence en permanence.\"L\'entraîneur de 49 ans ne doit pas être tenu comme unique responsable de cette situation, ni son prédécesseur Stéphane Le Mignan, artisan de la montée en Ligue 1 la saison dernière, mais peut-être trop ambitieux dans le jeu avec un tel effectif. Cet échec est aussi le fruit d\'une intersaison ratée, entre le départ du capitaine Matthieu Udol, auteur de sa plus belle saison à Lens, et un recrutement insuffisant. Le retour d\'anciens de la maison messine comme Habib Diallo (seulement quatre buts) et Boubacar Traoré, blessé une partie de la saison, n\'a pas suffi.Joueur majeur de la saison dernière, Gauthier Hein n\'a pas réussi à emmener ses coéquipiers vers le maintien, perdant même le brassard de capitaine, alors qu\'il possède les meilleures statistiques offensives de son club (six buts et huit passes décisives), dont un coup franc déposé sur la tête de Jessy Deminguet face à Monaco ce samedi (49e).Devant au score, les Messins ont cru un temps retarder l\'échéance d\'une descente inexorable. Mais les réalisations de Folarin Balogun (61e) et d\'Ansu Fati (90e+1) les ont officiellement renvoyé en Ligue 2.', 'https://rmcsport.bfmtv.com/football/ligue-1/leur-sort-est-scelle-battus-par-monaco-les-messins-sont-officiellement-relegues-en-ligue-2_AV-202605020323.html', NULL, '2026-05-02 21:42:49', '2026-05-02 21:42:49', 'Football', 1, 75, 'fr', 'https://images.bfmtv.com/xlw0doeo9rTBG4Gb7NLM5qV1A4U=/0x80:2048x1232/images/Les-joueurs-de-Metz-lors-du-match-contre-Monaco-le-2-mai-2026-2279754.jpg', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 6);
INSERT INTO `articles` (`id`, `title`, `content`, `url`, `author`, `published_at`, `collected_at`, `sport_category`, `sport_id`, `importance_score`, `langue`, `image_url`, `nb_mots`, `status`, `sentiment`, `metadata`, `source_id`) VALUES
(117, 'Premier League title race: Arsenal have \'flipped the pressure\' onto Man City by taking a six-point lead, says Jamie Redknapp', 'Arsenal moved six points clear at the top of the Premier League with 3-0 win over Fulham; Man City have two games in hand, starting with Everton away on Monday; Gunners have goal difference advantage, too, as Mikel Arteta says his team \"keep the dream alive\" Arsenal have \"flipped the pressure\" on to Man City in the Premier League title race after a 3-0 thumping of Fulham extended their lead to six points at the top of the table, says Jamie Redknapp. City went top with a win over Arsenal last month but the Gunners have won back-to-back games since then, making it essential Pep Guardiola\'s side respond with their next two Premier League fixtures, starting with Everton away on Monday Night Football. \"This Man City team can blow teams away, but what Arsenal have done is flipped the pressure. Anything can still happen, but I think Arsenal are favourites,\" said the Sky Sports pundit. Arsenal\'s three goals on Saturday also extended their goal difference advantage over City to four goals. They have scored 67 goals to City\'s 66. Redknapp believes Arsenal\'s remaining Premier League games - against West Ham, Burnley and Crystal Palace - present an opportunity to further strengthen their position in that differentiator. \"For Man City, the Bournemouth fixture is going to be Andoni Iraola\'s last home game so there\'s going to be a celebration there and Bournemouth will want to put on a bit of a show,\" said Redknapp. \"Everton away against a David Moyes side is always going to be difficult, and Brentford are going for Europe. \"If it goes to goal difference, I look at the games Arsenal have got as a big advantage. There\'s a game that really shouts at me and it\'s Burnley at home. \"If we work on the basis that both teams are perfect and win their remaining games, if Arsenal can\'t beat Burnley 3-0 or 4-0 and get their goal difference up... That\'s a big opportunity.\" For former Arsenal midfielder Paul Merson, if the Gunners can win their final three Premier League fixtures, it may be too much for City to overhaul, with a goal-difference margin to make up. \"If Arsenal win their next three Premier League matches, Man City will have to pull up trees,\" he said. \"With the FA Cup final [against Chelsea on May 16], they will always be playing catch up between now and the end of the season - unless they win big against Everton and Brentford, and they can swing it around where Arsenal are playing catch-up and the goal difference becomes a lot. \"Otherwise, they\'re always going to be chasing their tail and it takes its toll in the end - knowing you\'ve just got to win this game just to stay on the tails. \"The easiest game they\'ve got to come is against Aston Villa. They will already be in the top five, that\'s cemented. They could have played in the Europa League final on the Wednesday before. Arsenal boss Mikel Arteta was delighted with his side\'s performance against Fulham, particularly in the first half. Asked if the win over Fulham sent a manager to Man City, he said no - it sent a message to his own squad. \"It was a great team performance from the beginning. There were some great individual performances as well, which is very important. \"We started in the game like we wanted. Very aggressive and lively. Great combinations, attacking combinations, rally intense in the high press. \"We got the crowd going and when this stadium creates that kind of atmosphere, it can be difficult for the opponent. \"It was the type of game we expected, we had more players available today as we have been missing some players as it was true we lost some players before the game. \"We showed a lot of authority, determination and composure. We brought a lot of energy to the stadium and they responded in a brilliant way and that was a big win.\"', 'https://www.skysports.com/football/news/12040/13539530/premier-league-title-race-arsenal-have-flipped-the-pressure-onto-man-city-by-taking-a-six-point-lead-says-jamie-redknapp', NULL, '2026-05-02 21:42:49', '2026-05-02 21:42:49', 'Handball', NULL, 15, 'en', 'https://e0.365dm.com/26/05/1600x900/skysports-premier-league-arsenal_7237471.jpg?20260502183717', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 7),
(118, 'Miami GP Sprint: Lando Norris takes his first win of 2026 while Kimi Antonelli drops from fourth to sixth after penalty', 'World champion Lando Norris impresses to lead team-mate Oscar Piastri in McLaren one-two in Sprint; Title-leading Kimi Antonelli drops from fourth to sixth; watch Miami Grand Prix Qualifying later on Saturday at 9pm on Sky Sports F1 and Main Event, with build-up from 8pm Lando Norris claimed the first win of his world title defence with an impressive victory in the Miami Sprint in a one-two for much-improved McLaren. Mercedes\' title-leading Kimi Antonelli finished fourth on the road but was relegated to sixth immediately after the 19-lap contest by a five-second penalty for repeat track limits infringements. Team-mate George Russell had finished directly behind his team-mate in fifth after losing out in an earlier battle over the place on track so took over fourth place in the final classification, trimming Antonelli\'s world championship lead to seven points in the process ahead of Sunday\'s full-length Grand Prix. Oscar Piastri held off Ferrari\'s Charles Leclerc for second in the second McLaren, with Russell eventually fourth and Red Bull\'s Max Verstappen, who won out after an early duel with Lewis Hamilton, fifth ahead of the demoted Antonelli. But Norris was untouchable out front as he followed up becoming the first non-Mercedes driver to claim a pole position this season on Friday by ending the Silver Arrows\' hitherto perfect Sprint/Grand Prix winning record in 2026 on Saturday. The tone for the reigning champion\'s success was set at the start when he comfortably converted pole into the race lead while Antonelli continued his unwanted record of losing places at every race start this year amid a lack of grip as Piastri and Leclerc swept past the lead Mercedes. Leclerc finished on Piastri\'s tail in third to continue Ferrari\'s record of finishing in that place in every Grand Prix and Sprint so far this season, although Hamilton was only seventh after his pace faded following an entertaining early duel with Verstappen. The long-time rivals brushed wheels in the opening turns before Hamilton got ahead of the Red Bull later around the lap. But Verstappen appeared to have the superior pace and, after an initial overtake back on lap eight was scuppered when he completed the move by running both wide off track at Turn 11 and had to give the place back, the Dutchman got cleanly ahead next time around and pulled away comfortably from the Ferrari thereafter. Pierre Gasly took the final point on offer in the Sprint with eighth for Alpine after moving ahead of team-mate Franco Colapinto on the opening lap. 1) Lando Norris, McLaren2) Oscar Piastri, McLaren3) Charles Leclerc, Ferrari 4) George Russell, Mercedes5) Max Verstappen, Red Bull6) Kimi Antonelli, Mercedes7) Lewis Hamilton, Ferrari8) Pierre Gasly, Alpine While McLaren will not be getting carried away by their impressive start to the Miami weekend, the introduction of a suite of upgrades onto the MCL40 for the first race back after the sport\'s enforced April break has so far brought the reigning two-time constructors\' champions right back into play at the front of the field. Norris, who had not finished higher than fourth in the three Grands Prix and one Sprint before the extended break, won the Sprint by 3.8 seconds from Piastri and has appeared in the groove around the Miami International Autodrome all weekend so far. \"Nice to be back on the top step! A good day for us,\" said the world champion, whose last win in either race format came at the Sao Paulo Grand Prix last November. \"It was hot out there and sweaty. I was pushing, trying to find that balance of pushing and staying relaxed to not make mistakes. With only limited points on offer in a short-form Sprint, Norris remains 42 points behind Antonelli at the head of the Drivers\' Championship, although that is two points closer to the Italian than he would have been had the Mercedes driver not fallen foul of track limits breaches. Antonelli racked up four different offences of going off track during the 19-lap race, triggering an automatic five-second sanction. It capped a frustrating Sprint for Antonelli, even if he was absolved of any blame for another troubled getaway in his car at the lights from the front row. Antonelli told Sky Sports F1: \"On my side for once, I did everything right with the procedures. We need to check what happened. The grip was very low, probably lower than we expected. \"After that, I was really frustrated and didn\'t even drive well. I did a lot of mistakes and got track limits, which is something I need to avoid. \"This weekend has been more difficult but it was expected with everyone bringing big upgrades. We just need to maximise the result and now focus on qualifying.\" Saturday May 26.30pm: Ted\'s Sprint Notebook8pm: Miami GP Qualifying build-up*9pm: MIAMI GP QUALIFYING*11pm: Ted\'s Qualifying Notebook* Sunday May 35.25pm: F2 Feature Race7pm: Miami GP build-up: Grand Prix Sunday*9pm: THE MIAMI GRAND PRIX*11pm: Miami GP reaction: Chequered Flag*12am: Ted\'s Notebook* Formula 1 is in M', 'https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12040/13539201/miami-gp-sprint-lando-norris-takes-his-first-win-of-2026-while-kimi-antonelli-drops-from-fourth-to-sixth-after-penalty', NULL, '2026-05-02 21:42:49', '2026-05-02 21:42:49', 'Sports Mécaniques', NULL, 40, 'en', 'https://e0.365dm.com/26/05/1600x900/skysports-lando-norris-mclaren_7237423.jpg?20260502181608', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 7),
(119, 'الكوكب يشيد بجماهيره ويندد بأحداث بركان - هسبورت', 'أصدر نادي الكوكب الرياضي المراكشي بلاغا رسميا، أشاد فيه بالدعم الكبير لجماهيره التي تنقلت إلى مدينة بركان، حيث أكد النادي متابعته الدقيقة لكافة تفاصيل عودة المشجعين لضمان وصولهم بسلام إلى مدينة مراكش. وعبرت إدارة النادي المراكشي، عن اعتزازها بالوفاء الذي أظهره الجمهور بقطعه مئات الكيلومترات لمساندة الفريق. وفي المقابل، أعربت الإدارة عن أسفها الشديد تجاه بعض الأحداث التي وقعت في الملعب ومحيطه بعد نهاية المباراة، معتبرة إياها تصرفات بعيدة عن الروح الرياضية والدينامية الإيجابية التي تعرفها الكرة الوطنية. ‫‫من شروط النشر : عدم الإساءة للكاتب أو للأشخاص أو للمقدسات أو مهاجمة الأديان أو الذات الإلهية، والابتعاد عن التحريض العنصري والشتائم‬.', 'https://www.hesport.com/%d8%a7%d9%84%d9%83%d9%88%d9%83%d8%a8-%d9%8a%d8%b4%d9%8a%d8%af-%d8%a8%d8%ac%d9%85%d8%a7%d9%87%d9%8a%d8%b1%d9%87-%d9%88%d9%8a%d9%86%d8%af%d8%af-%d8%a8%d8%a3%d8%ad%d8%af%d8%a7%d8%ab-%d8%a8%d8%b1%d9%83-437226.html', NULL, '2026-05-02 20:12:59', '2026-05-02 21:42:49', 'Football', 1, 0, 'ar', 'https://i1.hesport.com/wp-content/overlay/2026/05/IMG_5814.jpeg?v2', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 9),
(120, 'إنريكي يشعر بخيبة أمل بعد ضياع فرصة لحسم لقب الدوري الفرنسي - هسبورت', 'عبر لويس إنريكي مدرب باريس سان جيرمان عن خيبة أمله في ضياع فرصة لحسم لقب الدوري الفرنسي بعد التعادل 2 / 2 مع لوريان، اليوم السبت. صرح إنريكي عبر قناة بي إن سبورتس عقب لقاء الجولة 32 من الدوري “هذه هي كرة القدم، ولكن أنا معجب بفريق لوريان، وأسلوب لعبه، إنهم فريق شجاع، وقدموا أداء مميزًا أمامنا في مباراتي الموسم الجاري”. وأضاف المدرب الإسباني: “كنا نستحق الفوز بهذه المباراة، لقد أشركنا العديد من البدلاء، لكنهم أظهروا رغبة قوية، ولكن إهدار الفرص أضاع علينا فوزًا مستحقًا”. وشدد: “لست سعيدًا أو راضيًا، لأننا لم نفز بالمباراة، لا يوجد مدرب يريد أن يكون من الطراز الرفيع يرضى بالتعادل، لكن نتقبل النتيجة أمام منافس مميز”. وتابع: “ولا يمكن بالطبع إغفال صعوبة هذه المباريات في مثل هذه الظروف، لكننا كنا بحاجة شديدة للنقاط الثلاث”. وبشأن تفكيره بعد هذه المباراة في الراحة أم الاستعداد لمواجهة بايرن في إياب قبل نهائي دوري أبطال أوروبا، أجاب لويس إنريكي “المدربون لا يعرفون الراحة بل نفكر دائمًا في المباريات والتحديات القادمة”. وختم تصريحاته: “لا مجال للراحة، وأشعر بالتعب بعد المباراة مثل أي مدرب، وغدًا سيكون الوقت المناسب لطي صفحة هذه المباراة”. ويستعد باريس سان جيرمان حامل لقب دوري أبطال أوروبا لاختبار صعب خارج أرضه عندما يواجه بايرن ميونخ، الأربعاء المقبل، في إياب قبل نهائي دوري الأبطال، علمًا بأن الفريق الفرنسي فاز 5 / 4 ذهابًا بعد مواجهة مثيرة في ملعب حديقة الأمراء. ويعتلي باريس سان جيرمان حامل لقب الدوري في المواسم الأربعة الأخيرة صدارة الترتيب برصيد 70 نقطة، وتتبقى له ثلاث مباريات، يطارده لانس 63 نقطة، وتتبقى له أربع مباريات أولها أمام نيس في وقت لاحق اليوم السبت. ‫‫من شروط النشر : عدم الإساءة للكاتب أو للأشخاص أو للمقدسات أو مهاجمة الأديان أو الذات الإلهية، والابتعاد عن التحريض العنصري والشتائم‬.', 'https://www.hesport.com/%d8%a5%d9%86%d8%b1%d9%8a%d9%83%d9%8a-%d9%8a%d8%b4%d8%b9%d8%b1-%d8%a8%d8%ae%d9%8a%d8%a8%d8%a9-%d8%a3%d9%85%d9%84-%d8%a8%d8%b9%d8%af-%d8%b6%d9%8a%d8%a7%d8%b9-%d9%81%d8%b1%d8%b5%d8%a9-%d9%84%d8%ad%d8%b3-437221.html', NULL, '2026-05-02 19:45:19', '2026-05-02 21:42:49', 'Football', 1, 10, 'ar', 'https://i1.hesport.com/wp-content/overlay/2026/05/IMG_5811.jpeg?v2', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 9),
(121, '76ers eyeing much more as they move on to second round after Game 7 win over Celtics', 'Philadelphia 76ers’ Joel Embiid celebrates following his team’s victory over the Boston Celtics after the Game 7 in a first-round NBA basketball playoffs series, Saturday, May 2, 2026 in Boston. (AP Photo/Jim Davis) Boston Celtics’ Jayson Tatum (right) and Philadelphia 76ers’ Joel Embiid (left) embrace following Philadelphia’s victory in Game 7 in a first-round NBA basketball playoffs series, Saturday, May 2, 2026 in Boston. (AP Photo/Jim Davis) Philadelphia 76ers’ Tyrese Maxey (left) and teammate VJ Edgecombe (right) during the second half of Game 7 in a first-round NBA basketball playoffs series, Saturday, May 2, 2026 in Boston. (AP Photo/Jim Davis) Philadelphia 76ers’ players greet teammate VJ Edgecombe (77) after he hit a third quarter three point shot during Game 7 in a first-round NBA basketball playoffs series, Saturday, May 2, 2026 in Boston. (AP Photo/Jim Davis) BOSTON (AP) — The Philadelphia 76ers didn’t know how many games, if any, they could count on from Joel Embiid in their first-round playoff series against the Boston Celtics. After debuting in Game 4 following appendectomy surgery last month, the former MVP played some of the best playoff basketball of his career over the final four games of the series to lead the 76ers to a 109-100 Game 7 victory over a Celtics team that had looked like a potential NBA title contender. The No. 7 seed’s reward is an Eastern Conference semifinals matchup with the No. 3 seed New York Knicks that begins Monday. In leading Philadelphia to just its second road Game 7 victory ever and first since 1982 against Boston, Embiid finished with 34 points, 12 rebounds and six assists to become the first player in NBA history to score 100 points in a playoff series despite missing the first three games. “Sometimes I’ve been in those positions where I’ve come up short,” Embiid said. “I’ve always said it, you can’t win alone. You need a team. ... The way we’re playing right now, we’re so in sync, offensively, defensively.” He and Tyrese Maxey (30 points, 11 rebounds and seven assists) also became the third duo in league history to each have 25 points, 10 rebounds and five assists in a Game 7. Maxey said this series demonstrated how he now knows when to be assertive and when to defer to Embiid. “It’s a growth, because I had to learn when to be aggressive, when not to be aggressive,” Maxey said. “It got a little bit difficult in the middle of this season. I was basically being first option every single night. Then he comes back and I’ve got to find a way to do both. And he does a really good job of just keeping me engaged and keeping me confident and keep me like, ’Hey I need you to do what you do.’” The 76ers will need everything Embiid gave and more to compete with a Knicks team that plays a much more physical game than Boston. Nurse said he believes Embiid is up for the challenge. He was limping at times in Game 7 but then got extra treatment while on the bench just to be able to contribute late. He had reason to be fatigued because even though nine 76ers players touched the floor in Game 7, only six logged double-digit minutes. Embiid played 39 minutes, tying his series high. “He was doing everything he could to stay in the game,” Nurse said. “Obviously, we ran a lot of things through him and we did just enough.” Nurse said being able to come out the hostile environment of TD Garden with a victory will serve his team well going forward. “It’s really good for us to go through that and respond to it,” Nurse said. “It’s going to be like that in the playoffs. You’re going to be in tight games and it’s going to be super loud. ... And you just have to play through it.” Nurse said he believes the difference was making Boston play halfcourt sets over the final three minutes after the Celtics were able to play in transition for about 12 straight minutes in the third and fourth quarters.', 'https://apnews.com/article/joel-embiid-76ers-advance-nba-playoffs-75b918079f2c498d1a98f68f85754fd8', NULL, '2026-05-03 14:25:23', '2026-05-03 14:25:23', 'Basketball', 2, 29, 'en', 'https://dims.apnews.com/dims4/default/640e4f7/2147483647/strip/true/crop/4315x2875+93+0/resize/980x653!/quality/90/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fassets.apnews.com%2Fbb%2F81%2F40dd224ebc1ac0594fc0d5950725%2F35da0cd238f74cf1b3b6faaa48284ec6', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 2),
(122, 'Stankoven, Andersen lead Hurricanes past Flyers 3-0 in Game 1 of 2nd-round series', 'Carolina Hurricanes goaltender Frederik Andersen (31) is congratulated by Jaccob Slavin, left, following Game 1 of an NHL hockey Stanley Cup second-round playoff series against the Philadelphia Flyers in Raleigh, N.C., Saturday, May 2, 2026. (AP Photo/Karl DeBlaker) Carolina Hurricanes’ Logan Stankoven (22) celebrates after his second goal with teammates Mike Reilly (6), Andrei Svechnikov, back right, and Seth Jarvis (24) during the second period of Game 1 of an NHL hockey Stanley Cup second-round playoff series against the Philadelphia Flyers in Raleigh, N.C., Saturday, May 2, 2026. (AP Photo/Karl DeBlaker) Carolina Hurricanes’ Jordan Staal (11) lunges for the puck with Philadelphia Flyers goaltender Dan Vladar (80) and Nick Seeler (24) nearby during the second period of Game 1 of an NHL hockey Stanley Cup second-round playoff series in Raleigh, N.C., Saturday, May 2, 2026. (AP Photo/Karl DeBlaker) Philadelphia Flyers’ Sean Couturier, right, talks with referee Kelly Sutherland (11) during the third period of Game 1 of an NHL hockey Stanley Cup second-round playoff series against the Carolina Hurricanes in Raleigh, N.C., Saturday, May 2, 2026. (AP Photo/Karl DeBlaker) Carolina Hurricanes’ Logan Stankoven speaks following Game 1 of an NHL hockey Stanley Cup second-round playoff series against the Philadelphia Flyers in Raleigh, N.C., Saturday, May 2, 2026. (AP Photo/Karl DeBlaker) RALEIGH, N.C. (AP) — Logan Stankoven scored twice to continue his postseason tear and the Carolina Hurricanes smothered the Philadelphia Flyers in a 3-0 victory Saturday night to open the second-round series. Jackson Blake also scored for Carolina, and Frederik Andersen stopped 19 shots for his second shutout of these playoffs and seventh in his postseason career. Game 2 of the series is Monday night in Raleigh, with Carolina yet to trail in any of its five postseason games so far after jumping to a 2-0 first-period lead in this one. Carolina closed a first-round sweep of Ottawa last weekend, then had an extended break while the Flyers battled to push past Pittsburgh in overtime of Game 6 on Wednesday night. That led to rest-versus-rust conversations about how the Eastern Conference’s top seed would start Saturday night. Instead, the Hurricanes pounced from the opening puck drop, a departure from how all four regular-season meetings went to overtime or a shootout. Stankoven scored in each of the four wins against the Senators, then scored on a redirect from the slot just 1:31 in. “I think you’re just trying to get it off quick,” Stankoven said. “Obviously, it’s nice to have that confidence that comes with putting the puck in the net, and yeah, you just kind of build off of it.” Blake followed at 7:30, splitting two defenders as he entered the zone and charging in to slip a puck behind Dan Vladar. That was more than enough offense on this night with the Flyers struggling to apply much pressure on Andersen — who opened the Ottawa series with a shutout, too. Philadelphia started its first postseason since 2020 by battling through Pittsburgh to close out a six-game series in overtime on Cam York’s Wednesday night winner. But the Flyers sputtered from the start, managing just nine shots on goal through two periods and being outshot 3-2 on their four power plays for the night. Otherwise, they struggled to find much open ice with Carolina’s aggressive style closing in rapidly to shut down lanes toward Andersen or for the pass. “We talked about it, we just didn’t live it on the ice,” Flyers coach Rick Tocchet said, pointing to a need to react quicker against Carolina’s pressure. “We weren’t quick enough for their speed. ... It’s a good baptism how some of our players are going to have to play.” By the final 10 minutes, the game had turned testy with players having to be separated multiple times. That included 10-minute misconduct penalties on Philadelphia’s Trevor Zegras and Nick Seeler, along with Blake and Shayne Gostisbehere for Carolina. Both teams were down key players. The Flyers didn’t have regular-season goals leader Owen Tippett because of an undisclosed injury, while the Hurricanes were missing defenseman Alexander Nikishin after he suffered a concussion in Game 4 against Ottawa. Carolina veteran Mike Reilly drew in for Nikishin and had the primary assist on Stankoven’s first goal and the secondary assist on Blake’s score.', 'https://apnews.com/article/flyers-hurricanes-score-nhl-stanley-cup-playoffs-91ee6640c10c0fa0b2c8cd4dbcb1ec1c', NULL, '2026-05-03 14:25:23', '2026-05-03 14:25:23', 'Hockey', NULL, 22, 'en', 'https://dims.apnews.com/dims4/default/c2c4308/2147483647/strip/true/crop/4526x3016+0+1/resize/980x653!/quality/90/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fassets.apnews.com%2F05%2F8a%2F4925d8f1a3f4fe558cbe1c3e50f8%2F2c064c169b804d84b73020a7d21bfc53', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 2),
(123, 'DIRECT. Lille-Le Havre : suivez le match de la 32e journée en live', 'Fernandez-Pardo prend le dessus sur Seko et centre aux six mètres mais Lloris intervient parfaitement et repousse en corner ! Le Portugais cherche Fernandez-Pardo dans le dos de Seko mais le défenseur japonais parvient à intercepter le ballon. L\'Islandais voit un peu d\'espace devant lui et déclenche une frappe puissante à 20 mètres, ça vient heurter le poteau droit de Diaw ! Servi dans la surface par Meunier, le capitaine lillois manque sa première touche de balle, c\'est dégagé par les Havrais. Mukau s\'ouvre un angle de tir dans la surface havraise et déclenche une frappe enroulée côté gauche mais cela n\'inquiète pas Diaw dans le but havrais. Gourna-Douath tacle Mukau sans maîtrise, carton logique et coup franc côté droit le long de la ligne de touche pour le LOSC. Le coup franc de Correia est repoussé par une tête havraise, ça revient sur Meunier qui centre dans la surface mais une nouvelle tête normande éloigne le danger. Le HAC n\'a remporté aucun de ses dix derniers matchs à l\'extérieur en championnat (quatre nuls, six défaites). Après avoir connu un début d\'année 2026 plus que compliqué, les hommes de Bruno Genesio ont repris leur marche en avant et restent sur sept victoires et quatre nuls en championnat. Issa Soumaré portera le brassard de capitaine en raison de l\'absence d\'Arouna Sanganté, suspendu cet après-midi. Le XI de départ havrais : Diaw - Zouaoui, Lloris, Seko, Nego - Ebonog, Gourna-Douath - Soumaré (Cap), Boufal, Doucouré - Samatta Le XI de départ lillois : Özer - Perraud, Mandi, Ngoy, Meunier - Bouaddi, André (Cap) - Correia, Haraldsson, Mukau - Fernandez-Pardo Le LOSC (4e) reçoit Le Havre (14e) cet après-midi au Stade Pierre-Mauroy. Les Dogues doivent s\'imposer pour rester bien placé dans la quête d\'une place qualificative en Ligue des champions tandis que les Havrais vont tenter de décrocher au moins un point pour valider officiellement leur maintien en Ligue 1. Coup d\'envoi donné à 15h.', 'https://rmcsport.bfmtv.com/football/ligue-1/direct-lille-le-havre-suivez-le-match-de-la-32e-journee-en-live_LS-202605030203.html', NULL, '2026-05-03 14:25:23', '2026-05-03 14:25:23', 'Football', 1, 77, 'fr', 'https://images.bfmtv.com/yH1elaRjbPikus20iEnFfiShuaE=/0x106:2048x1258/images/Lille-Le-Havre-32e-journee-de-Ligue-1-le-3-mai-2026-2279910.jpg', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 6),
(124, 'OM: \"Il n’y a même pas d’amour-propre\", Rod Fanni fustige les joueurs et les dirigeants après la défaite à Nantes', 'Rod Fanni vide son sac. Passé par l’OM entre 2010 et 2015 puis de 2016 à 2018, avec près de 200 matchs au compteur et plusieurs titres à la clé, Rod Fanni connaît mieux que personne l’exigence marseillaise. Invité dans le Stephen Brunch sur RMC, il a livré une analyse lucide, presque désabusée, de la situation actuelle du club Olympien. \"Moi je comprends toute la région (Provence Alpes Côte d’Azur) parce que j’y suis actuellement. Au-delà de la période qui est compliquée, c’est toutes les désillusions en fait. Je pense que c’est là que la dépression est encore plus forte, parce qu’ils ont fait croire qu\'on pouvait \'rivaliser\' avec le PSG à travers certains matchs, même si c’est une hérésie.\" Dans le viseur de Fanni, une succession d’échecs marquants depuis le début de saison: la défaite cruelle face au Paris Saint-Germain lors du Trophée des Champions après avoir mené jusqu’à la 87e minute, ou encore la lourde défaite contre Club Bruges (3-0) en Ligue des champions. \"Il y a eu le Trophée des champions, il y a eu la Ligue des champions contre Bruges et l\'élimination… En fait, il y a eu tellement de désillusions, tellement de manquements, que la région est vraiment dégoûtée, c’est vraiment un réel dégoût de ce qu’il s’est passé.\" Pour l’ancien international français (5 sélections), le mal est aussi né d’un excès d’optimisme en début de saison. L’enthousiasme populaire, caractéristique de Marseille, se serait transformé en pression mal calibrée. \"À un moment donné, on a mis la barre beaucoup trop haut par rapport à ce que l’on a. On avait une équipe qui était quand même intéressante, mais de là à avoir des espoirs aussi grands, c’est ce qui plombe tout le monde.\" Un constat qui met en lumière le décalage entre les ambitions affichées et le niveau réel de l’effectif. L’OM, porté par quelques performances encourageantes, a laissé croire à une possible rivalité avec Paris, avant de retomber brutalement dans ses travers. Au-delà du terrain, Rod Fanni dénonce un climat délétère en interne. Changements à répétition, tensions entre dirigeants et staff, comportements discutables des joueurs: le diagnostic est sévère. \"Maintenant on est arrivé à un point où ça \'pète\' en interne. Que ce soit le directeur sportif avec l’entraîneur qui s’envoient des messages subliminaux, on voit des joueurs avec des comportements... (…) On voit des joueurs avec des attitudes catastrophiques, notamment contre Nice où on voit des joueurs rigoler avec les adversaires\". Les récents bouleversements - départ de Roberto De Zerbi, arrivée d’Habib Beye, remplacement de Pablo Longoria par Alban Juster (en interim) - n’ont pas permis d’apaiser les tensions. La conclusion est sans appel, presque alarmante pour Fanni: \"Il y a plein de choses qui me choquent, mais ce qui me choque encore plus, c’est qu’il n’y a pas de leader… Il n’y a même pas d’amour-propre quand on voit le discours de Benatia. On sent plus rien.\" Un verdict dur, à l’image de la crise profonde qui traverse aujourd’hui l’OM.', 'https://rmcsport.bfmtv.com/football/clubs/olympique-marseille/om-il-n-y-a-meme-pas-d-amour-propre-rod-fanni-fustige-les-joueurs-et-les-dirigeants-apres-la-defaite-a-nantes_AV-202605030211.html', NULL, '2026-05-03 14:25:23', '2026-05-03 14:25:23', 'Football', 1, 59, 'fr', 'https://images.bfmtv.com/U47bKSZk1nlX8rj7JjYr9o_5HYU=/0x75:2048x1227/images/Rod-Fanni-2279902.jpg', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 6),
(125, 'Celtic move level with Hearts after win over 10-man Hibs', 'Match report and highlights as Celtic beat Hibs 2-1 at Easter Road; Kelechi Iheanacho scored 151 seconds after coming off the bench to secure the win and move Celtic level on points with Hearts at the top of the Scottish Premiership table Super-sub Kelechi Iheanacho was the hero for Celtic as the Hoops beat 10-man Hibernian to move level on points with league leaders Hearts. Iheanacho scored in the 72nd minute - just 151 seconds following his introduction - when Martin O\'Neill\'s side had looked to be limping to a disappointing draw having played for more than than 50 minutes with a man advantage courtesy of Jamie McGrath\'s 21st-minute red card. Had Celtic failed to win, there would have been more controversy surrounding the nature of Joe Newell\'s equaliser for Hibs, with the ball appearing to hit his hand in the build-up just minutes after Daizen Maeda\'s 41st-minute opener. However, Celtic were able to claim the three points in a near-empty Easter Road and move alongside Hearts ahead of the latter\'s clash with Rangers live on Sky Sports on Monday. Playing a day earlier than their title rivals, O\'Neill\'s side were given an opportunity to lay down a marker for Hearts and Rangers and were given the perfect opportunity to do so early on. After a tepid start, the game sprung into life as Newell lunged into a reckless challenge on Alistair Johnston. He was initially shown a yellow card, only for a VAR check to lead to that being upgraded to a red - Hibs\' fourth in three games. From then on, Celtic controlled proceedings without being overly threatening. That was until Maeda tapped home from close range to give the visitors the lead after originally being adjudged to have been offside. There was still time for drama late in the first half, as Newell fired home from close range after Celtic failed to clear their lines. Another lengthy VAR check ensued as the ball appeared to strike the Hibs man on the arm before his shot. However, the goal was allowed to stand much to the shock of everyone in black. It could have proved to have been a major talking point in the title race had O\'Neill\'s men not found a winner. After consistent second-half pressure, they did get their breakthrough as Iheanacho stabbed home past Jordan Smith to secure a crucial three points. It means Celtic move level with Hearts on 73 points ahead of Derek McInnes\' sides clash with third-placed Rangers on Monday. A win for Rangers will mean the top three is separated by just a single point ahead of the final Old Firm showdown next weekend live on Sky Sports.', 'https://www.skysports.com/football/hibernian-vs-celtic/report/555739', NULL, '2026-05-03 14:25:23', '2026-05-03 14:25:23', 'Football', 1, 22, 'en', 'https://e0.365dm.com/26/05/1600x900/skysports-celtic-iheanacho_7237967.jpg?20260503140653', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 7),
(126, 'Lindberg wins Turkish Airlines Open to qualify for US PGA Championship', 'Mikael Lindberg claims his first DP World Tour title and qualifies for the US PGA Championship from May 14-17 at Aronimink Golf Club; Daniel Rodrigues and Guido Migliozzi share second with Scotland\'s Ewen Ferguson in joint-fourth spot Mikael Lindberg secured his maiden DP World Tour title and qualified for the US PGA Championship with a two-stroke win at the Turkish Airlines Open. The 33-year-old Swede held off playing partner Daniel Rodrigues with a final round of 69 to finish on 10-under 278 at a rain-swept National Golf Club in Belek, Antalya. Lindberg, who ensured a debut major appearance at Aronimink Golf Club in two weeks\' time, said: \"This is a dream come true, I\'ve been dreaming about this for so many years. Rodrigues and Italy\'s Guido Migliozzi shared second place on eight under ahead of Scotland\'s Ewen Ferguson, Netherlands\' Darius van Driel and Dane Jacob Skov Olesen. \"I was in the lead after the first round and I just felt like... I don\'t know how to describe this, but it\'s been mentally very tough pretty much the whole week. So it\'s very nice to pull it off,\" added Lindberg. \"The weather on the front nine was actually a lot better than I expected, so I felt like I took advantage of that a little bit. It\'s been a very tough last few holes but the last one was definitely tough.\" Portugal\'s Ricardo Gouveia tied with Italy\'s second-round leader Gregorio De Leo for seventh on six under. Ugo Coussaud, the third member of the final group with Lindberg and Rodrigues, finished on five under alongside JC Ritchie, Kota Kaneko and Englishman Marcus Armitage. Watch all four rounds of the Estrella Damm Catalunya Championship live on Sky Sports. Coverage begins at 12.30pm on Thursday live on Sky Sports Golf. Get Sky Sports or stream with no contract.', 'https://www.skysports.com/golf/news/12040/13539652/dp-world-tour-mikael-lindberg-wins-turkish-airlines-open-to-qualify-for-us-pga-championship', NULL, '2026-05-03 14:25:23', '2026-05-03 14:25:23', 'Golf', NULL, 42, 'en', 'https://e0.365dm.com/26/05/1600x900/skysports-mikael-lindberg-golf_7237929.jpg?20260503130232', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 7),
(127, 'زكري يقلل من شأن \"منتخب سلامي\"', 'أطلق المدرب الجزائري نور الدين زكري تصريحات مثيرة للجدل بخصوص المواجهة المرتقبة بين المنتخب الجزائري ونظيره الأردني، ضمن نهائيات كأس العالم 2026 التي تستضيفها الولايات المتحدة الأمريكية وكندا والمكسيك. وشهدت منصات التواصل الاجتماعي، انتشارا واسعا لمقطع فيديو يوثق تصريحات نور الدين زكري، والتي جاءت خلال بث مباشر عبر تطبيق تيك توك. وقلل زكري في تصريحاته من شأن “النشامى”، معتبرا أن المقارنة بين المنتخبين غير عادلة نظرا للفوارق الفنية التي تميل لصالح محاربي الصحراء. وذهب زكري إلى أبعد من ذلك بوصفه المباراة بالمحسومة، حيث صرح بأنه في حال فشل المنتخب الجزائري في تحقيق الفوز على الأردن، فإنه سيكون لزاما على الجزائريين اعتزال كرة القدم بصفة نهائية. وأضاف أن مستوى المنتخب الأردني لا يرقى لمنافسة الجزائر، مشددا على أنه لا يمكن وضع الطرفين في كفة واحدة من الناحية التنافسية. وتأتي هذه الخرجة الإعلامية المستفزة للأردنيين في ظل تواجد المنتخبين في مجموعة واحدة بالمونديال، إلى جانب كل من الأرجنتين والنمسا، كما تضع هذه التصريحات ضغطا إضافيا على اللقاء، خاصة وأن المنتخب الأردني يقوده الإطار المغربي جمال سلامي، الذي يسعى للرد في الميدان على التقليل من قيمة فريقه الوطني في المحفل العالمي. ‫‫من شروط النشر : عدم الإساءة للكاتب أو للأشخاص أو للمقدسات أو مهاجمة الأديان أو الذات الإلهية، والابتعاد عن التحريض العنصري والشتائم‬.', 'https://www.hesport.com/%d8%b2%d9%83%d8%b1%d9%8a-%d9%8a%d9%82%d9%84%d9%84-%d9%85%d9%86-%d8%b4%d8%a3%d9%86-%d9%85%d9%86%d8%aa%d8%ae%d8%a8-%d8%b3%d9%84%d8%a7%d9%85%d9%8a-437272.html', NULL, '2026-05-03 14:25:23', '2026-05-03 14:25:23', 'Football', 1, 5, 'ar', 'https://i1.hesport.com/wp-content/overlay/2026/05/IMG-20260503-WA0000.jpg?v2', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 9),
(128, 'المغرب التطواني ينتقد قرارات تحكيمية', 'عبر المكتب المديري لنادي المغرب أتلتيك تطوان عن استنكاره الشديد للمستوى التحكيمي الذي شهدته مباراته أمام رجاء بني ملال، برسم الجولة 23 من البطولة الاحترافية في قسمها الثاني. وأكد النادي في بلاغ رسمي أن المواجهة عرفت قرارات “غير مفهومة” أثرت بشكل مباشر على النتيجة النهائية وحرمت الفريق من حقوقه المشروعة. وأوضح “الماط” أن الطاقم التحكيمي ارتكب هفوات مؤثرة، أبرزها إلغاء هدف مشروع بداعي تسلل غير صحيح، والحرمان من ضربة جزاء واضحة. واعتبر الفريق التطواني أن هذه القرارات ضربت مبادئ العدالة الرياضية وتكافؤ الفرص في مقتل، خاصة وأنها تكررت بشكل يثير التساؤلات من نفس الطاقم الذي أدار مباراة سابقة للفريق في الدورة 15. وشدد البلاغ على أن غياب تقنية المساعدة بالفيديو (VAR) وعدم النقل التلفزيوني لمباريات القسم الثاني، يزيد من خطورة هذه التجاوزات ويفتح الباب أمام أخطاء تؤثر على مصداقية المنافسة. وأشار النادي إلى أنه ظل يلتزم الصمت والمسؤولية في فترات سابقة، لكن تمادي الأخطاء التحكيمية فرض عليه الخروج لتنوير الرأي العام. واختتم المغرب التطواني بلاغه بالإعلان عن تقديم شكاية رسمية إلى مديرية التحكيم، مطالباً بفتح تحقيق جدي ومستعجل في ملابسات المباراة. كما أكد النادي تشبثه بسلوك كافة المساطر القانونية المتاحة للدفاع عن مصالحه وضمان احترام نزاهة البطولة، في ظل التحديات التي تواجه الفريق في سباق المنافسة. ‫‫من شروط النشر : عدم الإساءة للكاتب أو للأشخاص أو للمقدسات أو مهاجمة الأديان أو الذات الإلهية، والابتعاد عن التحريض العنصري والشتائم‬.', 'https://www.hesport.com/%d8%a7%d9%84%d9%85%d8%ba%d8%b1%d8%a8-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%aa%d8%b7%d9%88%d8%a7%d9%86%d9%8a-%d9%8a%d9%86%d8%aa%d9%82%d8%af-%d9%82%d8%b1%d8%a7%d8%b1%d8%a7%d8%aa-%d8%aa%d8%ad%d9%83%d9%8a%d9%85%d9%8a%d8%a9-437280.html', NULL, '2026-05-03 14:25:23', '2026-05-03 14:25:23', 'Football', 1, 5, 'ar', 'https://i1.hesport.com/wp-content/overlay/2026/05/FB_IMG_1777770650853_copy_800x533.jpg?v2', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 9),
(129, 'مزراوي يتحول إلى \"قدوة تكتيكية\" لمواهب مانشستر يونايتد الشابة', 'يحظى الدولي المغربي نصير مزراوي بإشادة جديدة داخل أروقة مانشستر يونايتد، بعدما شبّهت تقارير إنجليزية أحد أبرز مواهب أكاديمية النادي بالنجم المغربي، بالنظر إلى تشابه أسلوب لعبهما وقدرتهما على شغل أكثر من مركز. ووفق ما أورده موقع “يونايتد إن فوكوس”، فإن الموهبة الصاعدة يويل هيلافو بات يُلقب داخل الفئات السنية بـ”مزراوي 2.0″، بفضل مرونته التكتيكية وجودته الفنية، وهي الخصائص نفسها التي جعلت نصير مزراوي من العناصر المهمة في تشكيلة “الشياطين الحمر”. وأشار المصدر ذاته إلى أن إدارة مانشستر يونايتد والمدربين في الأكاديمية يثقون كثيرًا في هيلافو، إذ يحرصون على تطويره في مركز الظهير الأيمن، على غرار الدور الذي يؤديه النجم المغربي مع الفريق الأول. وأضاف التقرير أن أسلوب لعب نصير مزراوي، القائم على الذكاء التكتيكي والقدرة على بناء اللعب من الخلف، أصبح نموذجًا تحتذي به بعض مواهب النادي، وهو ما يفسر المقارنات المتزايدة بينه وبين اللاعب الشاب. كما أكد المصدر أن المدرب مايكل كاريك أبدى إعجابه بتطور هيلافو، الذي تدرب أكثر من مرة مع الفريق الأول، وسط توقعات بحصوله على فرصة الصعود مستقبلًا، خاصة مع حاجة النادي إلى لاعبين يملكون مرونة تكتيكية شبيهة بخصال مزراوي. وختم التقرير بالإشارة إلى أن وجود لاعبين بمواصفات نصير مزراوي يمنح مانشستر يونايتد حلولًا متعددة، سواء في مركز الظهير أو في الأدوار الدفاعية المتقدمة، وهو ما جعل النجم المغربي مرجعًا فنيًا داخل النادي. ‫‫من شروط النشر : عدم الإساءة للكاتب أو للأشخاص أو للمقدسات أو مهاجمة الأديان أو الذات الإلهية، والابتعاد عن التحريض العنصري والشتائم‬.', 'https://www.hesport.com/%d9%85%d8%b2%d8%b1%d8%a7%d9%88%d9%8a-%d9%8a%d8%aa%d8%ad%d9%88%d9%84-%d8%a5%d9%84%d9%89-%d9%82%d8%af%d9%88%d8%a9-%d8%aa%d9%83%d8%aa%d9%8a%d9%83%d9%8a%d8%a9-%d9%84%d9%85%d9%88%d8%a7%d9%87%d8%a8-437309.html', NULL, '2026-05-03 14:25:23', '2026-05-03 14:25:23', 'Football', 1, 10, 'ar', 'https://i1.hesport.com/wp-content/overlay/2026/05/IMG-20260503-WA0002.jpg?v2', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 9),
(130, 'Man United beats Liverpool 3-2 and will be back in the Champions League after 2-year absence', 'Manchester United’s Matheus Cunha celebrates after scoring his side’s opening goal during the English Premier League soccer match between Manchester United and Liverpool in Manchester, England, Sunday, May 3, 2026. (AP Photo/Dave Thompson) Manchester United’s Benjamin Sesko celebrates after scoring his side’s second goal during the English Premier League soccer match between Manchester United and Liverpool in Manchester, England, Sunday, May 3, 2026. (AP Photo/Dave Thompson) Liverpool’s Cody Gakpo celebrates after scoring his side’s second goal during the English Premier League soccer match between Manchester United and Liverpool in Manchester, England, Sunday, May 3, 2026. (AP Photo/Dave Thompson) Manchester United’s Kobbie Mainoo celebrates after scoring his side’s third goal during the English Premier League soccer match between Manchester United and Liverpool in Manchester, England, Sunday, May 3, 2026. (AP Photo/Dave Thompson) MANCHESTER, England (AP) — Manchester United guaranteed a return to the Champions League next season with a 3-2 win against Liverpool on Sunday. Kobbie Mainoo settled a thrilling Premier League clash at Old Trafford with his first-time strike from the edge of the area. Defending champion Liverpool had fought back from two goals down to level the game. But Mainoo’s goal meant United would again be playing in European club soccer’s top competition after a two-year absence. To the delight of its fans, United also completed a league double of home-and-away wins against Liverpool for the first time since the 2015-16 campaign. Victory saw Michael Carrick achieve the target he was set when in January he was handed the role of head coach until the end of the season. Rescuing United’s season from freefall, he has led the club to third in the standings and produced statement wins against Arsenal, Manchester City and now Liverpool. Matheus Cunha put United ahead after six minutes with a left-footed strike from inside the box and Benjamin Sesko doubled the lead in the 14th when bundling in from close range. United’s dominance should have produced more goals with Bruno Fernandes wasting a good chance to add a third. But the game was turned on its head after the break as Dominik Szoboszlai pulled one back for Liverpool two minutes into the second half and then a mix-up in United’s defense allowed Cody Gakpo to equalize in the 56th. Bournemouth earlier strengthened its unlikely push for Champions League qualification with a 3-0 win against Crystal Palace. Bournemouth is sixth in the standings, with the top five guaranteed to qualify for the Champions League. That could be extended to the top six if Aston Villa wins the Europa League and finishes fifth.', 'https://apnews.com/article/man-united-liverpool-champions-league-premier-league-36b8cf3b8351046da6d13d9edc2a62ce', NULL, '2026-05-03 18:03:00', '2026-05-03 18:03:00', 'Football', 1, 57, 'en', 'https://dims.apnews.com/dims4/default/c915a09/2147483647/strip/true/crop/3048x2031+0+1/resize/980x653!/quality/90/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fassets.apnews.com%2F1b%2Fff%2Fe781af38f8cb54ae289ea86079c2%2F1cccbba0ccfd41a3921367c299d23e13', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 2),
(131, 'DIRECT. Espanyol-Real Madrid: suivez le match de la 34e journée de Liga en live', 'Après un passage à Paris, Kylian Mbappé s’est rendu à Cagliari, en Sardaigne, en compagnie d’Ester Exposito comme le montrent plusieurs vidéos devenues virales sur les réseaux sociaux. Une escapade qui n’est pas du goût de nombreux supporters du Real Madrid alors que leur buteur, victime d’une blessure musculaire, est en convalescence. Le FC Barcelone pourrait être sacré champion d\'Espagne dès ce dimanche, en cas de défaite du Real Madrid contre l\'Espanyol Barcelone. Entraîneur du Barça, Hansi Flick s\'est amusé à indiquer qu\'il comptait assister à un spectacle avec sa femme plutôt que de regarder ce match potentiellement décisif. Vainqueur d\'Osasuna ce samedi (2-1), le Barça se rapproche un peu plus du titre en Liga. Ce dernier peut être officiel dès ce dimanche. Tout dépendra du résultat du Real Madrid sur la pelouse... de l\'Espanyol Barcelone. Si le club de la capitale ne gagne pas dimanche sur le terrain de l\'Espanyol, le Barça sera mathématiquement titré, à quatre journées de la fin. En revanche si le Real s\'impose dimanche, la prochaine occasion pour le Barça d\'être titré serait lors du clasico face aux Merengue, prévu le 10 mai au Camp Nou. Bienvenue sur le site et l\'appli RMC Sport pour suivre le match de la 34e journée de Liga entre l\'Espanyol Barcelone et le Real Madrid. Le coup d\'envoi sera donné à 21h.', 'https://rmcsport.bfmtv.com/football/liga/direct-espanyol-real-madrid-suivez-le-match-de-la-34e-journee-de-liga-en-live_LS-202605030253.html', NULL, '2026-05-03 18:03:00', '2026-05-03 18:03:00', 'Football', 1, 69, 'fr', 'https://images.bfmtv.com/A6dxZ4UZUWQRylIXMnjTqgrPZs8=/0x0:0x0/80x0/sport/equipes/football-177_1.png', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 6),
(132, 'Un nouveau classique au sommet: le Barça rejoint l\'OL Lyonnes en finale de la Ligue des champions', 'Le FC Barcelone s\'est imposé dimanche après-midi 4 à 2 contre le Bayern Munich en demi-finale retour de la Ligue des champions féminine, rejoignant l\'OL Lyonnes en finale, qui aura lieu le 23 mai au stade Ullevaal d\'Oslo. Accrochées à l\'aller la semaine dernière sur la pelouse de l\'Allianz Arena (1-1), les coéquipières d\'Alexia Putellas sont difficilement venues à bout des Munichoises, grâce à des buts de Salma Paralluelo (13e), Putellas (22e, 58e), et Ewa Pajor (55e), devant les 60.021 spectateurs du Camp Nou. Les Barcelonaises disputeront leur septième finale de la Ligue des champions sur les huit dernières éditions (élimination en demi-finales en 2020), et viseront un quatrième sacre européen après 2021, 2023 et 2024. Depuis 2019, ce sera la quatrième finale entre les Lyonnaises, octuples championnes d\'Europe (2011, 2012, 2016-2020 et 2022), et les Barcelonaises. Les coéquipières de Putellas ont dominé la rencontre sur les ailes, à droite avec Graham Hansen et à gauche avec Paralluelo. L\'ouverture du score est venue d\'un centre parfait de Graham, qui a trouvé Paralluelo au second poteau (13e). Surprises sur un contre munichois initié par Pernille Harder et conclu par Linda Dallmann (1-1, 17e), les Barcelonaises ont rapidement repris les commandes du match par Putellas (22e), qui a profité d\'un cafouillage sur un centre de Paralluelo.En seconde période, Paralluelo a une nouvelle fois servi un centre parfait pour Ewa Pajor (3-1, 55e). Et Putellas a donné trois buts d\'avance au Barça trois minutes plus tard (4-1, 58e). Les Munichoises ont repris espoir dans les vingt dernières minutes avec Harder (4-2, 71e), en vain malgré des tirs d\'Arianna Caruso (79e) et Dallmann (82e) sur la barre transversale de Cata Coll. A la 68e minute, Aitana Bonmati a effectué son retour sous les ovations du public du Camp Nou, un peu plus de cinq mois après sa fracture du péroné gauche. Un retour à point nommé pour la triple lauréate du Ballon d\'Or (2023, 2024, 2025), à trois semaines de la finale contre l\'OL Lyonnes.', 'https://rmcsport.bfmtv.com/football/feminin/ligue-des-champions/un-nouveau-classique-au-sommet-le-barca-rejoint-l-ol-lyonnes-en-finale-de-la-ligue-des-champions_AD-202605030272.html', NULL, '2026-05-03 18:03:00', '2026-05-03 18:03:00', 'Football', 1, 97, 'fr', 'https://images.bfmtv.com/IxlZ6KkzyVzIwxjvXtPIOqChuB4=/0x0:2048x1152/images/Alexia-Putellas-lors-de-la-demi-finale-retour-de-Ligue-des-champions-entre-le-Barca-et-le-Bayern-le-3-mai-2026-2279958.jpg', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 6);
INSERT INTO `articles` (`id`, `title`, `content`, `url`, `author`, `published_at`, `collected_at`, `sport_category`, `sport_id`, `importance_score`, `langue`, `image_url`, `nb_mots`, `status`, `sentiment`, `metadata`, `source_id`) VALUES
(133, 'Brilliant Bordeaux end Bath\'s Champions Cup hopes', 'Tries: Gazzotti (2), Bielle-Biarrey (15), Lucu (35), Tameifuna (69), Matiu (77) Conversions: Lucu (3,16,36,70,78) Penalties: Lucu (41) Tries: Muir (7,27), Hennessey (51), Carr-Smith (81) Conversions: Russell (8,52,82) Bath came up against an inspired Bordeaux as their Investec Champions Cup campaign ended in a 38-26 semi-final defeat at Stade Atlantique Bordeaux Metropole. The English champions were chasing Bordeaux from the moment they leaked an early try, with their opponents showing a ruthless streak when converting their chances. Wing Will Muir scored two tries, one of them a sublime finish, and Louie Hennessey added a third to keep the game alive in the final quarter, but they made too many mistakes. Bordeaux were worthy winners and they advance to the final in Bilbao on May 23 when they will look to retain their title. Kick-off was delayed by 10 minutes to allow fans to get into the stadium and Bath appeared to be caught cold when their line was breached after just 110 seconds, their lack of outside defence exploited through Damian Penaud before Marko Gazzotti arrived to crash over. England scrum-half Ben Spencer was at the heart of the response as he delivered kicks to each wing, the second picking out Muir who was presented with a simple run in. Bath were exposed out wide again as Louis Bielle-Biarrey struck in the left corner but it was a line-out drive a phase earlier that had really softened up the defence. Alfie Barbeary was prominent as Bath pounded the home whitewash but when they scored their second try it was through the handling of their backs and a clever run by Henry Arundell followed by a superb diving finish by Muir. There was no sign of the breathless pace letting up as lethal Bordeaux struck again with Maxime Lucu the scorer after the ball had been kept alive brilliantly as Bath ran out of defenders. The final act of the first half was Lucu landing a penalty to establish a 24-12 lead and Bath were in danger of being cut adrift, but Hennessey struck back for Bath as he side-stepped over, ignoring the overlap outside him. Charlie Ewels was shown a yellow card for pulling down the maul and Bath finally cracked when giant prop Ben Tameifuna surged over in the 69th minute before Temo Matiu and Tom Carr-Smith exchanged late tries. Follow Sky Sports on WhatsApp for the latest sports news, videos, features, analysis and much more \"We are gutted,\" fly-half Finn Russell said. \"We went behind, fought ourselves back, and didn\'t take our chances. And gave them soft entries into our 22 … at this level, you give soft penalties away and make silly mistakes, you get punished. \"We\'ll be better for this. there is a lot of frustration and disappointment. But when we come back in tomorrow we\'ll look at it, and how we get ready for Exeter next weekend.\" The Dragons went down fighting as their dream of reaching the Challenge Cup final ended with an 18-12 defeat by Montpellier. Top 14 title challengers Montpellier will face Ulster in the competition\'s showpiece in Bilbao on May 22, but they were left clinging on in the closing stages of their semi-final at Septeo Stadium. Aneurin Owen claimed his second try in the 73rd minute to leave the Dragons, who are positioned third from bottom in the United Rugby Championship, a converted try away from springing a dramatic upset.', 'https://www.skysports.com/rugby-union/bordeaux-beg-vs-bath/report/111164', NULL, '2026-05-03 18:03:00', '2026-05-03 18:03:00', 'Rugby', 4, 37, 'en', 'https://e2.365dm.com/26/05/1600x900/skysports-bordeaux-bath-champions-cup_7238260.jpg', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 7),
(134, 'Mainoo\'s winner for Man Utd sees off Liverpool comeback', 'Report and free match highlights as Kobbie Mainoo’s winner earned Manchester United a 3-2 victory over rivals Liverpool at Old Trafford; Arne Slot’s side had come from two down to level; Three points secure Champions League football for Michael Carrick’s side Kobbie Mainoo scored a dramatic winner for Manchester United as they beat Liverpool 3-2 in an epic Premier League encounter at Old Trafford. Matheus Cunha\'s left-footed shot deflected off the back of Alexis Mac Allister and beyond Freddie Woodman to give United an early lead and when Benjamin Sesko forced home after Bruno Fernandes\' centre was pushed his way by Woodman, it was two. But United squandered the advantage in the second half. Amad Diallo, just on as a substitute, gifted the ball to Dominik Szoboszlai who scored a fine solo goal before Senne Lammens\' poor kick was seized upon with Cody Gakpo levelling the game up. It was anybody\'s game at that point but when the ball fell to Mainoo on the edge of the box he fired hard and low beyond Woodman to win it for United. The youngster, who had been frozen out of the team by Ruben Amorim, stealing the show under Michael Carrick. The victory confirms that United will play in the Champions League next season as they tighten their grip on third spot in the table. Liverpool remain fourth with work to do - and with work for Arne Slot to do to persuade fans he is the man to lead them next season. Man Utd: Lammens (5), Dalot (7), Maguire (7), Heaven (7), Shaw (6), Casemiro (7), Mainoo (8), Fernandes (7), Cunha (8), Mbeumo (6), Sesko (7). Subs: Amad (5), Dorgu (5), Zirkzee (n/a), Yoro (n/a). Liverpool: Woodman (6), Jones (5), Van Dijk (5), Konate (5), Robertson (6), Gravenberch (6), Szoboszlai (8), Mac Allister (5), Frimpong (5), Wirtz (5), Gakpo (7). Subs: Kerkez (6), Ngumoha (6), Chiesa (n/a). Player of the Match: Kobbie Mainoo. Slow-motion replays later indicated that Sesko had got a feather-like touch on the ball with his hand, which will leave Liverpool aggrieved. The initial replays shown during the VAR process did not appear to have this close-up view and the goal was allowed to stand. For the majority of the supporters at Old Trafford, it was a game to savour. Former skipper Roy Keane had told Sky Sports beforehand that the result would \"have a big bearing on whether Michael Carrick will get the job\" - maybe this was his anointment. News of Sir Alex Ferguson falling ill and being taken to hospital before kick-off added poignancy to the occasion. That Carrick has this United playing with the pace and purpose of old is a fitting tribute to his old boss and offers hope for the team\'s future. For Slot, the talk of being in transition remains true and Liverpool were without a trio of forwards who he will feel could have made a difference. But the fear among fans is not the transition itself - it is what the Dutchman is transitioning this Liverpool into. They want to see a side that presses and it was this that sparked their brief comeback. Fans would embrace a Liverpool that tweaked the model established by Jurgen Klopp. A sterile possession game looks a divergence too far. The questions for him will continue.', 'https://www.skysports.com/football/manchester-united-vs-liverpool/report/531476', NULL, '2026-05-03 18:03:00', '2026-05-03 18:03:00', 'Football', 1, 57, 'en', 'https://e0.365dm.com/26/05/1600x900/skysports-kobbie-mainoo-premier-league_7238249.jpg?20260503171445', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 7),
(135, 'مانشستر يونايتد يهزم ليفربول بثلاثية مثيرة ويعود رسميا لدوري الأبطال', 'واصل مانشستر يونايتد نتائجه الرائعة في بطولة الدوري الإنجليزي الممتاز لكرة القدم، بعدما تمكن من إفساد (ريمونتادا) ضيفه وغريمه التقليدي ليفربول في قمة مباريات المرحلة الـ35 للمسابقة. وتقدم مانشستر يونايتد بهدفين نظيفين في أقل من ربع ساعة، حيث افتتح البرازيلي ماثيوس كونيا التسجيل في الدقيقة السادسة، وأضاف زميله السلوفيني بنيامين سيسكو الهدف الثاني في الدقيقة 14. وانتفض ليفربول في الشوط الثاني، ليتمكن من تحقيق الريمونتادا، بعدما سجل المجري دومينيك سوبوسلاي والهولندي كودي غاكبو الهدفين الأول والثاني للفريق الضيف في الدقيقتين 47 و56 على الترتيب. وجاء هدف الفوز لمانشستر يونايتد عن طريق نجمه الواعد كوبي ماينو في الدقيقة 77، ليؤكد الفريق الملقب بـ(الشياطين الحمر) عودته رسميا للمشاركة ببطولة دوري أبطال أوروبا في الموسم المقبل. وارتفع رصيد مانشستر يونايتد، الذي حقق انتصاره الثالث على التوالي في المسابقة، إلى 64 نقطة في المركز الثالث، فيما توقف رصيد ليفربول، الذي غاب عنه النجم الدولي المصري محمد صلاح بسبب الإصابة، عند 58 نقطة في المركز الرابع. ‫‫من شروط النشر : عدم الإساءة للكاتب أو للأشخاص أو للمقدسات أو مهاجمة الأديان أو الذات الإلهية، والابتعاد عن التحريض العنصري والشتائم‬.', 'https://www.hesport.com/%d9%85%d8%a7%d9%86%d8%b4%d8%b3%d8%aa%d8%b1-%d9%8a%d9%88%d9%86%d8%a7%d9%8a%d8%aa%d8%af-%d9%8a%d9%87%d8%b2%d9%85-%d9%84%d9%8a%d9%81%d8%b1%d8%a8%d9%88%d9%84-%d8%a8%d8%ab%d9%84%d8%a7%d8%ab%d9%8a%d8%a9-437327.html', NULL, '2026-05-03 18:03:00', '2026-05-03 18:03:00', 'Football', 1, 10, 'ar', 'https://i1.hesport.com/wp-content/overlay/2026/05/manu.jpg?v2', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 9),
(136, 'بن شرقي يقترب من البقاء بالأهلي', 'ارتفعت أسهم الدولي المغربي أشرف بن شرقي في الاستمرار رفقة النادي الأهلي المصري خلال الموسم الكروي المقبل، في ظل المستويات الجيدة التي بصم عليها كلما حصل على فرصة المشاركة، وآخرها تألقه في مباراة القمة أمام الزمالك. وساهم بن شرقي بشكل بارز في فوز فريقه بثلاثية نظيفة، بعدما سجل هدفين وقدم تمريرة حاسمة، ما أعاد النقاش داخل أروقة الأهلي بخصوص مستقبله، خاصة في ظل تقييم الإدارة لمردود اللاعبين الأجانب. ووفق معطيات أوردها موقع “اليوم السابع” المصري، فإن مسؤولي الأهلي ناقشوا في الآونة الأخيرة وضعية بن شرقي، الذي انضم إلى الفريق في يناير 2025 قادماً من الريان القطري في صفقة انتقال حر، حيث نال إشادة عدد من المسؤولين الذين يرون أنه يقدم الإضافة المطلوبة عند إشراكه. ويُجمع عدد من المتابعين داخل النادي على أن اللاعب يتوفر على إمكانيات تقنية وحلول فردية قادرة على صناعة الفارق، وهو ما تجلى بوضوح في مباراة “الديربي”، بينما تبقى مسألة توظيفه بشكل منتظم مسؤولية الطاقم التقني. في المقابل، ارتبط اسم بن شرقي ببعض العروض الخليجية، خاصة من الدوري القطري، غير أن مصدراً من داخل الأهلي نفى توصل النادي بأي عرض رسمي، مؤكداً أن التوجه الحالي يميل إلى الحفاظ على خدمات اللاعب، علماً أن عقده يمتد إلى غاية صيف سنة 2027. ‫‫من شروط النشر : عدم الإساءة للكاتب أو للأشخاص أو للمقدسات أو مهاجمة الأديان أو الذات الإلهية، والابتعاد عن التحريض العنصري والشتائم‬.', 'https://www.hesport.com/%d8%a8%d9%86-%d8%b4%d8%b1%d9%82%d9%8a-%d9%8a%d9%82%d8%aa%d8%b1%d8%a8-%d9%85%d9%86-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%a8%d9%82%d8%a7%d8%a1-%d8%a8%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%a3%d9%87%d9%84%d9%8a-437312.html', NULL, '2026-05-03 18:03:00', '2026-05-03 18:03:00', 'Football', 1, 5, 'ar', 'https://i1.hesport.com/wp-content/overlay/2026/05/IMG_20260503_150607_copy_800x533.jpg?v2', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 9),
(137, 'غيابات في صفوف الرجاء والدفاع الجديدي في مواجهة الجولة 18 من البطولة', 'عرفت قائمة نادي الرجاء الرياضي، التي وجهها المدرب الجنوب إفريقي فادلو ديفيز، غيابات بارزة قبل مواجهة نادي الدفاع الحسني الجديدي، مساء اليوم الأحد، ضمن منافسات الجولة الـ18 من البطولة الاحترافية. وواصل مدرب الفريق الأخضر استبعاد كل من عثمان الشرايبي، وأيوب المعموري، وصابر بوكرين، وعثمان ساخو، مقابل إعادة عبد الكريم باعدي وموسى كونتي إلى اللائحة المستدعاة للمباراة. وضمت قائمة الرجاء كلا من المهدي الحرار، خالد العلوي، عبد الله خفيفي، إسماعيل مقدم، مهدي مشخشخ، بدر بانون، أمين خماس، محمد بولكسوت، أيوب العملود، عبد الكريم باعدي، حليمي بيصار، أيمن برقوق، موسى كونتي، محمد المكعازي، هلال الفردوسي، آدم النفاتي، معاد الضحاك، محمد أبو زريق “شرارة”، إسماعيل خافي، وماتياس أويوسي. في المقابل، يحل الدفاع الحسني الجديدي ضيفا على الرجاء منقوصا من خدمات اثنين من ركائزه الأساسية، ويتعلق الأمر بمعاد مشتنم، الذي سيغيب بسبب الطرد الذي تعرض له في المباراة الماضية أمام نهضة بركان، إضافة إلى المدافع أشرف الإدريسي الموقوف لتراكم الإنذارات. وستجرى المواجهة على أرضية مركب محمد الخامس بمدينة الدار البيضاء، انطلاقا من الساعة السابعة مساء، بدون حضور جماهيري، تنفيذا لعقوبة “الويكلو” المفروضة على الرجاء عقب أحداث الشغب التي رافقت مباراة الكلاسيكو أمام الجيش الملكي. ‫‫من شروط النشر : عدم الإساءة للكاتب أو للأشخاص أو للمقدسات أو مهاجمة الأديان أو الذات الإلهية، والابتعاد عن التحريض العنصري والشتائم‬.', 'https://www.hesport.com/%d8%ba%d9%8a%d8%a7%d8%a8%d8%a7%d8%aa-%d9%81%d9%8a-%d8%b5%d9%81%d9%88%d9%81-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%b1%d8%ac%d8%a7%d8%a1-%d9%88%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%af%d9%81%d8%a7%d8%b9-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%ac%d8%af%d9%8a%d8%af%d9%8a-437322.html', NULL, '2026-05-03 18:03:00', '2026-05-03 18:03:00', 'Football', 1, 10, 'ar', 'https://i1.hesport.com/wp-content/overlay/2026/05/rd.jpg?v2', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 9),
(138, 'Joel Embiid wants 76ers fans at Philadelphia games. The Knicks know that New Yorkers are coming', 'Philadelphia 76ers’ Joel Embiid reacts during the first half of Game 4 against the Boston Celtics in a first-round NBA basketball playoffs series Sunday, April 26, 2026, in Philadelphia. (AP Photo/Matt Slocum) New York Knicks guard Josh Hart (3) reacts after making a 3-point basket in the final minute of an NBA basketball game against the Boston Celtics, Thursday, April 9, 2026, in New York. (AP Photo/John Munson) The 76ers and Knicks begin the Eastern Conference semifinals on Monday at Madison Square Garden, which is expected to be packed with Knicks fans, from the celebrities in the front row all the way to the die-hards way up top. Both teams already are looking ahead to what happens when the series moves to Philadelphia for Games 3 and 4. When they met two years ago in the first round, Knicks fans swarmed Philadelphia and Embiid pleaded with fans not to let it happen again. “Last time we played the Knicks it felt like this was Madison Square Garden East. So we’re going to need the support,” Embiid said. “Don’t sell your tickets. This is bigger than you. We need you guys. The atmosphere we’ve had the last couple games in Philly, especially the last one pushing it to Game 7, I mean, we need all of it.” The 76ers are trying to do their part. A message on their website reads: “Xfinity Mobile Arena is located in Philadelphia, PA. Sales to this event will be restricted to residents of Greater Philadelphia area. Residency will be based on credit card billing address. Orders by residents outside Greater Philadelphia area will be canceled without notice and refunds given.” Even if that works, there’s nothing that can prevent big-spending backers of the Knicks from buying from Philadelphia fans who choose to sell. “Good thing about New Yorkers, man, they’re persistent. They don’t care, bro. They’re going to do it, man,” Knicks forward Josh Hart said. “And for a lot of people, everything revolves around money. So, you know, if they get a good price for those tickets, they’re going to sell them.” Hart, who played in college at Villanova, noted that it’s less than a two-hour drive from New York to Philadelphia — even quicker by train — and that it’s likely far cheaper to buy tickets for the road games. Embiid was disappointed in 76ers fans during the 2024 series, when Jalen Brunson received raucous “MVP! MVP!” chants while scoring 47 points as the Knicks won Game 4 in Philadelphia. Embiid said afterward that: “I don’t think that should happen. It’s not OK.” Sixers owners then bought and gave away more than 2,000 tickets to people who serve the Philadelphia community when the Knicks returned for Game 6. “Knicks fans, they travel,” he said. “There’s going to be some people that need the money and probably going to sell tickets, but don’t do it. We need you guys. We’ve got a pretty good chance. We’re going to need our support. We’re going to need them to be extremely loud and if you need money, I got you.”', 'https://apnews.com/article/knicks-76ers-tickets-embiid-playoffs-ab45df2f208f5fcb186a1c67b2d17051', NULL, '2026-05-03 20:31:54', '2026-05-03 20:31:54', 'Basketball', 2, 29, 'en', 'https://dims.apnews.com/dims4/default/408ee58/2147483647/strip/true/crop/5434x3621+0+1/resize/980x653!/quality/90/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fassets.apnews.com%2F90%2Ff6%2Ff7a00ae4ecea237e5066ca71a69e%2Fae286c3083484765832fe64baf7f9490', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 2),
(139, 'Kimi Antonelli wins the Miami Grand Prix for his third straight F1 victory', 'Mohammed Ben Sulayem President of the Federation Internationale de l’Automobile (FIA) pours water on the head of Mercedes driver Kimi Antonelli of Italy after Antonelli won the Miami Formula One Grand Prix auto race, Sunday, May 3, 2026, in Miami Gardens, Fla. (AP Photo/Rebecca Blackwell) Mercedes driver Kimi Antonelli of Italy celebrates after winning the Miami Formula One Grand Prix auto race, Sunday, May 3, 2026, in Miami Gardens, Fla. (AP Photo/Rebecca Blackwell) Mercedes driver Kimi Antonelli of Italy finishes first in the Miami Formula One Grand Prix auto race, Sunday, May 3, 2026, in Miami Gardens, Fla. (AP Photo/Rebecca Blackwell, Pool) Mercedes driver Kimi Antonelli of Italy holds his trophy after winning the Miami Formula One Grand Prix auto race, Sunday, May 3, 2026, in Miami Gardens, Fla. (AP Photo/Lynne Sladky) Mercedes driver Kimi Antonelli of Italy celebrates after winning the Miami Formula One Grand Prix auto race, Sunday, May 3, 2026, in Miami Gardens, Fla. (AP Photo/Rebecca Blackwell) MIAMI GARDENS, Fla. (AP) — Kimi Antonelli made history as the first driver to win his first three Formula 1 races from the pole when the 19-year-old Mercedes driver won the Miami Grand Prix on Sunday. It was the third consecutive victory for Antonelli, the current points leader who is proving early this season to be a legitimate championship contender. “It is just the beginning, the road is still long, but we’re working super hard,” Antonelli said. “The team is doing an incredible job and without them I wouldn’t be here. I’m going to enjoy this one and then get back to work.” The Italian and teammate George Russell have won the first four races of this season for Mercedes and all four poles to date. They were blocked from the podium in Saturday’s sprint race, which was a 1-2 finish for Lando Norris and Oscar Piastri of McLaren in the only thing the Mercedes drivers have not won this season. “Kimi, that was very, very impressive. You know I like to complain, but there was nothing to complain about today,” Mercedes boss Toto Wolff told his young driver. “Very good.” Antonelli started from the pole but had a slick start on a damp surface at the Miami International Autodrome. Threats of heavy rain led F1 to move up the start of the race by three hours, and there was an early morning thunderstorm with lightning strikes directly over the Hard Rock Stadium, but it cleared by the time the event began. Still, the first 25 laps were attacked by the drivers as if the rain could return at any moment, and that led to early chaos, even for Antonelli. Charles Leclerc of Ferrari had a spectacular start from third and surged to the lead when Antonelli went wide off course trying to defend. A split-second later, Max Verstappen spun trying to hold off Leclerc when the two cars made contact. Antonelli recovered and reclaimed the lead on the fifth lap, and the leaders briefly swapped positions as Leclerc moved back to the front before reigning world champion Norris took over on Lap 14. Verstappen worked his way through the field and briefly took the lead as others pitted, but Antonelli beat Norris off pit lane and reclaimed the lead for good once everything cycled out. “A mixed bag, really. We just got undercut (in the pits). There’s no excuses other than that,” Norris said. “We should have boxxed first. Kimi did a good job. Hats off to Merc and Kimi. They drove a good race.” Leclerc was poised to finish third until Oscar Piastri of McLaren passed him on the final lap. Leclerc spun and settled for sixth. Russell was fourth and Verstappen finished a season-best fifth for Red Bull. Lewis Hamilton of Ferrari was seventh. Cadillac, in its first race in the United States, had an unimpressive weekend on the track even as it splashed its way through Miami with appearances and events. Sergio Perez finished 16th and Valtteri Bottas was 18th — the last car to finish in the 22-driver field. Isack Hadjar had been disqualified after qualifying and started last, but his race lasted five laps before he drove his Red Bull into the wall. Hadjar was openly angry at the result as he pounded his helmet before climbing from his car and angrily stomping away. Seconds later, Pierre Gasly and Liam Lawson made contact that caused Gasly’s car to do a full rollover. The Frenchman’s car ended stuck with its rear tires atop a barrier and he climbed from the half-suspended BMW on his own. The Canadian Grand Prix is next for F1 at Circuit Gilles Villeneuve in Montreal on May 24. That date was traditionally held by the Monaco Grand Prix but a tweak to the schedule shifted it to Canada, and F1 will no longer be the opener for what had traditionally been the most prolific day in motorsports. The F1 race typically opened the morning ahead of the Indianapolis 500 and then NASCAR’s Coca-Cola 600. Because the race is in Canada and not Monaco, it has a late afternoon start time and will follow the Indy 500 and end during the NASCAR race.', 'https://apnews.com/article/f1-miami-grand-prix-rain-antonelli-6b82cf3af8a4b7bc35289a2de84fde63', NULL, '2026-05-03 20:31:54', '2026-05-03 20:31:54', 'Sports Mécaniques', NULL, 42, 'en', 'https://dims.apnews.com/dims4/default/4fd2700/2147483647/strip/true/crop/4846x3229+0+1/resize/980x653!/quality/90/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fassets.apnews.com%2Fbb%2Fcc%2Fb5037d6bd331b5c15f2e4e8670fb%2Fbe495c06b8b74399beaff84a92abcabe', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 2),
(140, 'DIRECT. Lyon-Rennes: tout va mieux pour les Lyonnais', 'Tolisso donne l’avantage à l’Olympique Lyonnais sur penalty et fait exploser le Groupama Stadium ! 2-1 pour Lyon, qui inscrit deux buts en quelques minutes seulement et renverse totalement la rencontre. Égalisation logique pour l’Olympique Lyonnais, qui multipliait les grosses occasions depuis le début de la rencontre. Le pressing et l’intensité lyonnaise finissent par payer. Quel centre magnifique de Tolisso côté gauche ! Il trouve Yaremchuk dans la surface, qui prend le dessus sur Brassier et trompe Samba. 1-1 entre l’OL et Rennes ! Rennes récupère enfin le ballon et essaie de faire circuler pour se dégager et souffler un peu, après plusieurs minutes étouffantes. Rennes est complètement sous l’eau malgré son avantage d’un but. Les Bretons n’arrivent pas à ressortir le ballon et subissent de plein fouet le très gros pressing de l’OL. Rennes est en difficulté dans la relance. Depuis l’ouverture du score signée Al Tamari, c’est l’Olympique Lyonnais qui dicte le rythme de la rencontre et multiplie les occasions. Nouvelle tentative d’Afonso Moreira à 25 mètres, plein axe, mais le ballon passe de peu à côté. Lyon continue de pousser fort. La frappe d’Endrick passe finalement au-dessus, mais elle se rapproche dangereusement des cages de Samba et de Rennes. L’OL monte en puissance. Le centre de Morton à destination d’Endrick est trop long et file directement en sortie de but. L’Olympique Lyonnais continue néanmoins de tenter sa chance et de mettre du rythme dans cette rencontre. Rennes subit la pression exercée par le pressing haut des Lyonnais, de plus en plus intense. Les Bretons peinent à ressortir proprement le ballon. Le meilleur buteur de Ligue 1 avec 18 buts vient percuter Mata violemment par derrière alors qu\'il avait perdu le ballon. Il était hors jeu en plus de ça. L’Olympique Lyonnais s’appuie sur sa vitesse sur les ailes, notamment à gauche avec Afonso Moreira pour multiplier les centres. Mais les Gones manquent de présence et de poids dans la surface rennaise pour concrétiser leurs offensives. Camara arrive très en retard et fauche le jeune lyonnais par derrière. Coup franc à 35 mètres sur le côté droit mais pas de carton. Brice Samba s’interpose sur un centre dangereux, alors que Moreira fait des différences sur son côté gauche. Lyon continue de pousser et obtient un nouveau corner. Lyon accentue la pression sur Rennes et obtient un nouveau corner. Les Lyonnais évoluent désormais très haut depuis plusieurs minutes, et mettent la défense rennaise sous tension. Rennes évolue très haut en phase offensive. Tout le bloc rennais se projette pour exercer une pression constante sur l’Olympique Lyonnais. Lyon vient d’être cueilli à froid par Rennes avec ce but d’Al Tamari. L’OL va devoir réagir rapidement pour revenir au score. Quel bijou ! Al Tamari expédie une reprise de volée magistrale au fond des filets lyonnais. Le Jordanien inscrit là son sixième but de la saison. Plus de peur que de mal pour le capitaine de l\'OL qui peut reprendre sa place mais marqué au niveau du visage. Le Français est conscient mais sacrément secoué. Il va faire un protocole commotion avec les médecins lyonnais. Tous les joueurs de l\'OL et de Rennes entourent Tolisso qui reste encore au sol. Ca semble assez grave. C’est parti au Groupama Stadium ! Monsieur Turpin donne le coup d’envoi de cette affiche de la 32e journée de Ligue 1. L’Olympique Lyonnais engage avec Endrick. Ambiance électrique au Groupama Stadium ! Les Gones entament un clapping impressionnant à quelques instants du coup d’envoi. Le coup d’envoi est imminent au Groupama Stadium, où une superbe ambiance s’est installée pour ce rendez-vous crucial. Derniers ajustements avant ce choc de la 32e journée de Ligue 1 dans la course à la qualification en Ligue des champions. Samba – Merlin, Brassier, Aït-Boudlal, Seidu – Camara, Rongier, Szymanski, Al-Tamari - Embolo, Lepaul Si l\'OL reste sur trois succès en Ligue 1, dont une victoire au Parc des Princes face au PSG (2-1), Rennes affiche la meilleure dynamique sur les 10 dernières journées. Depuis le départ d\'Habib Beye début février, les Bretons ont pris 25 points sur 30 possibles, soit 10 de plus que l\'OL, jusqu\'à s\'inviter dans la lutte pour la troisième place. En septembre dernier au Roazhon Park, l\'OL a rapidement mené 1-0 avant de perdre 3-1, encaissant trois buts dans les dix dernières minutes après l\'exclusion de Tyler Morton, une décision alors contestée par les Lyonnais. En bonne position dans leur quête de qualification directe en Ligue des champions, Lyon et Rennes ne sont séparées que d\'un point à trois journées de la fin. Si Lille a repris un point d\'avance sur l\'OL après son match nul contre Le Havre (1-1), Rennes n\'est qu\'à un point derrière. Bienvenue sur le site et l\'appli RMC Sport pour suivre le dernier match de la 32e journée de Ligue 1 entre Lyon et Rennes. Le coup d\'envoi sera donné à 20h45 au Groupama Stadium.', 'https://rmcsport.bfmtv.com/football/ligue-1/direct-ol-rennes-suivez-le-dernier-match-de-la-32e-journee-de-ligue-1-en-live_LS-202605030250.html', NULL, '2026-05-03 20:31:54', '2026-05-03 20:31:54', 'Football', 1, 99, 'fr', 'https://images.bfmtv.com/J3bQD7nOCaZ_vp77bqQzJnhWNiU=/0x83:2048x1235/images/La-celebration-d-Endrick-apres-son-but-avec-l-OL-3-mai-2026-2280026.jpg', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 6),
(141, '\"J\'entends l\'inquiétude des supporters\": la ministre des Sports souhaite une \"régulation de la multipropriété\" au niveau européen', 'La ministre des Sports, de la Jeunesse et de la Vie associative Marina Ferrari s\'est dite favorable à \"une régulation de la multipropriété mais dans un cadre européen\", à la mi-temps du match entre Strasbourg et Toulouse dimanche après-midi. En déplacement au stade de la Meinau lors de cette rencontre de la 32e journée de Ligue 1, Marina Ferrari a évoqué le sujet de la multipropriété, brûlant à Strasbourg depuis la prise de pouvoir en 2023 du consortium américain BlueCo, également à la tête de Chelsea, en Angleterre. Début février, les Ultra Boys 90, principal groupe d\'ultras strasbourgeois, avaient appelé les instances dirigeantes du football à agir contre les \"multiples dérives engendrées par la multipropriété\". Les UB90 demandaient alors d\'éviter que les clubs dans cette situation soient \"relégués au rang d\'équipes nourricières, sans ressources propres, sans âme, sans lien avec leur territoire\", citant en exemple le départ de leur entraîneur Liam Rosenior vers le navire amiral Chelsea en plein milieu de saison. \"J\'entends l\'inquiétude des supporters parce qu\'elle pourrait poser problème\", a répondu Marina Ferrari. \"Aujourd\'hui, elle se structure, c\'est de plus en plus encadré. (...) Je suis pour une régulation de la multipropriété mais ça doit se faire dans un cadre européen. On voit bien qu\'on a besoin aussi d\'avoir des capitaux qui arrivent dans nos clubs et donc il faut qu\'on arrive à réguler tout ça.\" \"Une régulation seule au niveau français n\'aurait pas de sens, a-t-elle ajouté. J\'ai déjà porté ce message au sein du Conseil de l\'Europe, j\'y retourne le 11 et 12 (mai), je serai également à Bruxelles à nouveau pour aborder ce sujet.\" Sa position diffère de celle du député Éric Coquerel (LFI), qui a déposé en septembre 2025 une proposition de loi visant à interdire la multipropriété des clubs en France. Dix des 18 clubs de Ligue 1 font partie de consortiums internationaux, signe de la domination de ce modèle économique au sein du football français, pris dans une crise financière depuis l\'échec de la vente des droits TV l\'an dernier. \"Il ne faut pas jeter le bébé avec l\'eau du bain\", a poursuivi Marina Ferrari. \"Force est de constater que si on n\'avait pas eu certains investisseurs, on n\'aurait pas pu maintenir des clubs à un certain niveau. Et on sait qu\'aujourd\'hui il faut, et c\'est le cas de Strasbourg qui va jouer ce match très important jeudi (une demi-finale retour de la Ligue Conférence, NDLR), qu\'on ait des clubs qui montent le plus possible au niveau européen.\"', 'https://rmcsport.bfmtv.com/football/j-entends-l-inquietude-des-supporters-la-ministre-des-sports-souhaite-une-regulation-de-la-multipropriete-au-niveau-europeen_AV-202605030314.html', NULL, '2026-05-03 20:31:54', '2026-05-03 20:31:54', 'Football', 1, 47, 'fr', 'https://images.bfmtv.com/2a43EbakaCb7u7a94F_n7gateWM=/0x106:2048x1258/images/La-ministre-des-Sports-Marina-Ferrari-au-micro-de-Ligue-1-3-mai-2026-2279993.jpg', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 6),
(142, 'Korda continues glittering form with dominant Riviera Maya Open win', 'Nelly Korda win the Riviera Maya Open on 17-under to secure her third LPGA Tour win of 2026; Korda has now finished second or better in every tournament she has played since the turn of the year; watch the LPGA Tour live on Sky Sports Nelly Korda has won her third tournament of 2026 and continued her fine form with a fantastic four-shot victory over Arpichaya Yubol at the Riviera Maya Open at Mayakoba. The Chevron Championship winner capped off a brilliant performance with a sumptuous putt on the 18th after a mishap to secure a three-under 69 and a brilliant 17-under over the weekend. Korda has not finished lower than second in any of the six tournaments she has played in since the turn of the year, tying her with Annika Sorenstam as the only other woman to ever achieve that feat. \"I\'m just enjoying myself - I love the competition,\" the world No 1 said after her victory. \"I love travelling to places like Mexico and all over the world. I\'m just having fun. \"You put the same amount of work in every time - you just never know - it\'s golf! I was humbled at the last hole, I had a pretty smooth day otherwise. \"Everyone out here puts in the work - I\'m so thankful to have such a great team around me. We all are super motivated and just happy to be out here.\" Thailand\'s Yubol was not able to match Saturday\'s stunning 66 and finished on a two-under 70 for the day, leaving her unable to mount a substantial challenge to Korda. Futher down the leaderboard, England\'s Jodi Ewart Shadoff had a fine afternoon, finishing three-under and matching Korda\'s 69 to finish tied sixth on the weekend with Spain\'s Carlota Ciganda. The LPGA Tour heads to Mountain Ridge in Michigan next week for the this week for the Mizuho Americas Open, with all four rounds live on Sky Sports. Stream the LPGA Tour with no contract here.', 'https://www.skysports.com/golf/news/12040/13539881/lpga-tour-nelly-korda-wins-third-tournament-of-2026-with-dominant-performance-at-riviera-maya-open', NULL, '2026-05-03 20:31:54', '2026-05-03 20:31:54', 'Football', 1, 42, 'en', 'https://e0.365dm.com/26/05/1600x900/skysports-nelly-korda-mexico-riviera-maya-open_7238516.jpg?20260503201149', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 7),
(143, 'Antonelli holds off Norris in Miami thriller to extend title lead', 'Kimi Antonelli claims third successive race win to extend world championship lead to 20 points; Lando Norris second and Oscar Piastri third as McLaren claim double podium; George Russell salvages fourth to limit title-battle damage after two late passes Kimi Antonelli beat Lando Norris to victory in a thrilling Miami Grand Prix to claim his third successive race win and extend his world championship lead to 20 points. As had been the case in his previous two victories, Antonelli was unable to hold the lead from pole position as he dropped to third in the early stages, but the Mercedes driver regained the lead by pulling off an undercut at the only round of pit stops, overtaking Norris as they went wheel-to-wheel at the pit exit before holding off the McLaren in a tense finale. The 19-year-old Italian becomes just the third driver to have claimed his first three Grand Prix victories consecutively, following in the footsteps of former world champions Damon Hill and Mika Hakkinen. Antonelli\'s team-mate George Russell was able to limit the damage on a weekend where he was never able to match the Italian\'s pace, passing Red Bull\'s Max Verstappen and Ferrari\'s Charles Leclerc in a chaotic finale to claim fourth, meaning the gap between the Mercedes pair at the top of the standings grew from seven to 20 points. Oscar Piastri also passed Leclerc on the penultimate lap to seal a double podium for McLaren, completing a solid weekend for the reigning constructors\' champions after Norris led a one-two for them in Saturday\'s Sprint as their major upgrade package resulted in a significant upturn. Verstappen, also enjoying more speed from Red Bull\'s considerable upgrade package, had to settle for fifth after an uncharacteristic spin at the start saw him drop back from second on the grid and opt to pit under an early Safety Car, leaving him fighting to hang onto his aged hard tyres in the closing stages. Leclerc, who took the lead at the start but had his race ruined by a slow pit stop, spun and hit the barrier as he tried to fight back against Piastri, causing damage to his car which allowed Russell and Verstappen to pass in the final corners. Both Verstappen and Leclerc must await the outcome of post-race investigations before their positions are confirmed. Verstappen could face action for crossing the white line at the pit-lane exit after his stop, and Leclerc for driving in an unsafe condition after his late spin. Lewis Hamilton finished behind his Ferrari team-mate in seventh, as the Italian team\'s own major upgrade package failed to produce its desired effect. Ultimately, the fact that Mercedes were able to make it four victories from as many races this season despite holding off bringing their own major upgrade package until the next round in Canada will be seen as a major triumph for the Silver Arrows, and give them huge confidence that can remain at the head of the field in Montreal. Franco Colapinto claimed seventh for Alpine after his team-mate Pierre Gasly was flipped over following an early collision, while Carlos Sainz and Alex Albon both scored points in an improved display from Williams. Formula 1 next heads to Montreal for the Canadian Grand Prix and another Sprint weekend. Watch live on Sky Sports F1 on May 22-24. Stream Sky Sports with NOW - no contract, cancel anytime', 'https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12040/13539714/miami-gp-kimi-antonelli-holds-off-lando-norris-to-claim-third-successive-win-and-extend-championship-lead', NULL, '2026-05-03 20:31:54', '2026-05-03 20:31:54', 'Sports Mécaniques', NULL, 67, 'en', 'https://e0.365dm.com/26/05/1600x900/skysports-kimi-antonelli-mercedes_7238494.jpg?20260503195423', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 7),
(144, 'Hull slip to disappointing Toulouse defeat in Super League', 'Hull FC miss out on top-half spot after out-of-form Toulouse upset home side; the Black and Whites are ninth in Super League after Toulouse win their first match in eight; Sky Sports is only place to watch every Super League game live in 2026 Hull FC failed to move into the top half of the Betfred Super League table after suffering a disappointing 12-4 defeat to Toulouse. Interim boss Andy Last hoped to capitalise on the win they secured against Castleford Tigers in his first match in charge since becoming caretaker for a second time. Instead, they slipped to a Toulouse side who had suffered seven straight league defeats before their trip to the MKM Stadium. The visitors scored two tries within the first 10 minutes, the first via Olly Ashall-Bott just five minutes in. Joe Cator added a second four minutes later, and Jake Shorrocks successfully booted the extras for a second time. Tom Briscoe got Hull on the board with nine minutes remaining in the first half, but they could not claw back any more points after Zak Hardaker missed the conversion. A more determined Hull emerged in the second half, when they forced the French side to defend resolutely against waves of attack, but could never find the breakthrough. Ashall-Bott ensured the hosts would not narrow the gap with a brilliant clearance under the posts with 15 minutes remaining. Sky Sports will again show every game of the Super League live this season - including two matches in each round exclusively live, with the remaining five matches each week shown on Sky Sports+', 'https://www.skysports.com/rugby-league/news/12040/13539763/hull-fc-4-12-toulouse-black-and-whites-slip-to-super-league-home-defeat-to-struggling-french-side', NULL, '2026-05-03 20:31:54', '2026-05-03 20:31:54', 'Football', 1, 22, 'en', 'https://e0.365dm.com/26/05/1600x900/skysports-hull-fc-tolouse-super-league_7238179.jpg?20260503163858', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 7),
(145, 'الوداد يتلقى الهزيمة الثانية تواليا على يد نهضة الزمامرة بهدف نظيف', 'واصل فريق الوداد سلسلة نتائجه السلبية، بتعرضه لخسارة جديدة أمام نهضة الزمامرة بنتيجة هدف نظيف، برسم الجولة 18 من الدوري الاحترافي، والتي احتضنها ملعب أحمد شكري بالزمامرة. وظهر الفريقان بوجه شاحب في الشوط الأول، إذ لم يعرف محاولات خطيرة من الجانبين، وظلت محتشمة دون أن تشكل أي خطورة على دفاعهما، لتنتهي الفترة الأولى بدون أهداف. في الشوط الثاني تحسن الأداء نسبيا، وحاول الوداد أن يخلف فرصا من أجل تسجيل التقدم، إلا أن الخط الهجومي للفريق لم يشكل خطورة واضحة على شباك الحارس مروان فخر. بدوره، حاول نهضة الزمامرة المبادرة للهجوم معتمدا على خطة الهجمات المرتدة والضربات الثابتة، قبل أن يستفيد من إحداها بهدف سجله رضا أيت بوغيمة في الدقيقة 70 من المباراة. انتظر الجميع استفاقة الوداد بحثا عن هدف التعادل لتفادي الخسارة الثانية على التوالي، كما قام الإطار الوطني محمد بنشريفة القيام ببعض التغييرات في الخط الهجومي، لكن المحاولات باءت بالفشل وتنتهي المباراة بفوز نهضة الزمامرة بهدف نظيف. ‫‫من شروط النشر : عدم الإساءة للكاتب أو للأشخاص أو للمقدسات أو مهاجمة الأديان أو الذات الإلهية، والابتعاد عن التحريض العنصري والشتائم‬.', 'https://www.hesport.com/%d8%a7%d9%84%d9%88%d8%af%d8%a7%d8%af-%d9%8a%d8%aa%d9%84%d9%82%d9%89-%d8%a7%d9%84%d9%87%d8%b2%d9%8a%d9%85%d8%a9-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%ab%d8%a7%d9%86%d9%8a%d8%a9-%d8%aa%d9%88%d8%a7%d9%84%d9%8a%d8%a7-%d8%b9-437335.html', NULL, '2026-05-03 20:31:54', '2026-05-03 20:31:54', 'Football', 1, 10, 'ar', 'https://i1.hesport.com/wp-content/overlay/2026/05/IMG_5830.jpeg?v2', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 9),
(146, 'Spurs move out of relegation zone with crucial victory at Villa', 'Report and free match highlights as Tottenham produced arguably their best performance of the season to beat Aston Villa and move out of the relegation zone; Goals from Conor Gallagher and Richarlison mean Spurs are now one point above 18th-placed West Ham with three games left Tottenham breathed new life into their battle to stay in the Premier League with a 2-1 victory at Champions league-chasing Aston Villa to move out of the relegation zone. West Ham\'s 3-0 defeat at Brentford on Saturday opened the door for Spurs, and Roberto De Zerbi\'s side stepped confidently through it as the battle to beat the drop took a plot twist. Spurs looked a different side under De Zerbi The way they pressed and won back possession all over the pitch was reminiscent of De Zerbi\'s Brighton, giving every indication Spurs will have enough to stay in the top flight next season. Aston Villa, who made seven changes from their Europa League semi-final first leg defeat to Nottingham Forest, were second best from the very first whistle as first-half goals from Conor Gallagher and Richarlison as good as finished the game as a contest. The expected Villa resurgence never came in the second half and despite Emi Buendia\'s stoppage-time header, it was Spurs\' night as they produced arguably their best performance of the season at such a crucial point in the campaign. Spurs, who now have back-to-back wins in the league since their first two games of the season, are now one point above 18th-placed West Ham with three games of the season left to play and favourites to beat the drop, and with a home game to come against Leeds, after the Hammers host Arsenal, their position could be even better next week. While it was Spurs\' best performance of the season, Villa produced their worst display of the campaign, with their attention clearly on Thursday\'s Europa League semi-final second leg against Nottingham Forest. Villa, who stay fifth with a six-point cushion to Bournemouth in sixth, have suffered three straight defeats in all competitions and missed the chance to all but seal a Champions League spot for next season. Unai Emery\'s men now have to produce a response from a lacklustre display to overcome a one-goal deficit against Forest on Thursday. \"We played against Aston Villa and Aston Villa is a very good team, with a lot of very good players and a great manager, but we played very well for 60 minutes, I think, with the ball, without the ball. \"Then we suffered Watkins, we suffered Buendia, we concede a goal. The only bad thing on the pitch was the goal we conceded. \"We could have scored more goals, especially in the first half, but I\'m pleased for this performance from my players. I know how much they suffered this season and for that I\'m very proud.\" On what pleased him the most about Spurs\' performance, he added: \"The high pressure, for sure, because the high pressure is a mentality. Then the possession because we played very, very well, with calm. When we had to attack the space or to go to shoot, we did. When we had to keep the ball, we did. \"I love playing football. Especially if you have these players in the squad, my job is to help them, to put them in the right condition to play, to show what they are capable of doing.\" Spurs midfielder Conor Gallagher to TNT Sports: \"We\'re really happy with the performance and the three points. It\'s been a perfect night but hopefully it\'s just the start. We want to carry it on for the last few games of the season. On the impact of Roberto De Zerbi, he added: \"I can\'t speak highly enough of him. He\'s been so good. Every player in the squad has taken to him; he makes you feel so good. He brings the best out of you.\"', 'https://www.skysports.com/football/aston-villa-vs-tottenham-hotspur/report/531470', NULL, '2026-05-03 21:46:16', '2026-05-03 21:46:16', 'Football', 1, 42, 'en', 'https://e0.365dm.com/26/05/1600x900/skysports-premier-league-spurs_7238452.jpg?20260503191619', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 7),
(147, 'الفتح الرياضي يفوز على اتحاد تواركة', 'حقق نادي الفتح الرياضي فوزا ثمينا على مضيفه اتحاد تواركة، بنتيجة 2-0، في المباراة التي أجريت مساء يومه الأحد على أرضية ملعب المدينة بالرباط، ضمن منافسات الجولة 18 من البطولة الاحترافية. وتمكن فريق الفتح الرياضي، من إنهاء الشوط الأول متفوقا بنتيجة 1-0، بفضل هدف اللاعب حذيفة جمعان في الدقيقة 43. وخلال الشوط الثاني، أضاف الفتح الرياضي الهدف الثاني في الدقيقة 80، من ضربة جزاء سجلها أيوب مولوعة، لتنتهي المباراة بفوز الفتح بنتيجة 2-0. وبفضل هذا الانتصار، رفع الفتح الرياضي رصيده إلى النقطة 24 في المركز الثامن، بينما تجمد رصيد اتحاد تواركة عند النقطة 13 في المركز 14. ‫‫من شروط النشر : عدم الإساءة للكاتب أو للأشخاص أو للمقدسات أو مهاجمة الأديان أو الذات الإلهية، والابتعاد عن التحريض العنصري والشتائم‬.', 'https://www.hesport.com/%d8%a7%d9%84%d9%81%d8%aa%d8%ad-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%b1%d9%8a%d8%a7%d8%b6%d9%8a-%d9%8a%d9%81%d9%88%d8%b2-%d8%b9%d9%84%d9%89-%d8%a7%d8%aa%d8%ad%d8%a7%d8%af-%d8%aa%d9%88%d8%a7%d8%b1%d9%83%d8%a9-437364.html', NULL, '2026-05-03 21:46:16', '2026-05-03 21:46:16', 'Football', 1, 5, 'ar', 'https://i1.hesport.com/wp-content/overlay/2026/05/IMG_5840.jpeg?v2', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 9),
(148, 'الرجاء الرياضي يفوز على الدفاع الجديدي ويرتقي للمركز الثاني مؤقتا', 'حقق نادي الرجاء الرياضي فوزا ثمينا على ضيفه الدفاع الحسني الجديدي، بنتيجة هدف نظيف، في المباراة التي جرت مساء يومه الأحد بمركب محمد الخامس بمدينة الدار البيضاء، في إطار منافسات الجولة 18 من البطولة الاحترافية. ونجح الرجاء في تدبير الفصل الأول بذكاء، مكنه من أخذ الأسبقية وحماية مرمى الفريق من الهجمات المبكرة للمنافس. وعرف الشوط الثاني صحوة الفريق الضيف الدفاع الجديدي، الذي قام بمحاولات كثيرة على مرمى الرجاء، غير أن غياب اللمسة الأخيرة حال دون بلوغ الشباك. وبفضل هذا الانتصار، ارتقى الرجاء للمركز الثاني برصيد 36 نقطة، بينما تجمد رصيد الدفاع الحسني الجديدي عند النقطة 27 في المركز السابع. ‫‫من شروط النشر : عدم الإساءة للكاتب أو للأشخاص أو للمقدسات أو مهاجمة الأديان أو الذات الإلهية، والابتعاد عن التحريض العنصري والشتائم‬.', 'https://www.hesport.com/%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%b1%d8%ac%d8%a7%d8%a1-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%b1%d9%8a%d8%a7%d8%b6%d9%8a-%d9%8a%d9%81%d9%88%d8%b2-%d8%b9%d9%84%d9%89-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%af%d9%81%d8%a7%d8%b9-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%ac%d8%af%d9%8a%d8%af-437357.html', NULL, '2026-05-03 21:46:16', '2026-05-03 21:46:16', 'Football', 1, 10, 'ar', 'https://i1.hesport.com/wp-content/overlay/2026/05/IMG_5839.jpeg?v2', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 9),
(149, 'Un 21e titre au palmarès: Marcus Thuram et l\'Inter reprennent leur couronne en Serie A', 'Privé du titre de champion d\'Italie par Naples pour un point la saison dernière, l\'Inter Milan a retrouvé sa place au sommet de la Serie A en s\'offrant ce dimanche son 21e Scudetto, son troisième en six ans. Vainqueurs de Parme à San Siro (2-0), pour le compte de la 35e journée, grâce à des buts de Marcus Thuram (45e+1) et Henrikh Mkhitaryan (80e), les Nerazzurri ne peuvent plus être rejoints. A trois journées du terme de la saison, ils comptent 12 points d\'avance sur Naples (2e) et 15 sur l\'AC Milan (3e).La saison de l\'Inter n\'est toutefois pas encore terminée. Le club lombard peut encore réaliser le doublé championnat-Coupe d\'Italie, le troisième de son histoire après 2005-06 et 2009-10, s\'il bat en finale la Lazio Rome, le 13 mai au Stade olympique. Ce titre valide déjà la décision de confier l\'équipe à Cristian Chivu, un ancien joueur de l\'Inter qui n\'avait pourtant qu\'une poignée de matches de Serie A à son actif comme entraîneur lorsqu\'il a succédé en juin dernier à Simone Inzaghi, parti à la surprise générale entraîner le club saoudien d\'Al-Hilal. Même s\'ils devaient réaliser le doublé Championnat/Coupe d\'Italie, les joueurs de l\'Inter, portés par leur capitaine Lautaro Martinez, meilleur buteur de Serie A avec 16 buts, ne feraient pas complétement oublier leur déroute en Ligue des champions. Ils ont été éliminés de l\'épreuve-reine du football européen, dont ils étaient finalistes en 2023 et 2025, dès février et les barrages d\'accession aux 8e de finale par le modeste club norvégien de Bodo-Glimt.', 'https://rmcsport.bfmtv.com/football/serie-a/un-21e-titre-au-palmares-marcus-thuram-et-l-inter-reprennent-leur-couronne-en-serie-a_AV-202605030358.html', NULL, '2026-05-03 22:43:20', '2026-05-03 22:43:20', 'Football', 1, 67, 'fr', 'https://images.bfmtv.com/tY1mYLobA-cEVcxXaL-gdkLQpnE=/0x0:2048x1152/images/Marcus-Thuram-avec-l-Inter-le-3-mai-2026-2280029.jpg', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 6),
(150, 'ريال مدريد يتخطى إسبانيول بثنائية ويؤجل حسم لقب الدوري للكلاسيكو', 'فاز ريال مدريد على مضيفه إسبانيول بنتيجة 2 / 0، مساء الأحد، في منافسات الجولة الرابعة والثلاثين من الدوري الإسباني لكرة القدم، ليؤجل تتويج غريمه التقليدي برشلونة باللقب رسميًا قبل أربع جولات على انتهاء المسابقة. بهذا الفوز يرفع العملاق المدريدي رصيده إلى 77 نقطة في المركز الثاني، ليقلص الفارق إلى 11 نقطة مع برشلونة متصدر الترتيب. وبذلك يتأجل حسم لقب الدوري رسميًا إلى مباراة الكلاسيكو يوم الأحد المقبل، عندما يحل ريال مدريد ضيفًا على برشلونة الذي يحتاج لنقطة واحدة فقط ليحسم تتويجه. أما إسبانيول فقد واصل سلسلة نتائجه السلبية، بخسارته الرابعة في آخر ست جولات، ليتراجع للمركز الثالث عشر برصيد 39 نقطة، ويورط نفسه في صراع الهبوط للدرجة الثانية حيث يبتعد بفارق خمس نقاط فقط عن منطقة الخطر. ‫‫من شروط النشر : عدم الإساءة للكاتب أو للأشخاص أو للمقدسات أو مهاجمة الأديان أو الذات الإلهية، والابتعاد عن التحريض العنصري والشتائم‬.', 'https://www.hesport.com/%d8%b1%d9%8a%d8%a7%d9%84-%d9%85%d8%af%d8%b1%d9%8a%d8%af-%d9%8a%d8%aa%d8%ae%d8%b7%d9%89-%d8%a5%d8%b3%d8%a8%d8%a7%d9%86%d9%8a%d9%88%d9%84-%d8%a8%d8%ab%d9%86%d8%a7%d8%a6%d9%8a%d8%a9-%d9%88%d9%8a%d8%a4-437376.html', NULL, '2026-05-03 22:43:20', '2026-05-03 22:43:20', 'Football', 1, 10, 'ar', 'https://i1.hesport.com/wp-content/overlay/2026/05/IMG_5844.jpeg?v2', NULL, 'pending', NULL, NULL, 9);
